{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "Implemented three independent JALR sum-bit-one predicates in ex_stage.sv:\nsource[1] XOR original immediate[1] XOR (source[0] AND immediate[0]).\nThe original registered forwarding selector chooses among register snapshot,\nEX/MEM and retained WB candidates, with the original default. Only the JALR\narm of misalign_jump changes. Full-width target/effective-address addition,\nJAL alignment, trap/write/forwarding/recovery consumers, pipeline registers,\nhold rules, original operand snapshots, ALU grants, predictor, M/ALTOPS and\nnret=1 RVFI ports remain intact.\n\nAdded pipeline coverage of all 16 source/immediate low-bit combinations for\nall three sources with positive offsets, negative offsets and 32-bit wrap.\nEach case runs with and without deterministic simultaneous imem/dmem holds;\nWB-source cases hold JALR after WB validity clears. Checks cover rd=rs1,\noverlapping producer priority, target/link/trap/bypass suppression and exactly\none recovery. Additional cases cover x0 and reserved JALR encodings. Existing\nassertions are retained. Every harness cycle checks all three candidates\nagainst independent full-width addition and bit-zero clearing, including\nunselected sources, invalid payloads and backend holds.\n\nInitial trial: warning-free Verilator lint; all 39 pipeline cocotb tests pass;\nlocal formal PASS (53 passed, 0 failed), first attempt, no fixes/counterexample.\nNRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench passes all eight full-RVFI comparisons (selftest,\nrandom1, random2, random3, each with and without both bus stalls) and canonical\nstalled CoreMark. Plain make cosim defaults the C++ harness to NRET=2 and fails\nto compile against this nret=1 core; NRET=1 is the declared contract, not a gate\nchange. CoreMark reaches EBREAK, has oob=false, bench_bracketed=true, start\n15648 and stop 4542719: exactly 4,527,071 bracketed cycles. UART retains all\nfive required CRCs (e9f5, e714, 1fd7, 8e3a, fcaf) and the literal\n\"Correct operation validated.\" The ELF was built with canonical 2K/-O3 flags;\nthe port's existing printed compiler-flags string\n…[1682 of 4754 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d5435f04a3dd457e]…\nnot a measured performance improvement. No wider ALU,\nforwarding, predictor or pipeline optimization was attempted.\n\nThe final option-0 worst path is 15.660 ns and 24 cells, from ID/EX rs2 bit 2\nto arithmetic_result_q bit 16 through the ALU. Other worst paths cross the\nALU, direct-target preparation and register-file reads. The old JALR\nalignment/eligibility feedback path is not among the five worst reported\npaths. Synthesis/placement changes and source/control fanout remain concerns;\nthe final area also exceeds the champion's 4462 logic cells. Vendor netlists\nare encrypted, so the exact candidate LUT mapping was not inspected.\n\nFull cocotb suite: all 12 pytest runners passed, including real M arithmetic\nand ALTOPS. Final scalar-mux RTL: warning-free lint, all 39 pipeline cocotb\ntests passed again, all eight full-RVFI cosim comparisons and stalled CoreMark\npassed again. Final local formal recheck is still running; initial equivalent\ncase-mux RTL passed all 53 checks on its first attempt with no fix attempts.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
