{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; sed -n '1,190p' cores/bench/test/test_fetch_queue.py\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/fetch_queue.sv\n?? cores/bench/test/test_fetch_queue.py\nImplemented a three-entry registered circular fetch FIFO between raw IF and ID.\nEach generate slot owns a 98-bit packed payload and an independent producer\nwrite enable. Head/tail pointers and occupancy are one-hot; full credit is\ndeferred until the following registered occupancy state. No fall-through,\nwide shifting, or consumer-dependent producer acceptance exists. Recovery\nclears pointers/occupancy and overrides fetch holds; execution, M arithmetic,\npredictor training, memory effects and channel-0 retirement are unchanged.\n\nTests independently model accepted fetches, consumed heads, complete saved\nprediction/recovery identity, occupancy, pointer wrap and transfer conservation.\nThe standalone randomized FIFO test covers every legal transfer/occupancy\ncombination, full-credit delay, independent long stalls, flush and reset.\nPipeline architectural/RVFI checks are retained. Internal assumptions about\nlive fetch payloads, branch refill latency and decode-PC identity were updated.\n\nInitial implementation: lint passed; all 53 unchanged formal checks passed on\nthe first attempt; all 13 Python unit runners passed (37 pipeline cases).\nSelftest complete-RVFI cosim and canonical stalled 2K CoreMark validation passed.\nCoreMark marker-only cycles: 4,271,914; all five canonical CRCs and the validation\nliteral matched, and no out-of-bounds accesses occurred.\nInitial actual Gowin Fmax options 0/1/2: 87.867/96.433/96.433 MHz, median 96.433.\nInitial fitness was below the required 249.30364 iterations/sec threshold.\n\nDeviation under evaluation: each FIFO slot also registers redundant 24-bit\nsource-address predecode with the same independent producer enable. The core\nuses these grants for grouped register-file reads while exact raw source f\n…[4696 of 7768 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d305c894361cd771]…\nt consumer and producer holds reach full and empty.\n        for _ in range(30):\n            await edge(1, 0)\n        await edge(1, 1)\n        await edge(1, 1)\n        for _ in range(30):\n            await edge(0, 1)\n        await edge(1, 1, reset=1)\n    for cycle in range(2500):\n        await edge(int(rng.random() < 0.65), int(rng.random() < 0.55),\n                   recovery=int(cycle % 73 == 0), reset=int(cycle % 251 == 0))\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await edge(0, 1)\n    assert occupancy_visits == {0, 1, 2, 3}\n    for occupancy in range(4):\n        for producer in range(2):\n            for consumer in range(2):\n                assert (occupancy, bool(producer and occupancy < 3),\n                        bool(consumer and occupancy > 0)) in transfers\n    assert min(wraps) > 100 and credit_delays > 20\n    assert accepted == delivered + discarded\n\n\ndef test_fetch_queue_runner():\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"fetch_queue\", sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"fetch_queue.sv\"],\n                test_module=\"test_fetch_queue\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
