{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_95", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_predictor.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/direction_predictor.sv\n?? cores/bench/rtl/direction_ram.sv\n# Reset-scrubbed distributed-RAM direction predictor\n\nResult: correctness and actual LUT-RAM inference pass; performance\nacceptance fails. The retained RTL scores 222.26 iterations/sec, below\nthe required strict threshold of 249.30364 iterations/sec.\n\nImplemented the 64-entry PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8] direction table as four\n16-word banks. Each bank instantiates two resetless, asynchronous-read,\nsynchronous-write 16x2 memories with shared writes and separate fetch and\ntraining addresses. One shared saturating-counter calculation supplies the\nselected bank. There is no write-through bypass.\n\nOnly the initialized bit and four-bit scrub address reset. The first 16\nnon-reset clocks write 01 to one word in every bank and both copies;\ntraining is discarded on all 16 edges, including the last scrub edge.\nConditional direction is masked during reset and initialization. Aligned\nJAL prediction, fetch acceptance, backend execution, recovery, and the\nexisting legal/aligned one-shot MEM training interface are retained.\n\nThe memory template is in rtl/direction_ram.sv, with Gowin's documented\nsyn_ramstyle=\"distributed_ram\" attribute on both the leaf module and\nits array, plus the ram_style=\"distributed\" hint for other synthesis tools. Generated\ninline arrays fell back to 128 counter flops despite their array attributes;\nthe leaf template inferred eight SSRAM blocks. No vendor primitives or\nformal black boxes were introduced. The retained implementation uses a\nfour-way bank mux for the fetch MSB and old training counter.\n\nTests retain the existing architectural checks and use an independent\nscrub/counter model. Added coverage includes ignored early training,\nall banks and words, both saturation limits, hysteresis, independent read\naddresses, aliasing, pre-edge lookup, reset during and after initialization,\nJAL prediction during scrub, retirement/recovery during scrub, initialization\nthrough a prolonged memory hold, and repeated execution after reset. RVFI\norder is checked consecutively from zero on every retirement in the shared\npipeline harness. The alias workload uses two taken branches and one\nuntaken branch sharing an entry to exercise predictions in both states.\n\nLocal validation of the retained RTL:\n\n- Verilator lint: pass, no warnings.\n- Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed. Earlier implementations also passed.\n  No counterexamples or formal fix attempts were needed.\n- Unit tests: all 12 pytest runners passed, including all 39 pipeline\n  cocotb tests and the predictor test.\n- Cosim: passed both ELF gates, including selftest retirement comparison\n  with and without stalls and stalled CoreMark CRC/validation checks.\n- Canonical CoreMark checks pass: seedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714,\n  crcmatrix=1fd7, crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf; the validation text and\n  bounded-access gate pass. Timing uses the MMIO start/stop markers.\n- Final vendor score: placement Fmax 95.000 / 100.620 /\n  100.620 MHz; median 100.620 MHz; 4323 logic cells, 1782 registers,\n  eight LUT-RAM blocks, four BSRAM blocks, two DSPs. Canonical stalled\n  CoreMark completed in 4,527,071 marker-bracketed cycles, giving\n  222.26 iterations/sec. The final rerun reproduces the first leaf-memory\n  result exactly. This does not meet the required 249.30364.\n\n- A masked-OR bank selector variant also passed all correctness checks,\n  but its three-option median was 88.547 MHz and its score was 195.59\n  iterations/sec. It was reverted to retain the faster bank-mux form.\n\nThe predictor storage reduction is real, but the measured timing benefit\nhas not materialized. No other datapath, arithmetic, pipeline, interface,\nevaluation contract, or other core was changed.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
