{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv; rg --files cores/bench/test; rg -n 'pytest|test_pipeline|verilator|cosim|random' tools/eval test/cosim/run_cosim.py\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// Decode always sees the raw bus payload, including during a redirect or\n// an instruction-bus stall. Only validity marks an unavailable/killed\n// fetch, keeping redirect control out of decode and regfile addressing.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,            // hold PC (load-use)\n  input  logic              flush,            // kill fetch validity only\n  input  logic              redirect,         // EX has resolved a branch/jump\n  input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\n  output if_id_t  out\n);\n\n  localparam logic [31:0] RESET_PC = 32'h0000_0000;\n\n  logic [31:0] pc;\n  logic [31:0] next_pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : pc + 32'd4;\n  end\n\n  // Redirect must override stall: a BRANCH/JAL/JALR in EX may fire\n  // redirect on the same cycle as imem_stall or dmem_stall — without\n  // this priority the redirect target would be silently dropped, the\n  // PC would hold its old (wrong-path) value, and execution would\n  // resume on the wrong path once the bus unstalls. Verified by the\n  // VexRiscv-binary CoreMark sweep with --istall enabled.\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if      (reset)    pc <= RESET_PC;\n    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\n    else if (!stall)   pc <= next_pc;\n  end\n\n  assign imem_addr = pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    out.pc    = pc;\n    out.instr = imem_data;\n    out.valid = !(flush || redirect);\n  end\n\nendmodule\n// rtl/ex_stage.s\n…[16607 of 19679 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:83dbb55ba1b3d6ac]…\ncosim for a single ELF using the run_cosim script.\"\"\"\ntools/eval/cosim.py:54:            [sys.executable, str(worktree_path / \"test/cosim/run_cosim.py\"),\ntools/eval/cosim.py:73:    Full-trace cosim would take >30 min; the CRC guard is sensitive to any\ntools/eval/cosim.py:76:    cross-checks it at the cosim stage too.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:79:    # projects that only run cosim.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:125:def run_cosim(worktree: str, target: str | None = None) -> dict:\ntools/eval/cosim.py:130:                cosim_sim from cores/<target>/obj_dir/cosim_sim instead of\ntools/eval/cosim.py:131:                the default test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim, and injects\ntools/eval/cosim.py:143:    obj_dir = Path(env.get(\"OBJ_DIR\", \"test/cosim/obj_dir\"))\ntools/eval/cosim.py:146:    sim_bin = str(obj_dir / \"cosim_sim\")\ntools/eval/cosim.py:148:    # Split ELFs into full-trace cosim vs CRC-validated coremark.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:156:    # 1. Full-trace cosim of small ELFs (parallel).\ntools/eval/cosim.py:184:    result = run_cosim(\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
