{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_72", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Replace JALR alignment carry logic with an exact low-bit predicate\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz and\n  4,527,071 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its option-0 worst path\n  starts at EX arithmetic_result_q bit zero, crosses operand bypass,\n  two jalr_sum carry cells and three write-eligibility cells, then\n  ends at fwd_rs1_sel through forwarding priority: 15.050 ns and ten\n  cells. A fresh unchanged-core Gowin run reproduces this path and\n  102.509 MHz option-0 Fmax. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior micro_opt\n  successes removed late selectors; no prior hypothesis isolated\n  JALR target alignment from the address carry chain.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute JALR instruction-address misalignment with the exact\n  Boolean expression sum_bit1 = rs1[1] XOR imm[1] XOR\n  (rs1[0] AND imm[0]). JALR clears sum bit zero, so its only RV32IM\n  target-alignment fault is sum_bit1. Use this dedicated predicate in\n  misalign_jump instead of observing jump_target[1:0] from the full\n  rs1-plus-immediate expression. This four-input Boolean function can\n  map to one LUT4, removing the two carry cells and their routing from\n  the late alignment-to-producer-eligibility path. Keep the full exact\n  addition and low-bit clearing for the architectural JALR target and\n  independently registered effective address. Do not replace address\n  arithmetic with the predicate or assume rs1 is aligned.\n\n  Preserve the validated is_jump/is_jalr qualification and direct JAL\n  alignment rule. Drive the same misalign_jump predicate into trapping,\n  reg_write suppression and recovery eligibility, so a fault cannot\n  enable a bypass producer, write a link or redirect. Ordinary source\n  forwarding, priority, encoded and complete registered selections,\n  consumer capture/hold timing, M ownership and arithmetic, predictor\n  training, memory handling, ALTOPS formulas, nret=1 IO and ordered RVFI\n  remain unchanged. This is one local Boolean datapath micro_opt with\n  no change in stages or instruction cycle schedule.\n\n  Initial trials that moved eligibility after a register or replaced\n  encoded forwarding with registered one-hot grants passed pipeline\n  and RVFI cosim checks but measured only 94.732 and 103.692 MHz median\n  Fmax respectively. Neither is part of this proposal: they lengthened\n  other execution paths. The low-bit predicate targets the confirmed\n  carry path while retaining the champion's operand topology.\n\n  The expected gain is higher median Gowin Fmax at the same 4,527,071\n  CoreMark cycles. Measure all three scored placement options. Fitness\n  must exceed 249.30364 iterations/sec, requiring median Fmax above\n  approximately 112.861528 MHz at unchanged cycles. The main risks are\n  synthesis merging the predicate back into address arithmetic and\n  another nearly critical path limiting the gain. Require unchanged\n  formal, pipeline and full-RVFI cosim gates, canonical stalled\n  CoreMark CRCs and validation text, and bounded memory accesses.\n  Timing for this exact predicate is pending; the gain is a prediction.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the exact four-input JALR sum-bit-one Boolean predicate and\n      use it for JALR misalignment, retaining direct JAL checks, all\n      qualification and consumers of misalign_jump, full target and\n      effective-address arithmetic, register topology and cycle timing.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all assertions. Cover all sixteen combinations of\n      forwarded rs1[1:0] and signed JALR immediate[1:0], with independent\n      full-width target addition and bit-zero clearing as the reference.\n      Include register snapshot, EX/MEM and retained WB sources, x0,\n      rd=rs1, negative offsets, upper-bit carries, both bus stalls,\n      faulting jump link/bypass suppression and recovery exactly once.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
