{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids=['hyp-20261004-001-r7s0','hyp-20261004-001-r8s0','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-001-r10s0','hyp-20261004-002-r7s1']\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID:',r['id'])\n  h=r.get('hypothesis')\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print(h.get('hypothesis'))\n  else: print(h)\n  print('changes',json.dumps(r.get('changes')))\n  print('notes:',r.get('implementation_notes'))\n  print('seeds',r.get('seeds'),'LUT',r.get('lut4'),'FF',r.get('ff'),'cycles',r.get('cycles'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: hyp-20261004-001-r7s0\nKeep the 31 resettable architectural words and existing four groups\nof eight words per read port. Replace each read port's final encoded\ngroup-selection case and nested x0/write-first mux with one parallel\nmasked-OR network over five sources: groups 0 through 3 and WB data.\n\nFor port p define bypass_p = w_en && w_addr == rs_p_addr &&\nrs_p_addr != 0. Give WB data grant bypass_p. Give group g grant\n!bypass_p && rs_p_addr[4:3] == g. Form rs_p_data as the OR of each\n32-bit source masked by its grant. These five grants are mutually\nexclusive and exhaustive for every read address. Preserve words[0]\nas literal zero inside group 0; when the read address is zero, bypass\nis excluded and that group's existing low-address read selects zero.\nA separate final x0 data mux is therefore redundant. Explicitly\nretain same-cycle write-first behavior, including while reset is\nasserted, and silent suppression of storage writes to x0.\n\nThis is one register-file read-selection micro-optimization. It\nremoves the serial bank-selection-to-WB-bypass data mux by making\nbypass priority part of the source grants. No extra pipeline stage,\nstorage changes, bank conflicts, instruction latency, forwarding\nselection, ALU arithmetic, multiply/divide handshake, memory request\nschedule or branch behavior is proposed. Preserve default-illegal\ndecoding, all traps, nret=1 IO, retained WB values through backend\nholds, exactly-once retirement and every fixed correctness gate.\n\nThe intended benefit is higher median Gowin Fmax at unchanged\nmarker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Compare all three scored placement\noptions; at 4,773,836 cycles, exceeding the 4.6 percent acceptance\nmargin requires fitness above 189.75486 iterations/sec and median\nFmax above approximately 90.585 MHz. The principal risk is added\nfanout of the bypass grant or the synthesis tool factoring the OR\nback into serial muxes. Require exact register-file behavior, all\nformal and RVFI cosim checks, canonical CoreMark CRCs and validation\ntext, in-bounds accesses and the \n…[21803 of 24875 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b31ff9f68b523e0a]…\ne still pending, so the\npredicted clock/fitness gain has low confidence and is not measured.\n\nchanges [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the three exact source-specific JALR sum-bit-one\\npredicates before ordinary operand selection. Select the\\nscalar predicate with the existing registered forwarding\\nselector and feed the existing JALR misalignment arm. Preserve\\nevery full-width address, source selection, producer qualifier,\\ntrap and recovery consumer, register boundary and hold rule.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain every existing assertion. Cover all sixteen combinations\\nof source[1:0] and signed JALR immediate[1:0] for register, EX/MEM\\nand retained WB sources, using independent full-width addition\\nand bit-zero clearing as the reference. Include x0, rd=rs1,\\nnegative offsets and carries, both bus stalls, overlapping\\nproducers, trap/link/bypass suppression and exactly-once recovery.\\n\"}]\nnotes: \nseeds [96.47, 99.72, 99.72] LUT 4550 FF 1905 cycles 4527071\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
