{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"The request-edge narrow MUL passed CoreMark CRC validation and cut measured cycles by about 4.2%, but its clock speed fell enough to erase the gain. The current hypothesis moves that fast path behind the multiplier’s existing operand registers. I’m checking whether skipping one reduction cycle can preserve the champion’s clock speed.\n"}}
