{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-001-r10s0','hyp-20261004-001-r11s0'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in wanted:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(d['id'])\n  print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r9s0\nAdd a twelve-bit integer result-grant field to the existing ID/EX bundle.\nBits 0 through 10 correspond to ALU_ADD through ALU_LUI in their existing\nencoding order; bit 11 selects the PC+4 jump link. Compute each grant\nfrom ctrl_decoded at ID capture: bit j is !is_jump && alu_op == j, and\nbit 11 is is_jump. Use the already overridden branch ALU_LUI control,\nso the branch's prepared recovery address still occupies the arithmetic\nlane. Legal M operations have all twelve grants zero. Reset grants to\nzero and capture/hold with the existing ID/EX payload enable, including\ninvalid payload captures; do not introduce validity or flush gating.\n\nGive alu.sv an elaboration-time predecoded-result option enabled only by\nthe core, retaining the encoded standalone interface behavior by default.\nPass the registered grants, in.pc+4 and the existing owned completion\ncondition divide_active_q && div_result_valid into this option. Form one\nparallel OR of selected integer, link and completed-M values. ADD/SUB,\nbitwise operations, comparisons and LUI retain their exact expressions,\nmasked by their registered grant; PC+4 and m_result are additional OR\nsources. M completion uses exactly its current acceptance condition and\nregistered exclusive service owner. Do not gate integer grants with\nlate completion: ID/EX holds its M opcode throughout ownership, so all\nordinary/link grants are already zero whenever M completion selects.\nAssert this disjointness in tests. Preserve the held result behavior.\n\nFor the three shifts absorb their result grant at the DATA INPUT of the\nexisting barrel expression, instead of masking after the barrel. Compute\nSLL contribution as (a & {32{grant_SLL}}) << b[4:0], SRL contribution as\n(a & {32{grant_SRL}}) >> b[4:0], and SRA contribution as the unsigned\nresult of $signed(a & {32{grant_SRA}}) >>> b[4:0]. Mask before the signed\ncast so an unselected arithmetic shift is zero even for negative a.\nKeep the three original shift directions and five-bit shift amount;\ndo not replace the shifters wit\n…[7480 of 10552 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:77dc9388a31f9209]…\ne M ownership, saved source/RVFI snapshots, launch/busy frontend\nholds, older-memory priority and exactly-once transfer unchanged.\nThe accepted narrow MUL now has one calculation edge after request\nacceptance, instead of two; consumption remains a separate edge.\nNo other instruction changes latency. Preserve all real arithmetic\nand all ALTOPS substitutions, default-illegal decode, alignment traps,\nnret=1 ports, full architectural RVFI and consecutive retirement.\n\nCompare scored median Gowin timing times actual marker-bracketed cycles.\nRequire all fixed formal/cosim gates, canonical CoreMark CRCs and\nvalidation literal, bounded accesses and exact start/stop timing.\nUpdate latency-specific unit expectations only to independently derived\noperand-dependent latency, preserving all bit-result and handshake\nassertions and testing both fast and fallback paths. The gain depends\non how many products qualify and whether the saved-operand DSP maps\nwithout adding result-selection delay; confidence is low until measured.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
