{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport difflib\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r12s0.yaml')\nnew='''id: hyp-20261004-001-r12s0\ntitle: \\\"Predecode valid normal writers to shorten forwarding eligibility feedback\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz with\n  4,527,071 bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Its worst\n  vendor path runs from a forwarded low operand bit through JALR\n  alignment, normal-write qualification and forwarding priority into\n  a registered source selection. Earlier alignment arithmetic changes\n  regressed. The remaining opportunity is to shorten the control AFTER\n  the exact alignment decision, while retaining its existing datapath.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one exact normal_writer flag to the existing ID/EX bundle. Decode\n  it from validated dec_reg_write, excluding all eight decoded M\n  operations, and the accepted instruction's validity. The flag includes\n  legality through the original validated decoder's reg_write control;\n  do not clear is_illegal using a new shortcut. Reset clears the flag.\n  Flush clears it with the same priority as ID/EX valid, independently\n  of payload capture; otherwise an unstalled capture sets it from the\n  incoming validity and validated normal-writer class. Backend holds\n  retain it exactly as they retain ID/EX valid. This scalar must always\n  equal ID/EX valid AND decoded reg_write AND NOT an M operation.\n\n  Form next_reg_write as \"'!stall AND the parallel OR of two disjoint\n  sources: (in.normal_writer AND !recovery_valid_q AND !misalign_jump)\n  and (divide_active_q AND div_result_valid AND the saved M instruction'\"'s\n  post-trap reg_write). A normal_writer is zero for a held M instruction,\n  so the normal source needs neither a live \"'!is_divide test nor the\n  divide_active_q priority mux. This removes redundant validity,\n  execution-class and ownership qualification after JALR alignment.\n  Preserve !stall, exact jump-fault cancellation and saved-M completion\n  eligibility; do not repeat the failed removal of hold qualifiers.\n  Keep actual EX/MEM side-effect controls and valid generation unchanged.\n\n  Retain the existing full forwarded JALR sum and alignment decision,\n  architectural PC/link results, EX/MEM and WB producer priority, x0\n  exclusion, loads'\"' post-MEM misalignment qualification and retained WB\n  forwarding. An illegal or misaligned producer must never advertise\n  a destination. M launch and busy cycles cannot advertise a writer;\n  completion may advertise it exactly once on its original release edge.\n  Pending recovery suppresses every younger normal writer as before.\n\n  This is one local control-predecode micro_opt, with no new stage,\n  instruction latency, speculative forwarding, replay, predictor change\n  or arithmetic redesign. Keep every ALTOPS formula, real RV32IM result,\n  decoder legality check, trap, memory request, pipeline capture/hold\n  enable, nret=1 IO and consecutive architectural retirement intact.\n  Normal CoreMark cycles should remain exactly 4,527,071. Expected\n  fitness gain is eight percent from removing serial control gates,\n  with low confidence because ALU, RF and IF paths are nearly tied.\n  Local RTL trials are evidence only for the exact version tested;\n  acceptance requires the unchanged formal/cosim gates, canonical\n  stalled CoreMark CRCs and validation text, bounded memory accesses,\n  marker-bracketed timing, median Gowin Fmax above 112.861528 MHz and\n  fitness above 249.30364 iterations/sec. Do not claim an improvement\n  unless the scored trial clears those thresholds.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a scalar normal_writer field to ID/EX without changing any\n      top-level port or architectural retirement bundle.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture exact valid, validated non-M writer eligibility in the\n      new scalar. Give it the same reset, flush and hold priorities as\n      ID/EX valid while retaining all existing payload/decode behavior.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace only anticipated EX/MEM forwarding eligibility with the\n      parallel normal-writer and owned-M-completion terms. Retain the\n      exact existing alignment predicate, stall qualification, recovery\n      cancellation and actual EX/MEM side-effect controls.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing checks; independently assert the scalar against\n      valid, validated controls and instruction class. Verify next-writer\n      eligibility matches the actual advancing EX/MEM producer for all\n      integer/link/load/M classes, illegal and misaligned instructions,\n      x0, wrong-path recovery, load-use kills, both bus stalls, M launch,\n      busy and completion, saved WB operands, flush during a hold and\n      reset. Compare full RVFI and exact memory effects and order.\n'''\ndiff=list(difflib.unified_diff(p.read_text().splitlines(True),new.splitlines(True)))\nprint('*** Begin Patch\\\\n*** Update File: '+str(p)+'\\\\n'+''.join(diff[2:])+'*** End Patch')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
