{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport difflib\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r12s0.yaml')\nnew='''id: hyp-20261004-001-r12s0\ntitle: \\\"Predecode valid normal writers to shorten forwarding eligibility feedback\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz with\n  4,527,071 bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Its worst\n  vendor path crosses JALR alignment, normal-write qualification and\n  forwarding priority before capturing a source selection. Prior\n  alignment arithmetic changes regressed. This proposal instead\n  removes redundant control qualification AFTER the exact fault check.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one exact normal_writer scalar to the existing ID/EX bundle.\n  Capture accepted validity AND validated dec_reg_write AND NOT any\n  of the eight decoded M operations. Legality comes from the original\n  default-illegal decoder's validated reg_write control. Reset clears\n  the flag. Flush clears it with the same priority as ID/EX valid;\n  otherwise capture it only when \"'!stall, retaining it during every\n  backend hold. It must always equal ID/EX valid AND decoded reg_write\n  AND NOT an M operation. Do not change ordinary payload captures.\n\n  Replace next_reg_write with !stall AND a parallel OR of two disjoint\n  terms: (in.normal_writer AND !recovery_valid_q AND !misalign_jump)\n  and (divide_active_q AND div_result_valid AND\n  divide_snapshot_q.ctrl.reg_write). The held M instruction'\"'s scalar\n  is zero, so the normal term needs neither the live \"'!is_divide test\n  nor the divide_active_q priority mux. Preserve the stall qualifier,\n  saved-M completion eligibility and exact jump-fault cancellation.\n  Keep actual EX/MEM controls and validity generation unchanged.\n\n  Retain the original full forwarded JALR sum and alignment decision,\n  architectural PC/link results, youngest-writer priority, x0 exclusion,\n  post-MEM load alignment checks, retained WB forwarding and registered\n  recovery. Illegal or misaligned producers must never advertise a\n  destination. M launch/busy cycles advertise no writer; completion\n  advertises the saved result only on its original release edge.\n\n  This is one local control-predecode micro_opt. No new stage, latency,\n  replay, speculation, predictor or arithmetic change is included.\n  Preserve decoder legality, all traps, all ALTOPS formulas, real M\n  arithmetic, bus requests, capture/hold enables, exact nret=1 ports\n  and consecutive architectural RVFI retirement. CoreMark cycles\n  should remain 4,527,071. Expected fitness improvement is eight percent,\n  with low confidence because other paths are nearly tied. Require all\n  unchanged formal/cosim gates, canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs and\n  validation text, bounded accesses and exact start/stop brackets.\n  Acceptance requires scored median Gowin Fmax above 112.861528 MHz\n  and fitness above 249.30364 iterations/sec at unchanged cycles.\n  Private trials establish only the behavior and timing of their exact\n  tested RTL; do not claim an improvement without scored validation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add normal_writer to ID/EX; preserve all top-level ports and\n      architectural retirement bundles.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture exact valid non-M writer eligibility from validated\n      decode, with ID/EX valid'\"'s reset/flush/hold priorities. Preserve\n      existing payload captures and decoder legality checks.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Change only anticipated forwarding writer eligibility to parallel\n      normal and owned-M completion terms. Retain existing alignment,\n      stall, recovery and actual side-effect control behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing check. Independently assert the scalar's\n      relation to valid/decode/class and eligibility's equivalence to\n      the actual advancing producer. Cover integer/link/load/M results,\n      illegal and misaligned producers, x0, load-use kills, recovery,\n      both bus stalls, held WB data, M launch/busy/completion and reset.\n      Compare full RVFI, memory effects and consecutive retirement order.\n'''\ndiff=list(difflib.unified_diff(p.read_text().splitlines(True),new.splitlines(True)))\nbody=''.join('@@\\\\n' if line.startswith('@@') else line for line in diff[2:])\nprint('*** Begin Patch\\\\n*** Update File: '+str(p)+'\\\\n'+body+'*** End Patch')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
