{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-001-r10s0','hyp-20261004-002-r11s1','hyp-20261004-003-r12s2']:\n  print('\\\\nID',r['id'])\n  print(r.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20261004-001-r9s0\nAdd a twelve-bit integer result-grant field to the existing ID/EX bundle.\nBits 0 through 10 correspond to ALU_ADD through ALU_LUI in their existing\nencoding order; bit 11 selects the PC+4 jump link. Compute each grant\nfrom ctrl_decoded at ID capture: bit j is !is_jump && alu_op == j, and\nbit 11 is is_jump. Use the already overridden branch ALU_LUI control,\nso the branch's prepared recovery address still occupies the arithmetic\nlane. Legal M operations have all twelve grants zero. Reset grants to\nzero and capture/hold with the existing ID/EX payload enable, including\ninvalid payload captures; do not introduce validity or flush gating.\n\nGive alu.sv an elaboration-time predecoded-result option enabled only by\nthe core, retaining the encoded standalone interface behavior by default.\nPass the registered grants, in.pc+4 and the existing owned completion\ncondition divide_active_q && div_result_valid into this option. Form one\nparallel OR of selected integer, link and completed-M values. ADD/SUB,\nbitwise operations, comparisons and LUI retain their exact expressions,\nmasked by their registered grant; PC+4 and m_result are additional OR\nsources. M completion uses exactly its current acceptance condition and\nregistered exclusive service owner. Do not gate integer grants with\nlate completion: ID/EX holds its M opcode throughout ownership, so all\nordinary/link grants are already zero whenever M completion selects.\nAssert this disjointness in tests. Preserve the held result behavior.\n\nFor the three shifts absorb their result grant at the DATA INPUT of the\nexisting barrel expression, instead of masking after the barrel. Compute\nSLL contribution as (a & {32{grant_SLL}}) << b[4:0], SRL contribution as\n(a & {32{grant_SRL}}) >> b[4:0], and SRA contribution as the unsigned\nresult of $signed(a & {32{grant_SRA}}) >>> b[4:0]. Mask before the signed\ncast so an unselected arithmetic shift is zero even for negative a.\nKeep the three original shift directions and five-bit shift amount;\ndo not replace the shifters\n…[16727 of 19799 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cfa7db0467dc0252]…\neserved/SYSTEM checks,\nreal RV32IM and ALTOPS arithmetic, nret=1 IO and architectural RVFI.\nUse the identical indirect protocol in formal and production builds.\n\nLocal precursors for segmented fetch addresses, store-lane recovery,\nGray counters and direct recovery-operand bypass reached only 98.797,\n99.924, 105.687 and 95.323 MHz median and were rejected. The FINAL\nreturn-stack/registered-validation architecture is unimplemented and\nunmeasured. Estimate eight percent fitness improvement with low confidence.\nEven eliminating all 13,735 existing two-cycle JALR recoveries saves only\nabout 0.61 percent of 4,527,071 cycles, while each JALR adds a validation\ncycle; ordinary ALU paths may still limit Fmax. Snapshot/control routing\nand stack flops can erase the clock benefit. Measure actual bracketed\ncycles and all Gowin options; do not assume unchanged cycles. Require all\nunchanged formal/cosim gates, canonical CoreMark CRCs and validation text,\nbounded accesses, exact markers and fitness above 249.30364 iter/sec.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypgen_r13')\np.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nrtl=p/'rtl'\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',rtl,dirs_exist_ok=True)\na=rtl/'alu.sv'\ns=a.read_text()\nanchor='  logic        [4:0]  shamt;'\nnetwork='''  // Independent parallel ADD/SUB candidates with short carry chains.\n  logic [31:0] add_result, sub_result;\n  for (genvar operation = 0; operation < 2; operation++) begin : gen_short_arithmetic\n    wire [31:0] y = operation == 0 ? b : ~b;\n    wire [3:0] carry, g, p;\n    wire [31:0] value;\n    assign carry[0] = operation \"'!= 0;\n    assign carry[1] = g[0] | (p[0] & carry[0]);\n    assign carry[2] = g[1] | (p[1] & g[0]) | (p[1] & p[0] & carry[0]);\n    assign carry[3] = g[2] | (p[2] & g[1]) | (p[2] & p[1] & g[0])\n                            | (p[2] & p[1] & p[0] & carry[0]);\n    for (genvar block_index = 0; block_index < 4; block_index++) begin : gen_block\n      wire [8:0] sum0, sum1;\n      assign sum0 = {1'\"'b0, a[block_index*8 +: 8]} + {1'b0, y[block_index*8 +: 8]};\n      assign sum1 = {1'b0, a[block_index*8 +: 8]} + {1'b0, y[block_index*8 +: 8]} + 9'd1;\n      assign g[block_index] = sum0[8];\n      assign p[block_index] = &(a[block_index*8 +: 8] \"'^ y[block_index*8 +: 8]);\n      assign value[block_index*8 +: 8] = carry[block_index] ? sum1[7:0] : sum0[7:0];\n    end\n    if (operation == 0) assign add_result = value;\n    else assign sub_result = value;\n  end\n\n'\"'''\ns=s.replace(anchor,network+anchor)\ns=s.replace('((a + b) & {32{result_grants[0]}})','(add_result & {32{result_grants[0]}})')\ns=s.replace('((a - b) & {32{result_grants[1]}})','(sub_result & {32{result_grants[1]}})')\ns=s.replace('ALU_ADD:    out = a + b;', 'ALU_ADD:    out = add_result;')\ns=s.replace('ALU_SUB:    out = a - b;', 'ALU_SUB:    out = sub_result;')\na.write_text(s)\nprint('Trial RTL