{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r13s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Short-block carry-select integer ADD and SUB\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz and\n  4,527,071 marker-bracketed cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Reviewed\n  micro_opt attempts already cover operand selection, register-file\n  organization, result predecode, multiplier shortcuts and forwarding\n  eligibility. Recent failed candidates repeatedly expose 24-37-cell\n  paths from ID/EX operands through u_alu to arithmetic_result_q.\n  The champion's ordinary ADD and SUB still use unpartitioned 32-bit\n  expressions. A local reduction of their serial carry depth offers\n  a fresh timing angle without changing instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the ordinary integer ADD and SUB datapaths with explicit\n  four-block, eight-bit carry-select arithmetic. Keep addition and\n  subtraction as independent parallel result candidates, using the\n  existing registered result_grants to select them. Do not introduce\n  an opcode-controlled operand mux ahead of a shared add/sub unit.\n\n  For ADD use y=b and initial carry c0=0. For SUB use y=~b and c0=1,\n  implementing a-b modulo 2^32. In each fixed eight-bit block compute\n  two explicitly nine-bit sums in parallel: {0,a_block}+{0,y_block}\n  and {0,a_block}+{0,y_block}+9'd1. Select the low eight bits using\n  that block's carry-in. Derive block generate from sum0[8] and block\n  propagate from &(a_block ^ y_block). Form all four block carry-ins\n  with explicitly expanded group lookahead, rather than a serial mux\n  chain: c1=g0|p0*c0; c2=g1|p1*g0|p1*p0*c0; and the analogous\n  expression for c3. The low block uses its constant initial carry.\n  Discard only the final carry, preserving exact wraparound results.\n  This bounds native ripple arithmetic to eight bits and resolves\n  upper-block carry selection through a small LUT network.\n\n  Apply the same exact sum signals to the encoded ALU_ADD/ALU_SUB\n  fallback and the core's PREDECODED_RESULT path. Leave all ALTOPS\n  formulas as written; M arithmetic, comparisons, shifts, PC arithmetic,\n  effective-address arithmetic and JALR alignment remain outside this\n  focused change. Keep pipeline register enables, retained forwarding\n  values, memory requests, decoder legality, traps, nret=1 ports and\n  RVFI retirement behavior exactly equivalent.\n\n  The predicted gain is higher Gowin median Fmax at unchanged CoreMark\n  cycles. Confidence is low: the champion's reported worst path is\n  forwarding eligibility, other paths are nearly tied, and duplicated\n  short sums can increase LUT usage or be merged back by synthesis.\n  Confirm the mapped short carry chains and measure all scored placement\n  options; an isolated combinational delay estimate is insufficient.\n  Require unchanged formal and full-RVFI cosim gates, canonical stalled\n  CoreMark CRCs and validation text, bounded memory accesses and exact\n  marker timing. Acceptance needs fitness above 249.30364 iter/sec,\n  corresponding to about 112.862 MHz if cycles remain unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Add independent fixed-block carry-select ADD and SUB networks with\n      nine-bit speculative block sums, exact expanded carry lookahead\n      and modulo-32-bit outputs. Use them for ordinary ADD/SUB in both\n      ALU selection modes, preserving result grants, all other operations,\n      M service interfaces and the existing ALTOPS substitutions.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing checks. Add independently computed modulo-2^32\n      ADD/SUB cases exercising carry and borrow across bits 7/8, 15/16\n      and 23/24, all-block propagation, signed extrema, wraparound and\n      seeded random operands. Cover encoded and predecoded selection\n      without changing any M arithmetic or legality expectations.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
