{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r13s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Share integer subtraction and comparison through one exact borrow\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz with\n  4,527,071 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent.\n  Reviewed micro_opt attempts cover operand/result selection, register\n  file layout, multiplier shortcuts and JALR forwarding eligibility.\n  Current ALU SUB, SLTU and SLT are expressed independently despite\n  using the same operands. Native carry propagation is inexpensive\n  in the detailed Gowin report; routing and result selection dominate.\n  Sharing the arithmetic dependency is therefore more promising than\n  introducing speculative block sums and additional selection logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the integer ALU one explicit 33-bit unsigned difference:\n  difference = {1'b0,a} - {1'b0,b}. Use difference[31:0] for SUB and\n  difference[32] for unsigned less-than. With zero-extended operands,\n  bit 32 is exactly the borrow indication, including wraparound cases.\n  Compute signed less-than as (a[31] ^ b[31]) ? a[31] : difference[32].\n  This handles opposite signs directly and reuses unsigned ordering for\n  operands with the same sign; do not interpret subtraction sign alone\n  as signed less-than or omit the extra arithmetic bit.\n\n  Use these three exact candidates in both the registered-grant\n  PREDECODED_RESULT path and the standalone encoded ALU interface.\n  Keep the existing parallel result-grant selection and ordinary ADD.\n  Preserve every ALTOPS M formula, all real multiply and divide arithmetic,\n  ownership, shifts, branch comparators, address and PC calculations,\n  pipeline boundaries, capture/hold enables, decoder legality, alignment\n  traps, memory requests and the nret=1 RVFI ports. No instruction\n  latency or CoreMark cycle schedule changes are intended.\n\n  A private option-0 prototype reaches 104.759 MHz versus an exactly\n  reproduced unchanged-champion option-0 result of 102.509 MHz. Both\n  use 4,462 logic cells and 1,905 registers. This is only a 2.2 percent\n  option-0 clock gain and does not establish acceptance or area savings;\n  synthesis may already share much of the original comparison hardware.\n  The scored placement median and unchanged correctness gates must\n  determine whether the proposal is useful. Carry-select, early operand\n  masking, sparse carry lookahead and lookup-layout precursors regressed\n  and are excluded from this hypothesis.\n\n  Expected gain is six percent with low confidence. Require unchanged\n  formal and full-RVFI cosim gates, exact canonical stalled CoreMark\n  CRCs and validation text, bounded accesses and marker timing. Fitness\n  must exceed 249.30364 iter/sec; at unchanged 4,527,071 cycles this\n  requires scored median Fmax above approximately 112.862 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Add one zero-extended 33-bit subtraction and derive SUB, SLTU and\n      SLT from its low word, borrow and operand signs. Use these candidates\n      consistently in encoded and predecoded result modes. Preserve\n      all other ALU operations, result-grant behavior, service interfaces\n      and exact ALTOPS formulas.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing check. Independently verify modulo-2^32 SUB,\n      Python unsigned SLTU and signed-integer SLT for equal operands,\n      borrow chains across byte boundaries, sign changes, both signed\n      extrema, wraparound and seeded random inputs. Exercise encoded and\n      registered-grant selection, including unselected-candidate isolation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
