on and\\nremainder separately with / and %, exposing a large, deeply cascaded\\narithmetic network to Gowin synthesis. Shortening this network can\\nimprove every CoreMark cycle even when that cycle does not divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace just the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation in alu.sv with\\none shared, fully combinational radix-4 restoring divider. It produces\\nquotient and remainder together in 16 unrolled steps\n…[97343 of 100415 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7269ca4356a34d46]…\n-of-bounds access occurred.\\n\\nMeasured fitness:\\n\\n- Marker start/stop cycles: 15,022 / 4,205,303.\\n- Bracketed CoreMark cycles: **4,190,281**, 10 iterations.\\n- Iterations/cycle: 0.0000023864747973, a 7.1961% increase over the champion.\\n- Gowin placement options 0/1/2: **48.498 / 51.727 / 51.727 MHz**.\\n- Median Fmax: **51.727 MHz**; logic 2,885, registers 809, LUT-RAM 8.\\n- Fitness: **123.45 iterations/sec** (unrounded 123.4451818386).\\n\\nThe hypothesis does **not** meet the required 125.14344 iterations/sec\\nacceptance threshold. At this cycle count it needs median Fmax above\\n52.438617891 MHz. Cycle reduction matches the estimate, but the measured\\nFmax loss is too large. The final worst path still passes through register\\nfile/operand forwarding, the multiplier and the dmem RAM address path;\\nadded predictor routing/placement remains a concern. Leave acceptance to\\nthe orchestrator; this result should not be claimed as accepted.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T15:42:47.339158Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
