{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r4s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r4s0',\n'title':'Fold the captured WB bypass into parallel EX operand selection',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion delivers 129.85 iter/sec at median Gowin Fmax 61.988 MHz\nand 4,773,836 bracketed CoreMark cycles. No LESSONS.md exists. The prior\nmicro_opt forwarding-only attempt gained 0.94 percent on the older\ncombinational-multiplier parent. A fresh champion timing run reproduces\n61.131 MHz for option 0; the worst register-file-to-memory path crosses\nan ID write-first bypass, EX forwarding and ALU source selection.\nGowin absorbs the raw register-file read register into block RAM, so\nthe ID write-first data selection remains on the post-RAM EX data path.\nFlattening only the existing EX muxes leaves that upstream bypass intact.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the current pipeline depth, issue width, arithmetic units and cycle\nschedule. Remove the core's serial ID write-first data mux by recording\nits choice as metadata and merging that choice into the EX forwarding\nselection. Give reg_file a WRITE_FIRST parameter defaulting to enabled\nso standalone behavior and existing tests remain identical. Instantiate\nit with WRITE_FIRST disabled only in core; ID then captures raw register\narray read data, plus the current WB data and two per-source WB-match\nbits qualified by wb_w_en and a nonzero WB destination. Snapshot those\nthree new fields with the same reset, capture and backend hold behavior\nas the instruction's existing ID/EX payload. Both sources may match the\nsame WB, so one shared 32-bit snapshot suffices.\n\nFor each EX source, use mutually exclusive one-hot grants over four\nsources: EX/MEM, retained MEM/WB, captured decode-time WB, and raw ID/EX\nregister data. Preserve EX/MEM priority over MEM/WB and both over the\ncaptured decode-time value; select the captured WB value only when\nneither newer producer matches and its recorded match bit is set.\nExclude x0 producers and keep retained MEM/WB producer qualification\nindependent of its cleared retirement valid during dmem holds. The\ncaptured WB metadata and data must remain stable throughout a hold.\nDo not reconstruct this old WB value from the live WB port in EX.\n\nExpress forwarded operands as parallel masked-OR selections. For the\nALU inputs, include PC for AUIPC or the immediate for alu_src directly\nin the grants rather than placing another mux after forwarding. Keep\nseparate raw forwarded rs1/rs2 selections for branch comparisons,\nJALR, store data and RVFI/M-unit launch snapshots: immediate address\nselection must not disable store-data forwarding. Leave all ALU\noperators, multiplier/divider state machines, launch/result handshakes,\nload-use timing, redirects, alignment traps and decoder legality intact.\n\nThis is one bypass-network micro-optimization. Its distinguishing change\nfrom hyp-20261004-001-r3s0 is moving the captured decode-time WB choice\ninto the same selection as the EX bypasses, not merely recoding EX's\nexisting three-way mux. The intended gain is a shorter register-file\nand WB-to-EX path at unchanged iterations/cycle. Added snapshot storage,\ngrant fanout and Gowin's register/RAM inference are the main risks.\nKeep nret=1 and all fixed gates. Acceptance requires fitness above\n135.8231 iter/sec; at 4,773,836 cycles that means median Fmax above\n64.839720441 MHz. Measure all vendor placement options and canonical\nstalled CoreMark before claiming the gain.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'Add a default-enabled WRITE_FIRST parameter that controls only the combinational same-cycle WB read bypass. Preserve synchronous full reset, x0, write timing and both asynchronous read ports. Core opts out; standalone default behavior stays identical.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add one 32-bit decode-time WB snapshot and two WB-match bits to id_ex_t. Preserve all instruction, validity and downstream architectural fields.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Accept current WB enable/address/data, capture qualified rs1/rs2 WB matches and the shared data snapshot alongside raw RF operands, and retain/reset the added fields exactly with ID/EX payload ownership.'},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Generate exclusive one-hot raw/EX-MEM/MEM-WB grants with existing younger-writer priority and x0 exclusion, retaining MEM/WB forwarding during backend holds.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Split the raw grant between raw RF and captured decode-time WB using the held per-source match bits. Use parallel masked selection for four forwarded sources; fold PC/immediate into ALU grants while independently preserving branch/JALR/store/RVFI operands and M-unit snapshots.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Disable only this instance\\\\'s RF write-first mux, wire current WB data/address/enable into ID capture and connect one-hot EX bypass grants. Keep top-level nret=1 IO and all retirement, hazard and arithmetic ownership behavior.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain existing architectural assertions and adapt only internal selector expectations to the new encoding. Add WB-to-ID dependencies separated by two intervening instructions, simultaneous matches on both sources, competing newer EX/MEM/MEM/WB writers, x0, AUIPC/immediates, captured-WB store/branch/JALR/M-unit operands and prolonged dmem/divider holds. Verify source snapshots, held payload, exact retirement order and unchanged bus transactions/cycles.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Revised hypothesis written')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
