ynchronous read ports. Core opts out; standalone default behavior stays identical.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add one 32-bit decode-time WB snapshot and two WB-match bits to id_ex_t. Preserve all instruction, validity and downstream architectural fields.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Accept current WB enable/address/data, capture qualified rs1/rs2 WB matches and the shared data snapshot alongside raw RF operands, and retain/reset the added fields exactly with ID/EX payload ownership.'},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Generate exclusive one-hot raw/EX-MEM/MEM-WB grants with existing younger-writer priority and x0 exclusion, retaining MEM/WB forwarding during backend holds.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Split the raw grant between raw RF and captured decode-time WB using the held per-source match bits. Use parallel masked selection for four forwarded sources; fold PC/immediate into ALU grants while independently preserving branch/JALR/store/RVFI operands and M-unit snapshots.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Disable only this instance\\\\'s RF write-first mux, wire current WB data/address/enable into ID capture and connect one-hot EX bypass grants. Keep top-level nret=1 IO and all retirement, hazard and arithmetic ownership behavior.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain existing architectural assertions and adapt only internal selector expectations to the new encoding. Add WB-to-ID dependencies separated by two intervening instructions, simultaneous matches on both sources, competing newer EX/MEM/MEM/WB writers, x0, AUIPC/immediates, captured-WB store/branch/JALR/M-unit operands and prolonged dmem/divider holds. Verify source snapshots, held payload, exact retirement order and unchanged bus transactions/cycles.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Revised hypothesis written')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis written\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
