{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The bypass trial also reduced Fmax. I’m revising the hypothesis to a throughput opportunity: restore single-cycle low-half MUL with three truncated partial products and carry-save reduction, while keeping the registered high-half operations. Prior cycle counts suggest about 6.3% more throughput; timing will determine whether the fast path preserves enough of that gain."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r4s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r4s0','title':'Single-cycle low MUL with truncated DSP products and carry-save reduction','category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 129.85 iter/sec at 61.988 MHz and 4,773,836 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. No LESSONS.md exists. Recent micro_opt mux folding\nfailed the acceptance margin. Moving all four multiplies into a shared\nregistered unit improved Fmax, but increased CoreMark cycles from\n4,491,817 to 4,773,836: 282,019 extra cycles, approximately 6.28 percent.\nLow MUL now waits for operand capture, products, reduction and result\ntransfer even though its low 32 bits need no high-half or signed correction.\nThe old full-width signed high products caused the previous timing problem;\na dedicated truncated low product offers a narrower fast path.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Give only ALU_MUL a single-cycle combinational fast path, retaining the\nchampion's registered multiplier for MULH/MULHU/MULHSU and its iterative\ndivider unchanged. Compute three unsigned products: ll = a[15:0]*b[15:0]\nwith a 32-bit result, lh = a[15:0]*b[31:16] modulo 2\"'^16, and\nhl = a[31:16]*b[15:0] modulo 2''^16. Explicitly discard the upper bits of\nboth cross products and omit hh completely from this fast path. Signed\nand unsigned low multiplication have identical modulo-2''^32 results.\nUse Gowin-inferred DSP products, with no fabric multiplier fallback.\n\nReduce x=ll[31:16], y=lh, z=hl using a 16-bit carry-save compressor:\ns=x XOR y XOR z; c=((x AND y) OR (x AND z) OR (y AND z)) shifted left\none bit and truncated to 16 bits. Finish with exactly one 16-bit addition\ncolumn=s+c modulo 2''^16. Return {column,ll[15:0]}. This avoids serial\nthree-operand carry propagation and every high-word carry/correction.\nDo not truncate ll, forget shifted carry bits, or sign-normalize operands.\n\nRemove only legal valid ALU_MUL from EX'\"'s multicycle ownership condition.\nIt advances through the existing normal_result, EX/MEM forwarding and\nchannel-0 retirement in the same cycle as an integer ALU instruction.\nAll high-half multiply and divide requests retain their original launch,\nforwarded operand snapshots, frontend holds and exactly-once completion.\nGate the registered multiplier request and result-ready off for low MUL\nin the ALU dispatcher. Keep its standalone support for all four operations\nunchanged. Expose low MUL as a combinational operation in ALU unit tests;\nretain every existing vector and reference result. Preserve all exact\nsingle-cycle ALTOPS substitutions, which already model MUL combinationally.\n\nThis is one arithmetic micro-optimization, with no new pipeline stage,\nissue-width change, predictor or memory change. The expected benefit is\nrecovering roughly 6.28 percent iterations/cycle from low-MUL hold cycles.\nThe timing risk is forwarding through DSP products and the final 16-bit\nadder: register isolation must remain for all high-half operations, and\ntruncated carry-save reduction is essential. Only measured median Gowin\nFmax times marker-bracketed stalled CoreMark throughput determines success.\nIf the bracketed cycle count returns to 4,491,817, median Fmax must exceed\napproximately 61.009 MHz to beat 135.8231 iter/sec, the 4.6 percent margin.\nThe cycle prediction is informed by prior history, not a measured result\nfor this candidate. Retain nret=1, decoder defaults, traps and all gates.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Add the low-only combinational three-product DSP datapath with 16-bit carry-save compression and one final 16-bit add. ALU_MUL selects this result; registered multiplier request/result dispatch excludes only low MUL. Keep high multiplies, divider, integer operations and exact ALTOPS formulas unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Exclude legal valid ALU_MUL from multicycle ownership so it uses the existing single-cycle EX/MEM result, forwarding and retirement path. Preserve all high-half multiply and divide ownership, snapshot and backpressure behavior.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain all arithmetic vectors and exact references; test low MUL through the combinational helper while keeping high multiply/divide handshakes. Add directed low-column carry and truncation cases plus signed extrema, random pairs and changed operands between consecutive low-MUL evaluations.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all architectural checks and adapt only expectations specifically tied to old low-MUL latency. Cover low MUL dependencies into ALU, loads/stores, branches, JALR, x0 and consecutive low/high MUL/DIV; both bus stalls and older blocked memory. Check exact forwarded operands, single retirement/order and no low-MUL frontend hold beyond ordinary hazards. Require unchanged formal, real arithmetic tests, cosim, CRCs and measured full fitness.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nt=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/f88745d5/7e2575b4/hyp-r4s0-4jkqtrn6')\nfor f in ['core.sv','ex_stage.sv','forward_unit.sv','core_pkg.sv','id_stage.sv']:\n Path('cores/bench/rtl',f).write_text((t/(f+'.original')).read_text())\nPath('cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv').write_text((t/'reg_file.original.sv').read_text())\np=Path('cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv'); s=(t/'alu.original.sv').read_text()\ns=s.replace('  logic        [4:0]  shamt;','''  logic        [4:0]  shamt;\n\"'`ifndef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  logic [31:0] low_ll;\n  logic [15:0] low_lh, low_hl, low_x, low_sum, low_carry, low_column;\n  assign low_ll = a[15:0] * b[15:0];\n  assign low_lh = a[15:0] * b[31:16];\n  assign low_hl = a[31:16] * b[15:0];\n  assign low_x = low_ll[31:16];\n  assign low_sum = low_x ''^ low_lh ''^ low_hl;\n  assign low_carry = ((low_x & low_lh) | (low_x & low_hl) | (low_lh & low_hl)) << 1;\n  assign low_column = low_sum + low_carry;\n`endif'\"''')\ns=s.replace('assign is_multiply = op == ALU_MUL || op == ALU_MULH ||','assign is_multiply = op == ALU_MULH ||')\ns=s.replace('      ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU:\\\\n                   out = mul_result;','''      ALU_MUL:     out = {low_column, low_ll[15:0]};\n      ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU:\n                   out = mul_result;''')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv');s=p.read_text().replace('(in.ctrl.alu_op == ALU_MUL || in.ctrl.alu_op == ALU_MULH ||','(in.ctrl.alu_op == ALU_MULH ||');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/test/test_alu.py');s=(t/'test_alu.original.py').read_text();s=s.replace('async def _check_mul(dut, op, a, b, expected):\\\\n','''async def _check_mul(dut, op, a, b, expected):\n    if op == ALU_MUL:\n        await _check(dut, op, a, b, expected)\n        return\n''');p.write_text(s)\nprint('Written and trial prepared')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
