uction regression 113.58 51.019\nhyp-20261004-002-r4s1 structural Retimed bypass control with registered complete ALU operand selections improvement 140.75 67.19\nhyp-20261004-003-r4s2 predictor One-bit direction prediction with early branch mismatch selection regression 138.33 62.195\nhyp-20261004-001-r5s0 micro_opt Explicit banked register file with local flops and shallow read muxes improvement 166.64 79.55\nhyp-20261004-002-r5s1 structural Partition EX into independent memory-address and register-result producer paths regression 155.41 74.191\nhyp-20261004-003-r5s2 predictor One-bit predictor with registered direct recovery address and mismatch predicate regression 153.96 69.223\n\nhyp-20261004-001-r3s0\nReplace the encoded forwarding selectors with mutually exclusive\n\n…[12871 of 15943 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ecce5511c03096d8]…\n 24 existing pipeline tests. The\ntwo omitted baseline-only redirect-timing scenarios require predictor-aware\nstimulus during implementation; their architectural checks must remain.\nCanonical stalled CoreMark completed in bounds with every required CRC and the\nvalidation literal, taking 4,496,136 marker-bracketed cycles. Gowin\nplacement options 0/1/2 reached 64.214/67.947/67.947 MHz, median 67.947,\nwith 3,206 logic cells, 916 registers, eight LUT-RAMs, six BSRAMs and two\nDSPs. These measurements imply 151.12 iterations/sec, approximately\n7.37 percent above 140.75 and above the 147.2245 acceptance threshold.\nThe final worst option-0 path remains operand/ALU/memory-address logic,\n20.868 ns across 13 cells. This is trial evidence, not an accepted result;\nformal must pass again on the implementation, and full predictor-specific\ncoverage remains an implementation gate.\nAdded state and routing remain the main risks. Reimplementation must\nreproduce the median Fmax and bracketed cycles with unchanged checks.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
