 M select bits. ALU multiply/divide dispatch and divide\n  signed/remainder choices use the same registered vector. Retain the\n  encoded operation only where the multiplier snapshots its exact\n  requested high/low variant; do not introduce a new decode on the\n  completion-to-fro\n…[3195 of 6267 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2f62f43742c4f0ee]…\ninputs from EX.\n      Use those selects for M request class and DIV/REM mode without\n      changing integer or real RV32M arithmetic. Maintain\n      a truthful request-ready interface and exact ALTOPS substitutions.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing arithmetic vector and drive the one-hot\n      select vector consistently with each operation. Check changing live op/operands after\n      acceptance, held completion, multiply/divide alternation, reset\n      cancellation, and one result per accepted request.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all existing checks and add alternating MUL/high-MUL/DIV/REM\n      dependencies, consecutive M operations, illegal encodings, x0,\n      older stalled stores and simultaneous imem stalls. Verify exact\n      operands/results, stable requests, frontend release only on actual\n      completion and exactly-once monotonic retirement. Require the\n      unchanged formal, cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
