{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r8s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Register forwarding grants directly without encoded-select round trips\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 205.00 iterations/sec at median 97.865 MHz and\n  4,773,836 marker-bracketed cycles. Its recorded worst path starts at\n  fwd_rs1_sel and ends at fwd_rs2_sel through EX and the forwarding\n  unit. Ordinary branch/store/JALR forwarding still uses a binary\n  selection, unlike the complete registered ALU choices. Decoding that\n  binary choice precedes JALR alignment and producer eligibility;\n  encoding the next prioritized choice and decoding it again precede\n  capture of the next ALU grants. LESSONS.md is absent. r3s0 proposed\n  one-hot forwarding before selector retiming and gained only 0.94\n  percent; this proposal applies direct grants to the current registered\n  topology. The latest bank/bypass fusion regressed 1.81 percent.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the two encoded registered forwarding choices with two\n  three-bit, mutually exclusive grant vectors captured on exactly the\n  existing ID/EX payload-capture edge. Use bit zero for ID/EX register\n  value, bit one for EX/MEM and bit two for retained MEM/WB. The\n  forwarding unit computes these grants directly from the existing\n  destination matches and actual post-trap producer eligibility:\n  EX = eligible_EX && rd_EX != 0 && rd_EX == rs;\n  WB = !EX && eligible_WB && rd_WB != 0 && rd_WB == rs;\n  RF = !EX && !WB. Do not form or register a binary selector in the\n  functional path. Preserve all existing eligibility, younger-writer\n  priority and load-use handling; trapping writers cannot claim a grant.\n\n  Form ordinary architectural rs1 and rs2 as masked ORs of their three\n  data sources using the registered grant bits directly. These values\n  continue feeding branch comparison, JALR and effective-address adders,\n  raw store data and RVFI/M acceptance snapshots. Build the upcoming\n  complete ALU choices directly from the incoming grant bits and the\n  existing validated PC/immediate override controls, avoiding equal\n…[2058 of 5130 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f49991066461a584]…\nhe ordinary forwarding grant vectors alongside ID/EX\n      using the existing capture/hold schedule. Build complete ALU choices\n      from grant bits directly. Preserve reset values, one-hot ALU grants\n      and nret=1 ports; any encoded observation aliases feed tests only.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace binary ordinary forwarding cases with three-source masked\n      ORs driven directly by registered grants. Preserve all architectural\n      operand consumers, alignment traps, snapshots and target arithmetic.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every existing assertion. Check one-hot ordinary grants,\n      youngest-writer priority, x0, post-trap fallback, complete ALU\n      overrides and retained selections under memory and M holds. Cover\n      all JALR base/immediate low-bit combinations for each forwarding\n      source; verify traps, link suppression, sequential/redirect next PC,\n      exact source values, no wrong-path requests and retirement order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
