ushed invalid payload.\n  By the time its sequential successor is refetched, the trapped\n  producer's registered write eligibility is false. Thus no valid\n  instruction may consume the false predicted link value.\n\n  Preserve full branch/JAL/JALR target arithmetic, JALR bit-zero \n…[1624 of 4696 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c2907ca8bc4092fa]…\ne only predicted non-M next_reg_write from validated\n      write intent and validity rather than fault-qualified write control.\n      Keep actual EX/MEM write cancellation, alignment traps, RVFI next PC,\n      M completion and all pipeline/memory holds exactly enforced.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Keep all architectural assertions and fixed correctness gates.\n      Add misaligned JAL/JALR recovery cases across all base/immediate\n      low bits, each forwarding source, x0, older writer conflicts and\n      simultaneous instruction/data backpressure. Check recovery to PC+4,\n      killed prefetched payload, exact refetch and retirement once only,\n      trap and suppressed link writes, no wrong-path memory effects,\n      correct retained older register values and strict RVFI order.\n      Update the post-trap test's implementation-specific bypass-source\n      expectation to reflect refetch after a bubble, retaining every\n      source-value, trap, memory-effect and retirement assertion.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
