{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if x.strip()]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-001-r8s0','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-001-r10s0']:\n  print(r['id'])\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r8s0\nSimplify only the predicted producer eligibility consumed by the\nretimed forwarding unit, using the existing selection-register\ncapture enable as the authority for backend holds.\n\nIn EX remove !stall and the normal-path !is_divide term from\nnext_reg_write. Keep the exact completion selection:\ndivide_active_q ? (div_result_valid &&\ndivide_snapshot_q.ctrl.reg_write) : normal_result.ctrl.reg_write.\nIn MEM remove only !hold_wb from next_reg_write, retaining\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write && in.valid. Do not remove validity,\nalignment-fault or actual write qualification from these bundles.\n\nThe justification is cycle-local and must be checked: dmem stall\nalready makes hold_id_payload true, so no forwarding or complete\nALU selection register captures either predicted enable. M launch\nand busy likewise make hold_id_payload true. A result-completion\nedge that releases ID/EX already uses the active-owner completion\narm, which remains exactly unchanged. On every edge where\nhold_id_payload is false, both simplified predicted enables must\nequal the original expressions. Changed values during a held edge\nare unconsumed combinational values, not architectural write enables.\n\nLeave the actual EX/MEM and MEM/WB capture/hold logic, M request\ngating and ownership, regfile write enables, memory strobes and\nretirement validity exactly unchanged. Keep normal_result's complete\nvalidity and jump-alignment write suppression, MEM's load-alignment\ncancellation, x0 checks, youngest-writer priority, held retired WB\ndata, registered complete ALU overrides and all forwarding captures.\nPreserve redirect priorities, illegal decoding, every arithmetic and\nALTOPS result, nret=1 IO and strict retirement order.\n\nThis is one Boolean factoring micro-optimization without changing\npipeline stages, instruction schedules or any recovery behavior.\nRemoving redundant terms shortens producer qualification after JALR\nalignment and reduces backend-control fanout into forwarding logic.\nPredict 6 percent fitness improvement with low confidence b\n…[7363 of 10435 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:20092b44e67097d3]…\ns and Boolean-result factoring also regressed and are excluded.\n\nExpected marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles remain 4,527,071. Require\nall scored Gowin placement options, unchanged correctness gates,\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRCs and validation text, and bounded\naccesses. Acceptance requires fitness above 249.30364 iterations/sec\nand median Fmax above 112.861528 MHz at unchanged cycles. The main\nrisks are synthesis factoring the candidates back into a shared\ncarry/mux path, extra source/control fanout and other nearly critical\npaths. The exact final RTL trial passes warning-free Verilator lint,\nthe unchanged pipeline cocotb suite and all eight full-RVFI selftest\nand random-program cosim comparisons with and without both bus stalls.\nCanonical stalled CoreMark retains all five required CRCs, validation\ntext, bounded accesses and exactly 4,527,071 start/stop-bracketed cycles.\nIts final formal and scored vendor timing are still pending, so the\npredicted clock/fitness gain has low confidence and is not measured.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The champion’s worst path runs from an EX result through JALR alignment checking and back into forwarding selection. I’m proposing a structural break in that loop: predict bypass eligibility from decoded writer intent, and use sequential recovery to squash and refetch younger instructions when a jump faults. Actual writes remain suppressed on faults."}}
