{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id']=='hyp-20261004-002-r9s1':\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(r['hypothesis'],dict) else r['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Insert one two-entry FALL-THROUGH elastic instruction queue between the existing speculative fetch PC/predictor and decode, preserving single issue, in-order execution and nret=1. The fetch PC advances only when a real io_imemReady instruction is accepted directly by decode or stored in the queue, and capacity exists. Backend load-use, dmem and M holds inhibit queue consumption, not fetch production. Continue prefetching along the existing predicted path until the queue fills. No instruction or data cache, outstanding bus transaction, issue-width change or predictor algorithm change is involved.\n\nUse head and tail payload registers with a two-bit occupancy count. Each entry contains its own fetch PC, original instruction, prepared recovery address, predicted_taken and direct_aligned metadata. When occupied, decode observes the registered head directly. When empty, decode sees the current raw fetch payload and its prediction metadata through an occupancy-controlled bypass, retaining the champion's zero-buffer-latency delivery. Never mux payload by a live hazard/redirect signal; only the registered empty flag selects the bypass, and ready controls validity. A successful dequeue shifts tail to head only when needed. Support simultaneous enqueue/dequeue at occupancy one and two, including a full queue replacing its consumed tail, without dropping or duplicating any instruction. Do not count an unready raw imem payload as a queued instruction. When full without dequeue, retain the fetch PC; when external imemReady is low, retain the unaccepted fetch PC. An empty queue with ready instruction data and an accepting consumer transfers directly to decode without enqueue/dequeue or occupancy change. If decode is held instead, store that accepted fetch in the head. When occupied, preserve FIFO ordering while accepting new fetches into available tail capacity. There is no mandatory new instruction stage or initial/refill bubble; buffered entries alone cross the added storage boundary.\n\nDistinguish raw instruction-bus availabi\n…[2199 of 5271 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fa4d02b98565fb97]…\ntarget and memory alignment traps, default-illegal decoding, all real and ALTOPS arithmetic, memory bounds, exact top-level ports and strictly consecutive channel-0 order.\n\nThis is one structural decoupling of instruction production and consumption. Measure both bracketed cycles and all three Gowin placement options because queue registers and shift/occupancy controls cost area and the occupied/empty payload choice can lengthen decode paths. Require canonical CRCs, validation literal, bounded accesses, exact marker timing and fitness above 232.91282 iterations/sec. Predict an eight-percent gain with medium confidence; queue starvation during long instruction stalls, empty/occupied selection routing and fetch-control routing are the main risks. Preserve every architectural assertion in unit and fixed verification gates; update only internal test assumptions that incorrectly equate the live fetch address/payload with an occupied queue head. When the queue is empty, preserve that original direct-fetch relation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
