{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261004-002-r13s1\ntitle: \\\"Two-slot circular fall-through fetch buffer with producer-local writes\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 238.34 iter/sec at 107.897 MHz and 4,527,071\n  marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; structural\n  history was reviewed. The r9s1 two-entry fall-through queue reduced\n  cycles to 4,190,068 and scored 236.32 at 99.018 MHz, coming closest\n  among recent structural attempts. Its head/tail shifting and full-pop\n  producer lookahead coupled consumer control to wide payload enables.\n  The r12s1 circular queue removed shifting but mandatory registration\n  raised cycles to 4,271,914; it scored 233.01 at 99.541 MHz. A two-slot\n  circular buffer retaining empty fall-through targets these specific\n  costs within one frontend topology. Private arithmetic-duplication and\n  asynchronous full/hybrid RAM register-file trials failed option-0\n  timing, so those mechanisms are excluded from this final proposal.\nhypothesis: |\n  Insert one two-entry circular fall-through instruction buffer between\n  the existing speculative IF/predictor and ID. Preserve single issue,\n  nret=1 and the backend pipeline. Use two constant-index 98-bit local\n  packed-vector payload registers holding PC, instruction, recovery\n  address, predicted_taken and direct_aligned. Each slot owns an\n  independent producer write enable. Use one-bit head and tail pointers\n  and three one-hot occupancy states: empty, one and full. Never shift,\n  copy or compact a stored payload when decode consumes an entry.\n  Packed vectors avoid the unpacked-struct-array formal frontend failure\n  documented in the r12 precursor.\n\n  When empty, decode receives the current raw fetch immediately; when\n  occupied, it receives the stored head. Implement this as one shallow\n  three-source masked OR, driven by registered mutually exclusive source\n  grants for raw, slot zero and slot one. Derive those grants from next\n  occupancy/head state on each edge and reset to raw selection. Avoid a\n  slot mux followed by an empty-bypass mux. Ready and consumer hazards\n  affect availability and transfers, never the payload-source grants.\n  Stored prediction metadata belongs to its accepted fetch even when\n  subsequent training changes predictor direction.\n\n  Producer capacity is the registered not-full state, with no full-pop\n  lookahead. Accept a raw fetch only on actual io_imemReady, available\n  capacity and no reset/recovery. This acceptance alone advances fetch\n  PC. When empty and decode accepts that same fetch, deliver directly\n  without a slot write, pointer change or occupancy change. When empty\n  and decode is held, store the accepted fetch in the tail slot. When\n  occupied and not full, write the accepted fetch into the tail regardless\n  of decode consumption. A full queue deliberately declines a new fetch\n  even when decode pops that edge; its freed credit appears next cycle.\n  Never reintroduce consumer-ready lookahead into fetch-PC advancement\n  or occupied-buffer slot writes. The empty direct-transfer decision may\n  suppress a slot write but cannot stall an otherwise acceptable fetch.\n\n  Consume a stored head exactly when decode can capture a valid instruction:\n  no load-use interlock, older dmem hold, M ownership or recovery. Stored\n  heads remain available when raw imemReady is zero. Feed the existing\n  hazard logic decode availability equal to nonempty OR actual raw ready,\n  separating consumer interlocks from producer hold. Stored push alone\n  increments occupancy, stored pop alone decrements it, and simultaneous\n  stored push/pop preserves occupancy while toggling both pointers. Only\n  stored transfers change pointers. Maintain head=tail whenever empty.\n  Never enqueue an unready raw word or count direct delivery twice.\n\n  Keep predictor lookup and B/J target preparation attached to raw fetch\n  PC and word. Buffer all metadata on producer acceptance. Train exactly\n  once from the advancing registered EX/MEM branch, as today. Registered\n  recovery overrides capacity, bus unavailability and both transfers;\n  clear occupancy, reset pointers/source grants and redirect PC using the\n  existing registered target. The resident younger ID/EX instruction still\n  receives the existing recovery squash before any side effect or M launch.\n  Reset cancels all buffered instructions.\n\n  This is one structural reorganization of instruction production, storage\n  and consumption. Preserve all arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, actual\n  producer eligibility, youngest-writer priority, x0, retained WB bypass\n  values, load-use bubbles, M snapshots/completion, stable outstanding\n  requests, decoder default-illegal discipline, alignment traps, exact\n  nret=1 memory/RVFI ports and consecutive channel-0 retirement. Change\n  only internal test assumptions equating buffered decode with live fetch\n  PC/data; retain every architectural assertion and fixed gate.\n\n  This final topology has not been implemented, timed or verified. Prior\n  queue correctness supports its transfer protocol, not a measured gain\n  for this proposal. Expected benefit is roughly the earlier fall-through\n  cycle reduction with local write controls and less storage/read cost\n  than the three-slot registered design. At 4,190,068 cycles, acceptance\n  above 249.30364 iter/sec requires median Gowin Fmax above 104.459 MHz;\n  full-credit deferral may increase cycles and raise that requirement.\n  Measure actual bracketed cycles and all three placement options. Remaining\n  ALU paths, the decode OR, source-grant updates and forfeited full-pop fetches\n  may erase the gain; confidence is low. Require unchanged formal and\n  complete-RVFI cosim gates, canonical stalled 2K CoreMark CRCs, validation\n  literal, bounded accesses and marker-only timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/fetch_buffer.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the two-slot circular fall-through buffer with independent local\n      packed-vector slot writes, head/tail bits, one-hot occupancy and\n      registered raw/slot source grants. Implement direct delivery, exact\n      stored transfer conservation, registered producer credit, full-pop\n      deferral, saved prediction identity and reset/recovery priority.\n      Keep consumer pop out of occupied-buffer slot-write and producer\n      acceptance cones. Do not shift wide payloads.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect raw IF to the buffer and its selected payload to ID. Supply\n      actual io_imemReady separately from buffered decode availability.\n      Use hazards for consumer acceptance and registered buffer capacity\n      for fetch production. Wire recovery/reset to both. Preserve backend,\n      training, forwarding, bus outputs and retirement wiring.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Advance PC on accepted raw fetch rather than consumer interlocks.\n      Preserve raw instruction visibility, current predictor/target logic,\n      accepted metadata and unconditional registered recovery priority\n      over an unavailable instruction bus or full buffer.\n  - file: test/test_fetch_buffer.py\n    description: |\n      Use an independent Python FIFO to compare complete accepted/delivered\n      payloads across direct delivery, every occupancy, pointer wrap,\n      simultaneous push/pop, full-pop credit delay, ready/busy changes,\n      independent stalls, reset and recovery. Check registered source-grant\n      exclusivity and exact transfer conservation. Include the new RTL.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every architectural assertion; 