{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The full timing report revealed a more specific bottleneck: Gowin maps the register file into block RAM and absorbs the operand registers into its read ports. That leaves a long path from RAM output through forwarding and the ALU. I’ll test a flop-backed, banked register file that keeps an explicit operand register boundary. The initial YAML is already written and schema-valid."}}
