{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(x['id'],x['category'],x['outcome'], x.get('fitness'),x.get('fmax_mhz'),x.get('cycles'),x['title'])\n if x['category']=='micro_opt':\n  h=x.get('hypothesis')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('CRITICAL', x.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-0e2f75b micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nNone\nCRITICAL {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261004-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 12.55 5.637 4491485 Shared borrow-driven radix-4 combinational divider\nReplace just the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation in alu.sv with\none shared, fully combinational radix-4 restoring divider. It produces\nquotient and remainder together in 16 unrolled steps, each consuming\ntwo dividend bits. Precompute exact unsigned 34-bit divisor multiples\nD, 2D, and 3D. At each step compute trial-minus-multiple for all three\ncandidates in parallel; use the subtraction borrow and a priority\nselect to choose the largest nonnegative candidate and its two-bit\nquotient digit. Do not put a separate comparator before a subtractor.\nExploit the statically bounded partial-dividend width: step j needs\nW=2*(j+1) remainder bits, a W+1-bit difference, and a check that the\nchosen 34-bit divisor multiple has no set bits at positions W and\nhigher; explicitly zero-extend both W-bit subtraction operands. This avoids\nneedless full-width arithmetic at the early steps without truncating\noverflowing multiples or accepting an invalid subtraction.\n\nNormalize operands to unsigned magnitudes only for signed DIV/REM,\nthen restore quotient sign with a[31] XOR b[31] and remainder sign\nwith a[31]. Explicitly preserve division-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1\nresults, and keep all RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions unchanged.\nThis is a local combinational arithmetic optimization: retain the\nmultiplier, other ALU operations, ALU ports, pipeline stages,\nretirement contract, and bus handshake behavior. The proposed gain\ncomes from halving the serial quotient-selection steps and sharing\nthe four division operations, with unchanged iterations per cycle.\n\nCRITICAL {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu\n…[8032 of 11104 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:52c486b8e8ce9a75]…\n16-bit\nadder: register isolation must remain for all high-half operations, and\ntruncated carry-save reduction is essential. Only measured median Gowin\nFmax times marker-bracketed stalled CoreMark throughput determines success.\nIf the bracketed cycle count returns to 4,491,817, median Fmax must exceed\napproximately 61.009 MHz to beat 135.8231 iter/sec, the 4.6 percent margin.\nThe cycle prediction is informed by prior history, not a measured result\nfor this candidate. Retain nret=1, decoder defaults, traps and all gates.\n\nCRITICAL {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_28_s0', 'slack_ns': -14.882, 'arrival_ns': 25.176, 'logic_cells': 24, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261004-002-r4s1 structural improvement 140.75 67.19 4773836 Retimed bypass control with registered complete ALU operand selections\nhyp-20261004-003-r4s2 predictor regression 138.33 62.195 4496136 One-bit direction prediction with early branch mismatch selection\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
