ual\nforwarded source values, operation and instruction metadata on acceptance.\nHold PC and ID/EX while the divider owns EX, but allow older EX/MEM and\nMEM/WB instructions to drain. When memory is ready, EX/MEM receives a\ncleared bubble while the divide is incomplete; when memory is stalled,\nretain its outstanding request using the existing dmem hold behavior.\nA completed divide holds its result until EX/MEM can accept it exactly\nonce. Then release the fron\nhyp-20261004-003-r1s2 predictor regression 12.76 5.347 Small bimodal next-PC predictor eliminates taken-branch bubbles\nhyp-20261004-001-r2s0 micro_opt regression 110.74 49.7\n…[10320 of 13392 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6a4d474bff5ae46c]…\ne early register-result bypass source and WB source for nonloads.\n\nThe memory request address and raw store-data registers capture on every edge without an outstanding older dmem hold, independently of M launch, busy, result-valid, saved M metadata and whole-bundle bubble insertion. Store data captures actual forwarded rs2. An inert instruction may change these payloads but must never issue a request. During an outstanding memory hold retain the complete address, data, width and request strobes. Completed M instructions must not substitute their saved arithmetic result or snapshot into the request-payload registers. This independent capture is essential: merely adding an address field inside the existing zero/snapshot/normal mux did not improve the current champion.\n\nComplete the resource partition by giving the clocked M service a separate result path into the saved M instruction's EX/MEM a\nhyp-20261004-003-r7s2 predictor regression 180.33 82.236 Compact 32-entry direction predictor with registered recovery\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
