{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r8s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Split bypass dependency capture from registered producer qualification\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 205.00 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax\n  97.865 MHz and 4,773,836 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst\n  path runs from fwd_rs1_sel through EX into the next fwd_rs2_sel register:\n  16.869 ns and ten cells. The r4s1 bypass retiming moved dependency\n  selection into decode, but requires the actual post-trap write enables\n  of the producers entering EX/MEM and MEM/WB. In particular, forwarded\n  JALR target alignment feeds next_reg_write and therefore the following\n  consumer's selector. The r7s1 resource partition removed arithmetic\n  ownership from memory payloads, exposing this selector feedback as the\n  next structural bottleneck. LESSONS.md is absent; the structural history\n  contains no attempt to separate dependency matching from registered\n  producer eligibility.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure bypass control into two phases without adding a pipeline\n  stage. In decode, capture independent source/destination match bits for\n  both producers that will occupy EX/MEM and MEM/WB after the same edge.\n  Compare incoming rs1 and rs2 with ID/EX.rd and EX/MEM.rd, exclude x0,\n  and preserve BOTH age candidates rather than prematurely encoding a\n  priority winner. These match registers must not depend on next_reg_write,\n  jump target alignment, forwarded operand values, M result-valid or\n  combinational MEM alignment checks. They capture with ID/EX payload and\n  hold with it under backend ownership; reset initializes every token.\n\n  In EX, resolve the stored candidates using write eligibility already\n  registered with the corresponding producer payload. Select EX/MEM only\n  when its candidate matches and its post-trap ctrl.reg_write permits\n  forwarding. Otherwise select MEM/WB when its independent candidate\n  matches and its registered post-memory-trap ctrl.reg_write permits it;\n  otherwise use the captured register-file value. Preserve younge\n…[3449 of 6521 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4656124d9eaeb4f5]…\n control\n      while preserving the exact top-level nret=1 interface and retirement.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Resolve independent held age candidates against registered post-trap\n      EX/MEM and MEM/WB write status, with younger priority and correct\n      fallback. Use the decisions consistently for all architectural\n      operand paths and one-hot ALU choices. Preserve retained WB bypass\n      when retirement valid clears, M snapshots, request-register holds,\n      traps and current execution/redirect latency.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing assertion and adapt internal selector reset\n      observations if representation changes. Add exact source/result and\n      retirement checks for simultaneous age matches, trapping JALR/load\n      non-writers, x0, held retired WB producers, all operand consumers,\n      M completion and simultaneous bus stalls. Preserve bus-stability,\n      legality, trap, progress and monotonic-order expectations.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
