{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r8s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Retiming PC-derived addresses into an independent ID/EX control-flow lane\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 205.00 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax\n  97.865 MHz and 4,773,836 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its r7s1 resource\n  partition separated memory payloads and owned M results, but EX still\n  forms PC+4 and PC+immediate alongside forwarding, integer arithmetic,\n  branch comparison, trap qualification and result selection. The\n  structural history contains no retiming of these operand-independent\n  sums into decode; LESSONS.md is absent. Local trials of deferred bypass\n  qualification and canceled-writer replay removed the original selector\n  feedback but regressed timing, exposing integer-result and redirect\n  paths. This proposal instead partitions PC-derived arithmetic across\n  the existing ID/EX boundary, with no extra instruction stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a separately registered control-flow address lane to ID/EX. During\n  decode, compute and capture sequential_pc = incoming PC + 4 and\n  direct_target = incoming PC + the existing architectural immediate.\n  Capture both on every ordinary ID/EX payload capture, including bubbles\n  and killed fetches; hold them whenever backend ownership holds that\n  consumer and initialize them on reset with the rest of the bundle.\n  Do not add EX redirect or validity qualification to these wide sums or\n  their capture enables. They depend only on fetched PC and immediate,\n  not register-file values, bypass selectors or M-unit state.\n\n  In EX, use direct_target for every conditional-branch and direct JAL\n  target, their alignment checks, redirect target and architectural\n  next-PC metadata. Use sequential_pc for JAL/JALR link writeback,\n  ordinary sequential next PC and the existing sequential next PC on\n  alignment faults. Eliminate the corresponding live EX PC+immediate\n  and PC+4 adders from these functional paths. JALR must still compute\n  forwarded rs1 + immediate in EX and clear bit zero; AUIPC must still\n  use\n…[2081 of 5153 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dc33e14839a1d9d7]…\n    decode and capture them with the existing payload enable. Preserve\n      reset, backend holds, validity kills and raw fetch decoding without\n      adding redirect or validity muxes to these address registers.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume registered direct_target for branch/JAL resolution and\n      alignment, and registered sequential_pc for link results and next\n      PC. Remove duplicate live EX sums from these paths while preserving\n      forwarded JALR addition/bit-zero clearing, AUIPC, precise traps,\n      M snapshots, independent request payloads and all transfer cycles.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Keep all existing assertions. Check PC-derived fields against each\n      valid instruction's PC/immediate, their complete hold and reset\n      behavior, exact branch/JAL/JALR target and link results, positive\n      and negative offsets, illegal/misaligned instructions, killed\n      payloads, M ownership, simultaneous bus stalls and monotonic RVFI.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
