{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-002-r4s1','hyp-20261004-002-r5s1','hyp-20261004-001-r8s0']:\n        print(r['id']); print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(r['critical_path'])\nPY\nrg --files cores/bench | head -80; rg -n '\"'^timing|gowin|''^lint|''^test|''^cosim'\"' Makefile\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-002-r4s1\nMove dependency comparison and complete ALU source-choice computation\nto the cycle in which decode captures the consumer into ID/EX. Register\nthe selections alongside that consumer, without adding an instruction\nstage. Compare incoming raw rs1/rs2 indices against the actual producers\nabout to enter EX/MEM and MEM/WB, rather than comparing the resident\nconsumer against those tags combinationally during EX. Give the upcoming\nEX/MEM producer priority over upcoming MEM/WB, exclude x0 destinations,\nand use real post-trap write eligibility. These tags predict where each\noperand value will reside in the following EX cycle.\n\nExport from EX the write eligibility of the bundle it will actually\ntransfer: a normal valid instruction after jump-alignment checks, or\nthe captured M-operation instruction on a completed result transfer.\nExport from MEM the corresponding post-memory-alignment write eligibility\nfor its upcoming WB payload. Use ID/EX's destination for the upcoming\nEX/MEM producer and current EX/MEM's destination for upcoming MEM/WB.\nDuring M result transfer the held instruction and snapshot retain the\nsame destination. No invalid or trapping non-writer may claim bypass\npriority. Derive eligibility from the actual producer logic rather than\nassuming that every decoded reg_write causes a result.\n\nRegister complete one-hot ALU input selections. ALU A chooses ID/EX rs1,\nEX/MEM result, WB result or the consumer PC for AUIPC. ALU B chooses\nID/EX rs2, EX/MEM result, WB result or the decoded immediate. Form the\nAUIPC and immediate overrides using the validated incoming decoder\ncontrols before the capture edge. In EX implement each data choice as\na parallel masked OR, avoiding a serial forwarded-value mux followed\nby PC/immediate selection. Also register the ordinary rs1/rs2 bypass\nchoices used by branch/JALR, stores and RVFI operand snapshots, retaining\ntheir existing architectural values and younger-writer priority.\n\nAdvance these selection registers exactly when ID/EX payload advances,\nincluding captu\n…[10349 of 13421 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:416d3a7164c3e1ca]…\n_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/multiplier.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/divider.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/test_divider.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_service.py\ncores/bench/test/test_predictor.py\ncores/bench/test/test_multiplier.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\n97:lint:\n106:test:\n109:test-infra:\n112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n115:cosim-build: $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv) test/cosim/main.cpp\n136:# (tools/eval/gowin.py); V2 does not synthesize with Yosys.\n140:timing:\n141:\tpython3 -m tools.eval.gowin $(TARGET)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
