{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"None of the execution-lane trials cleared the 4.6% acceptance margin. I’m testing a different structural change for the final candidate: a two-entry fetch queue that lets instruction fetch continue while decode waits on loads, data memory or M execution. It could reduce cycles lost to instruction-bus stalls while preserving in-order retirement."}}
