{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r11s2',\n'title':'Predecode predictor recovery into registered one-hot branch predicates',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already predicts conditional direction with a small 64-entry\\\\nbimodal table and protects fetch with registered recovery. Predictor\\\\nhistory shows that tagged target tables are too expensive, including the\\\\nlast attempt's 33 percent regression. Reference replay finds 41559 misses\\\\namong 529588 conditional branches, leaving limited accuracy-only headroom.\\\\nRemoving the table also failed a reversible trial: static prediction\\\\nadded 138441 cycles and reduced placement-option-0 Fmax to 94.266 MHz.\\\\nFocus on the prediction-mismatch path rather than a larger target or\\\\nhistory table. LESSONS.md is absent; predictor history was reviewed.\\\\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing 64-entry hashed two-bit direction predictor unchanged.\\\\nReplace the three-bit encoded mismatch predicate in ID/EX with six\\\\nregistered one-hot recovery-predicate grants. At the existing decode\\\\ncapture edge, combine validated branch funct3 with predicted_taken: BEQ\\\\nand BNE exchange grants for a taken prediction, as do BLT/BGE and\\\\nBLTU/BGEU. Register the complete grants alongside the accepted instruction\\\\nand retain them throughout backend ownership. This moves predicate\\\\ndecoding and prediction complementation before the operand comparison.\\\\n\\\\nIn EX, form branch_mismatch as an OR of the granted equality, inequality,\\\\nsigned less-than, signed greater-or-equal, unsigned less-than and unsigned\\\\ngreater-or-equal comparisons. Use parallel masked terms rather than an\\\\nencoded case mux after the forwarded comparison results. Preserve one\\\\ncomparison datapath and let synthesis share complementary predicates;\\\\ndo not instantiate separate architectural-outcome and recovery networks.\\\\nRecover the actual branch outcome as branch_mismatch XOR predicted_taken,\\\\nexactly as today, for training, traps and architectural RVFI metadata.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve the original table hash, old-state lookup, saturating updates,\\\\naligned direct prediction, JAL prediction, unpredicted JALR, prepared\\\\nalternate recovery operand, registered recovery phase and reuse of the\\\\nexisting EX arithmetic/effective-address lanes. Train once at advancing\\\\nEX/MEM. No new instruction stage, queue, target table, arithmetic algorithm\\\\nor top-level interface change is part of this proposal. Prediction remains\\\\nindependent of hazard/ready/flush feedback; accepted-fetch and reset/\\\\nrecovery priorities remain unchanged. Invalid or squashed instructions\\\\ncannot recover, train, launch M, advertise producers or issue memory.\\\\n\\\\nRetain every decoder legality and alignment check, stable outstanding\\\\nmemory requests, retained WB forwarding, real/ALTOPS arithmetic, nret=1\\\\nIO and consecutive retirement order. A zero grant vector must be inert,\\\\nand reserved predicates must not become valid through the new encoding.\\\\nThis is one optimization to the predictor's recovery path. Its intended\\\\ngain is a shorter comparison-to-registered-recovery path and less encoded\\\\ncontrol fanout, with exactly unchanged canonical CoreMark cycle count.\\\\nExpect seven percent fitness improvement, with low confidence until vendor\\\\ntiming confirms it. Require the unchanged formal/cosim gates, all canonical\\\\nCRCs and validation text, bounded accesses, marker-only cycle counting and\\\\nfitness strictly above 249.30364 iterations/sec.\\\\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Replace id_ex_t.mismatch_op with a six-bit one-hot mismatch_grants field. Keep predicted_taken, alignment, recovery operand and every architectural/RVFI field intact.'},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Predecode and register the six complete complementary branch-predicate grants from validated branch funct3 and the accepted predicted_taken bit. Reset grants to zero; capture on the existing payload edge and hold with the consumer.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace encoded mismatch selection with parallel granted comparisons and OR reduction over the original forwarded operands. Preserve actual-outcome reconstruction, trap/alignment gating, one-shot registered recovery, lane reuse, training metadata and producer/M ownership semantics.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all architectural checks and adapt only bundle bit-offset introspection to the wider internal grant field. Verify exact one-hot/zero grants for all six legal predicates and both prediction directions, reset and held metadata. Exercise equality and signed/unsigned boundary operands, direction reversals, bus stalls, load-use, wrong-path suppression, traps, PCs and consecutive RVFI order.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Revised complete predictor hypothesis written.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
