{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport subprocess,os,json\nfrom tools.eval.fpga import validate_coremark_uart\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/predictor_research').resolve()\ndef trial(name):\n env=dict(os.environ,RTL_DIR=str(root/name/'rtl'),OBJ_DIR=str(root/name/'obj_dir'),NRET='1')\n with (root/name/'build.log').open('w') as f:\n  subprocess.run(['bash','test/cosim/build.sh'],env=env,stdout=f,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,check=True)\n r=subprocess.run([str(root/name/'obj_dir/cosim_sim'),str(root/'coremark.elf'),'50000000','--bench','--istall','--dstall'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True)\n (root/name/'coremark.jsonl').write_text(r.stdout)\n d=json.loads(r.stdout.splitlines()[-1]); print(name,'cycles',d['bench_stop_cycle']-d['bench_start_cycle'],'validation',validate_coremark_uart(d['uart'],10),'oob',d['oob'],flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n list(pool.map(trial,('shared16','shared32','shared32adj')))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r11s2',\n'title':'Share hysteresis between paired bimodal direction entries',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion's 64-entry hashed bimodal predictor is already accurate:\\\\nreference replay gives 41559 misses among 529588 conditional branches.\\\\nA tagged target predictor recently lost 33 percent fitness, and a new\\\\nstatic-direction trial added 138441 cycles while reducing Fmax. Larger\\\\naccuracy machinery has little throughput headroom. Sharing the confidence\\\\nstate behind independent direction bits offers a smaller adaptive\\\\npredictor without enlarging the fetch lookup or changing recovery.\\\\nLESSONS.md is absent; the predictor experiments in log.jsonl were reviewed.\\\\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the 64 independent two-bit saturating counters with 64 independent\\\\ndirection bits and 32 shared strong/weak confidence bits. Keep exactly the\\\\nexisting six-bit index, PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], and the existing grouped\\\\ndirection lookup. Pool index is the low five index bits; entries i and\\\\ni+32 share one confidence bit while keeping separate directions.\\\\nReset every direction to not taken and every confidence bit to weak.\\\\n\\\\nOn one advancing legal aligned branch training event, read the selected\\\\nentry's old direction and its pool's old confidence. If the confidence\\\\nis weak, overwrite only that entry's direction with the actual outcome;\\\\nif strong, retain direction. Then set the selected pool's confidence\\\\nto strong iff actual outcome equals the OLD selected direction, otherwise\\\\nweak. Other entries and pools hold. This is the usual two-bit hysteresis\\\\nstate machine expressed as direction plus confidence, with one confidence\\\\nbit shared per pair. Pooling can change prediction accuracy through\\\\naliasing; it must never change architectural resolution or trap behavior.\\\\n\\\\nImplement both state banks with constant-index local flops and write\\\\nenables. Each confidence pool selects its old direction from just its\\\\ntwo constant-index prediction bits using train_index[5], avoiding a\\\\n64-way indexed read/modify/write. Each direction entry has one local\\\\nselected-training enable additionally qualified by its pool being weak.\\\\nLookup sees pre-edge direction state with no training bypass. Publish the\\\\nsame counter_msb direction vector if needed for existing test visibility.\\\\nThere are 96 predictor state bits rather than 128, a 25 percent reduction.\\\\nThe intended gain is lower update/reset/control routing and a simpler\\\\nstate transition circuit while retaining the existing 64-entry fetch\\\\nread topology. No predictor SRAM, tags, target cache or global history.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve the champion's exact B/J target construction, legal predecode,\\\\nalignment gating, aligned JAL prediction and unpredicted JALR. Preserve\\\\npredicted_taken and complemented mismatch metadata, prepared recovery\\\\noperand, registered recovery, reuse of existing EX result/address lanes\\\\nand registered training at advancing EX/MEM. Prediction never depends\\\\non ready, flush or hazard feedback; stalled fetch is not accepted.\\\\nReset/recovery PC priorities, backend metadata holds, one-shot recovery\\\\nand training, load-use bubbles, retained WB forwarding, stable requests,\\\\nwrong-path suppression, decoder legality, real/ALTOPS M arithmetic,\\\\nnret=1 ports, architectural RVFI PCs and consecutive order remain intact.\\\\n\\\\nReference replay gives 42100 misses for this pooling versus 41559 for\\\\nindependent counters, only 541 additional misses; this is predictor-only\\\\nreplay, not an RTL cycle or timing guarantee. Expect six percent fitness\\\\nimprovement from reduced predictor circuitry, with low confidence because\\\\nthe champion's worst timing paths currently cross EX and bypass control.\\\\nRequire all unchanged correctness gates, canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs\\\\nand validation text, bounded accesses, marker-bracketed cycle counting and\\\\nmedian Gowin fitness strictly above 249.30364 iterations/sec.\\\\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace binary per-entry counters with 64 direction flops and 32 constant-index shared confidence flops. Pair entries that share index[4:0], use only a two-input local training-direction mux per pool, and implement the old-state update rule. Keep the existing hash, fetch read network, training interface, predecode/targets/recovery operand and acceptance priorities.'},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'Replace independent-counter internal expectations with an independent direction-plus-shared-confidence model while preserving every target, predecode, reset, stall and recovery assertion. Cover all 32 pools, both member entries, same-index collisions, opposite outcomes between paired members, saturation/hysteresis, old-state simultaneous lookup/training, non-selected-entry retention and reset after training.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all architectural assertions and update the independent predictor model and prediction-specific timing expectations to the exact 64-direction/32-confidence pooling policy. Exercise aliases that share only confidence, both direction mismatch cases, prolonged bus stalls, load-dependent branches, M ownership, traps, wrong-path stores and exactly-once training. Verify RVFI PCs/order and all retained result/forwarding behavior.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Complete pooled-hysteresis hypothesis written.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r11s2',\n'title':'Share hysteresis between paired bimodal direction entries',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion's 64-entry hashed bimodal predictor is already accurate:\\\\nreference replay gives 41559 misses among 529588 conditional branches.\\\\nA tagged target predictor recently lost 33 percent fitness, and a new\\\\nstatic-direction trial added 138441 cycles while reducing Fmax. Larger\\\\naccuracy machinery has little throughput headroom. Sharing the confidence\\\\nstate behind independent direction bits offers a smaller adaptive\\\\npredictor without enlarging the fetch lookup or changing recovery.\\\\nLESSONS.md is absent; the predictor experiments in log.jsonl were reviewed.\\\\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the 64 independent two-bit saturating counters with 64 independent\\\\ndirection bits and 32 shared strong/weak confidence bits. Keep exactly the\\\\nexisting six-bit index, PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], and the existing grouped\\\\ndirection lookup. Pool index is the low five index bits; entries i and\\\\ni+32 share one confidence bit while keeping separate directions.\\\\nReset every direction to not taken and every confidence bit to weak.\\\\n\\\\nOn one advancing legal aligned branch training event, read the selected\\\\nentry's old direction and its pool's old confidence. If the confidence\\\\nis weak, overwrite only that entry's direction with the actual outcome;\\\\nif strong, retain direction. Then set the selected pool's confidence\\\\nto strong iff actual outcome equals the OLD selected direction, otherwise\\\\nweak. Other entries and pools hold. This is the usual two-bit hysteresis\\\\nstate machine expressed as direction plus confidence, with one confidence\\\\nbit shared per pair. Pooling can change prediction accuracy through\\\\naliasing; it must never change architectural resolution or trap behavior.\\\\n\\\\nImplement both state banks with constant-index local flops and write\\\\nenables. Each confidence pool selects its old direction from just its\\\\ntwo constant-index prediction bits using train_index[5], avoiding a\\\\n64-way indexed read/modify/write. Each direction entry has one local\\\\nselected-training enable additionally qualified by its pool being weak.\\\\nLookup sees pre-edge direction state with no training bypass. Publish the\\\\nsame counter_msb direction vector if needed for existing test visibility.\\\\nThere are 96 predictor state bits rather than 128, a 25 percent reduction.\\\\nThe intended gain is lower update/reset/control routing and a simpler\\\\nstate transition circuit while retaining the existing 64-entry fetch\\\\nread topology. No predictor SRAM, tags, target cache or global history.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve the champion's exact B/J target construction, legal predecode,\\\\nalignment gating, aligned JAL prediction and unpredicted JALR. Preserve\\\\npredicted_taken and complemented mismatch metadata, prepared recovery\\\\noperand, registered recovery, reuse of existing EX result/address lanes\\\\nand registered training at advancing EX/MEM. Prediction never depends\\\\non ready, flush or hazard feedback; stalled fetch is not accepted.\\\\nReset/recovery PC priorities, backend metadata holds, one-shot recovery\\\\nand training, load-use bubbles, retained WB forwarding, stable requests,\\\\nwrong-path suppression, decoder legality, real/ALTOPS M arithmetic,\\\\nnret=1 ports, architectural RVFI PCs and consecutive order remain intact.\\\\n\\\\nReference replay gives 42100 misses for this pooling versus 41559 for\\\\nindependent counters, only 541 additional misses; this is predictor-only\\\\nreplay, not an RTL cycle or timing guarantee. Expect six percent fitness\\\\nimprovement from reduced predictor circuitry, with low confidence because\\\\nthe champion's worst timing paths currently cross EX and bypass control.\\\\nRequire all unchanged correctness gates, canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs\\\\nand validation text, bounded accesses, marker-bracketed cycle counting and\\\\nmedian Gowin fitness strictly above 249.30364 iterations/sec.\\\\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace binary per-entry counters with 64 direction flops and 32 constant-index shared confidence flops. Pair entries that share index[4:0], use only a two-input local training-direction mux per pool, and implement the old-state update rule. Keep the existing hash, fetch read network, training interface, predecode/targets/recovery operand and acceptance priorities.'},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'Replace independent-counter internal expectations with an independent direction-plus-shared-confidence model while preserving every target, predecode, reset, stall and recovery assertion. Cover all 32 pools, both member entries, same-index collisions, opposite outcomes between paired members, saturation/hysteresis, old-state simultaneous lookup/training, non-selected-entry retention and reset after training.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all architectural assertions and update the independent predictor model and prediction-specific timing expectations to the exact 64-direction/32-confidence pooling policy. Exercise aliases that share only confidence, both direction mismatch cases, prolonged bus stalls, load-dependent branches, M ownership, traps, wrong-path stores and exactly-once training. Verify RVFI PCs/order and all retained result/forwarding behavior.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Complete pooled-hysteresis hypothesis written.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Complete pooled-hysteresis hypothesis written.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport subprocess,os,json\nfrom tools.eval.fpga import validate_coremark_uart\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/predictor_research').resolve()\ndef trial(name):\n env=dict(os.environ,RTL_DIR=str(root/name/'rtl'),OBJ_DIR=str(root/name/'obj_dir'),NRET='1')\n with (root/name/'build.log').open('w') as f:\n  subprocess.run(['bash','test/cosim/build.sh'],env=env,stdout=f,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,check=True)\n r=subprocess.run([str(root/name/'obj_dir/cosim_sim'),str(root/'coremark.elf'),'50000000','--bench','--istall','--dstall'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True)\n (root/name/'coremark.jsonl').write_text(r.stdout)\n d=json.loads(r.stdout.splitlines()[-1]); print(name,'cycles',d['bench_stop_cycle']-d['bench_start_cycle'],'validation',validate_coremark_uart(d['uart'],10),'oob',d['oob'],flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n list(pool.map(trial,('shared16','shared32','shared32adj')))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"shared32adj cycles 4526375 validation (True, None) oob False\nshared16 cycles 4536139 validation (True, None) oob False\nshared32 cycles 4528646 validation (True, None) oob False\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/predictor_research')\nfor pools in (8,16,32):\n name='shared'+str(pools); out=root/name/'rtl'; out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n for p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'): shutil.copy2(p,out/p.name)\n p=out/'if_stage.sv'; s=p.read_text(); start=s.index('  // Each entry owns'); end=s.index('  for (genvar g = 0; g < 8;',start)\n bits=pools.bit_length()-1\n new=f'''  wire [{pools-1}:0] strong_bits;\n  for (genvar g = 0; g < {pools}; g++) begin : gen_shared_confidence\n    localparam logic [{bits-1}:0] POOL = {bits}'(g);\n    logic strong_q;\n    logic selected_direction;\n    always_comb begin\n      case (train_index[5:{bits}])\n'''\n for k in range(64//pools):\n  new+=f\\\"        {6-bits}'d{k}: selected_direction = counter_msb[g + {k*pools}];\\\\n\\\" if k<64//pools-1 else f\\\"        default: selected_direction = counter_msb[g + {k*pools}];\\\\n\\\"\n new+=f'''      endcase\n    end\n    always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n      if (reset) strong_q <= 1'b0;\n      else if (train_valid && train_index[{bits-1}:0] == POOL)\n        strong_q <= (train_taken == selected_direction);\n    end\n    assign strong_bits[g] = strong_q;\n  end\n  for (genvar e = 0; e < 64; e++) begin : gen_predictor\n    localparam logic [5:0] INDEX = 6'(e);\n    logic direction_q;\n    always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n      if (reset) direction_q <= 1'b0;\n      else if (train_valid && train_index == INDEX && \"'!strong_bits[e % {pools}])\n        direction_q <= train_taken;\n    end\n    assign counter_msb[e] = direction_q;\n  end\n\n'\"'''\n s=s[:start]+new+s[end:]; p.write_text(s)\nprint('Prepared pooled-hysteresis direction predictor trials.')\nPY\npython3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nimport json\nwt=Path.cwd(); root=wt/'cores/bench/generated/predictor_research'\ndef trial(name):\n r=build(wt,root/name/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,root/name/'gowin_p1')\n (root/name/'timing_p1.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\n print(name,json.dumps(r),flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n list(pool.map(trial,('shared8','shared16','shared32')))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Prepared pooled-hysteresis direction predictor trials.\nshared8 {\"place_option\": 1, \"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 99.836, \"levels\": 13, \"logic\": 4444, \"regs\": 1849, \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_paths\": [{\"from\": \"cpu/alu_a_sel_3_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_31_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.016, \"arrival_ns\": 15.311, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_3_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.009, \"arrival_ns\": 15.303, \"logic_cells\": 9, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/alu_a_sel_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_25_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.002, \"arrival_ns\": 15.296, \"logic_cells\": 23, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/alu_b_sel_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.0, \"arrival_ns\": 15.295, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/alu_b_sel_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -4.987, \"arrival_ns\": 15.282, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu\"]}]}\nshared32 {\"place_option\": 1, \"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 101.932, \"levels\": 13, \"logic\": 4465, \"regs\": 1873, \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_paths\": [{\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_