{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"Shared-confidence predictors passed stalled CoreMark, but their timing gains were insufficient. The final hypothesis uses a small distributed-RAM direction table with reset scrubbing to remove the flop-heavy storage while preserving the existing recovery scheme. Its fitness gain remains unmeasured."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r11s2',\n'title':'Reset-scrubbed distributed-RAM bimodal direction predictor',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current 64-entry direction predictor stores 128 resettable counter\\\\nflops, distributes indexed training enables to every entry and reads\\\\ndirection through a grouped flop mux. Predictor history rules out larger\\\\ntagged target tables: the latest one lost 33 percent fitness. Reference\\\\nreplay already gives 41559 direction misses among 529588 branches, so\\\\naccuracy-only improvements have little headroom. Reversible research\\\\ntrials of static direction, smaller tables, one-hot recovery and shared\\\\nhysteresis did not clear the timing threshold. A physically compact\\\\ndirection-only memory offers a different storage implementation without\\\\nintroducing wide target/tag lookup or changing the pipeline topology.\\\\nLESSONS.md is absent; relevant predictor history in log.jsonl was read.\\\\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the direction-table storage and update network with four\\\\n16-entry banks of two-bit counters inferred as asynchronous-read,\\\\nsynchronous-write distributed LUT RAM. Preserve exactly the current\\\\n64-entry hash PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], two-bit saturating update semantics,\\\\nweakly-not-taken initialization and pre-edge lookup behavior. Index[5:4]\\\\nselects a bank and index[3:0] its word. Keep this direction-only: no tags,\\\\nstored targets, global history, indirect prediction or added fetch stage.\\\\n\\\\nProvide independent fetch and training read addresses. Describe each\\\\nbank as two identical resetless 16x2 memories with common write address,\\\\ndata and enable: one asynchronous copy reads fetch index and the other\\\\nreads training index. Four shallow bank selectors yield the fetch MSB\\\\nand old two-bit training counter. Compute the saturating next state once\\\\nfrom the old training counter, then write only the selected bank and\\\\nboth of its copies on the existing one-shot train_valid. There is no\\\\nwrite-through bypass; simultaneous lookup and training use old state.\\\\nUse portable synthesizable memory RTL and the vendor's supported\\\\ndistributed-memory inference attributes. Do not introduce unmodeled\\\\nvendor black boxes into formal. Confirm actual LUT-RAM inference in\\\\nGowin area reports; a flop fallback would defeat this hypothesis.\\\\n\\\\nDo not reset the memory arrays. Instead reset one initialized bit and\\\\na four-bit scrub address. During the first 16 non-reset clocks, write\\\\n2'b01 to the same scrub word in ALL four banks and both copies. Scrub\\\\nhas priority over training, which is ignored until initialization ends.\\\\nSet initialized only after the address-15 write has completed. During\\\\nscrubbing force conditional direction to not taken independently of\\\\nunknown RAM contents; aligned JAL remains predicted taken. The CPU must\\\\ncontinue normal execution and recovery during these 16 clocks: scrubbing\\\\nnever stalls fetch or the backend. A repeated reset restarts the scrub\\\\nand immediately disables RAM-derived conditional predictions. Reset-time\\\\nand pre-initialization lookup must never expose unknown target control.\\\\n\\\\nRetain the current legal B/J predecode, exact full-width target arithmetic,\\\\nalignment gating, unpredicted JALR, accepted predicted_taken metadata,\\\\ncomplemented mismatch predicate, prepared alternate recovery operand,\\\\nregistered recovery and existing execution-lane reuse. Training still\\\\ncomes only from valid legal aligned branches when EX/MEM advances; held\\\\nentries do not train repeatedly. Lookup remains independent of ready,\\\\nflush and hazard feedback. Keep accepted-fetch and reset/recovery PC\\\\npriorities, payload holds, load-use bubbles, retained WB forwarding,\\\\nstable memory requests, wrong-path suppression, all legality/alignment\\\\nchecks, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, nret=1 IO and consecutive RVFI order.\\\\nArchitectural next PCs and traps always use actual resolution.\\\\n\\\\nThis is one predictor storage architecture change. Its intended benefit\\\\nis replacing the counter-flop/reset/write-enable fabric with tiny LUT\\\\nmemories and shallow bank selection. After scrub, the predictor has the\\\\nsame capacity and hysteresis; boot training discarded during scrub can\\\\naffect initial state, so do not assume an identical benchmark cycle count.\\\\nExpect eight percent fitness improvement, with low confidence: this RAM\\\\ncandidate has not been timed, the current worst paths cross EX/bypass,\\\\nand asynchronous RAM delay or training read-modify-write can erase gains.\\\\nRequire unchanged formal and cosim gates, canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs\\\\nand validation text, bounded accesses, marker-bracketed timing and scored\\\\nmedian Gowin fitness strictly above 249.30364 iterations/sec.\\\\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/direction_predictor.sv','description':'Add a direction-only 64-entry predictor using four mirrored 16x2 resetless distributed-memory banks, independent asynchronous fetch/training reads, one shared saturating update, bank-local writes, and a global 16-clock reset scrub. Mask lookup until all banks are initialized; discard training during scrub without stalling the CPU.'},\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace the local counter flops and grouped flop lookup with the new predictor module. Preserve the exact hash and existing training interface, target/alignment logic, direction-only prediction metadata, recovery payload, raw instruction visibility and accepted-fetch/reset/recovery priorities.'},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'Preserve existing predecode, exact target, alignment, stall and recovery assertions. Extend an independent saturating-counter model with the specified 16-clock scrub and ignored early training. Cover all banks/words, both saturation limits, hysteresis reversals, collisions, two-address lookup/training, pre-edge simultaneous read/write, reset during scrub and after training, initialized masking and unaffected JAL prediction.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all architectural checks while extending the independent predictor model for reset scrub. Verify execution and recovery continue during initialization, conditional predictions stay sequential until completion, and training is accepted exactly once thereafter. Exercise prolonged bus stalls, load-dependent branches, M ownership, aliases, traps and wrong-path stores; check exact architectural PCs/links, stable requests, consecutive RVFI order and restart after reset.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261004-003-r11s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert isinstance(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'],int)\nassert -50<=d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nprint('Final hypothesis written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\ngit status --short\nls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
