{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|prediction|branch|return.address|gshare|history' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shared borrow-driven radix-4 combinational divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has a 199.837 ns worst path with 156\\ncells through forwarding and the combinational ALU, and median Fmax\\nis only 5.442 MHz. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately with / and %, exposing a large, deeply cascaded\\narithmetic network to Gowin synthesis. Shortening this network can\\nimprove every CoreMark cycle even when that cycle does not divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench result has a 199.837 ns worst path with 156\\ncells through forwarding and the combinational ALU, and median Fmax\\nis only 5.442 MHz. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately with / and %, exposing a large, deeply cascaded\\narithmetic network to Gowin synthesis. Shortening this network can\\nimprove every CoreMark cycle even when that cycle does not divide.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace just the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation in alu.sv with\\none shared, fully combinational radix-4 restoring divider. It produces\\nquotient and remainder together in 16 unrolled steps, each consuming\\ntwo dividend bits. Precompute exact unsigned 34-bit divisor multiples\\nD, 2D, and 3D. At each step compute trial-minus-multiple for all three\\ncandidates in parallel; use the subtraction borrow and a priority\\nselect to choose the largest nonnegative candidate and its two-bit\\nquotient digit. Do not put a separate comparator before a subtractor.\\nExploit the statically bounded partial-dividend width: step j needs\\nW=2*(j+1) remainder bits, a W+1-bit difference, and a check that the\\nchosen 34-bit divisor multiple has no set bits at positions W and\\nhigher; explicitly zero-extend both W-bit subtraction operands. This avoids\\nneedless full-width arithmetic at the early steps without truncating\\noverflowing multiples or accepting an invalid subtraction.\\n\\nNormalize operands to unsigned magnitudes only for si\n…[349488 of 352560 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e9e135dfc7583260]…\nuential until completion, and training is accepted exactly once thereafter. Exercise prolonged bus stalls, load-dependent branches, M ownership, aliases, traps and wrong-path stores; check exact architectural PCs/links, stable requests, consecutive RVFI order and restart after reset.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 229.29, \"delta_pct\": -3.8, \"vs_baseline\": 1791.83, \"fmax_mhz\": 103.799, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4527071, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4284, \"ff\": 1782, \"seeds\": [103.258, 103.799, 103.799], \"perturbations\": [[0, 103.258, 13], [1, 103.799, 10], [2, 103.799, 10]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.imm_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/arithmetic_result_q_27_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -4.684, \"arrival_ns\": 14.979, \"logic_cells\": 36, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T21:10:49.996916Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
