{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d.get('category')\"'!='\"'predictor': continue\n print('\\\\n', d['id'], d['title'],d.get('outcome'), d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'))\n if d.get('round_id',0)>=4 and d.get('round_id',0)<=10:\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print('IMPLEMENTATION NOTES:', d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261004-003-r1s2 Small bimodal next-PC predictor eliminates taken-branch bubbles regression 12.76 5.347 4190281\n\n hyp-20261004-003-r2s2 PC-indexed next-PC predictor with timing-isolated recovery regression 118.59 49.908 4208611\n\n hyp-20261004-003-r3s2 Direction-only branch prediction with one-bit recovery metadata regression 123.45 51.727 4190281\n\n hyp-20261004-003-r4s2 One-bit direction prediction with early branch mismatch selection regression 138.33 62.195 4496136\nImplement one compact fetch-time direction predictor on the CURRENT\nregistered-multiplier champion: 64 untagged one-bit last-outcome entries,\nindexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset to not taken. Read the selected bit\ncombinationally from PC. Predecode only legal BRANCH funct3 encodings and\nJAL from raw imem_data. A legal conditional branch predicts taken when\nits selected outcome bit is one; JAL predicts taken unconditionally.\nJALR and all other instructions predict PC+4. Construct the exact B/J\nimmediate and use a dedicated full-width PC-relative target adder in\nparallel with the existing PC+4 increment. Suppress taken prediction\nfor targets whose low two bits are nonzero. There is no BTB, tag array,\nreturn stack, lookahead register, added fetch stage or global history.\n\nCarry only predicted_taken through IF and ID/EX, capturing the actual\naccepted prediction and retaining