{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-003-r4s2','hyp-20261004-003-r5s2','hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r7s2','hyp-20261004-003-r8s2','hyp-20261004-003-r9s2','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0']:\n  print(d['id'], d['title'], 'fit',d.get('fitness'),'fmax',d.get('fmax_mhz'), 'cycles',d.get('cycles'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis'); print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-003-r4s2 One-bit direction prediction with early branch mismatch selection fit 138.33 fmax 62.195 cycles 4496136\nImplement one compact fetch-time direction predictor on the CURRENT\nregistered-multiplier champion: 64 untagged one-bit last-outcome entries,\nindexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset to not taken. Read the selected bit\ncombinationally from PC. Predecode only legal BRANCH funct3 encodings and\nJAL from raw imem_data. A legal conditional branch predicts taken when\nits selected outcome bit is one; JAL predicts taken unconditionally.\nJALR and all other instructions predict PC+4. Construct the exact B/J\nimmediate and use a dedicated full-width PC-relative target adder in\nparallel with the existing PC+4 increment. Suppress taken prediction\nfor targets whose low two bits are nonzero. There is no BTB, tag array,\nreturn stack, lookahead register, added fetch stage or global history.\n\nCarry only predicted_taken through IF and ID/EX, capturing the actual\naccepted prediction and retaining it throughout backend holds. The\nimmediate direct target is exact for that same instruction, so recovery\nneeds no stored target or 32-bit predicted-next-PC equality test.\nFold the prediction into the branch predicate selection BEFORE the\nforwarded-operand comparison result: compare using branch_op XOR\n{2'b00, predicted_taken}. This exchanges BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU,\nso the selected comparator directly says whether the predicted direction\nwas wrong. Gate conditional recovery by a legal conditional branch and\nan aligned direct target. Keep the original architectural branch outcome\nfor training, traps and RVFI. For jumps, recover when aligned actual\njump direction differs from predicted_taken; JALR stays unpredicted.\n\nSelect the recovery ADDRESS early using the carried prediction bit:\nif predicted_taken is one, recovery goes to PC+4; otherwise it goes to\nthe existing JAL/JALR or branch target. This address is consumed only\nwhen the mismatch predicate fires, making it equivalent to the resolved\nnext PC without a late\n…[34429 of 37501 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2d92a77f066626be]…\nHz. That gain\nis only about 3.1 percent, below acceptance. An existing-imm precursor\nthat retained a separate post-ALU jump select reached only 101.069\nMHz, despite passing 53 formal checks, all 36 pipeline tests, eight\nRVFI cosim comparisons and canonical stalled CoreMark with unchanged\ncycles. The FINAL proposal also folds jump result selection into the\nexisting ALU_LUI path, removing the post-ALU mux from ordinary integer\nresults rather than only shortening the jump adder. Its timing remains\nto be established. A parallel-direct-adder precursor and a 32-entry\nagree table were slower, so neither is part of this proposal. The\nprincipal risks are the JALR effective-immediate select, ID operand\nrouting and the still-present main integer ALU critical path.\nMeasure all Gowin placement options. At 4,527,071 measured cycles,\nacceptance requires fitness above 232.91282 iter/sec and median\nFmax above approximately 105.442 MHz. A seven-percent clock gain\nwould clear that threshold with unchanged CoreMark throughput.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
