{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r4s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r4s2',\n'title':'One-bit direction prediction with early branch mismatch selection',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current nret=1 champion scores 129.85 iter/sec at 61.988 MHz and\n4,773,836 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Taken control transfers\ncurrently discard the younger instruction. LESSONS.md does not exist.\nThe 32-entry tagged next-PC predictor in r2s2 reduced cycles but reached\nonly 49.908 MHz; r3s2's 64-entry two-bit direction predictor reached\n4,190,281 cycles at 51.727 MHz on the older iterative-divider parent.\nBoth failed acceptance because timing lost too much of the CPI gain.\nThe current parent has since registered multiplication. A predictor\nshould now minimize state and late recovery logic to preserve that gain.\nOne outcome bit per branch index saves half the direction-table flops,\nand selecting the mismatch predicate before branch comparison avoids\nappending a late prediction XOR to the forwarded-operand comparator.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Implement one compact fetch-time direction predictor on the CURRENT\nregistered-multiplier champion: 64 untagged one-bit last-outcome entries,\nindexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset to not taken. Read the selected bit\ncombinationally from PC. Predecode only legal BRANCH funct3 encodings and\nJAL from raw imem_data. A legal conditional branch predicts taken when\nits selected outcome bit is one; JAL predicts taken unconditionally.\nJALR and all other instructions predict PC+4. Construct the exact B/J\nimmediate and use a dedicated full-width PC-relative target adder in\nparallel with the existing PC+4 increment. Suppress taken prediction\nfor targets whose low two bits are nonzero. There is no BTB, tag array,\nreturn stack, lookahead register, added fetch stage or global history.\n\nCarry only predicted_taken through IF and ID/EX, capturing the actual\naccepted prediction and retaining it throughout backend holds. The\nimmediate direct target is exact for that same instruction, so recovery\nneeds no stored target or 32-bit predicted-next-PC equality test.\nFold the prediction into the branch predicate selection BEFORE the\nforwarded-operand comparison result: compare using branch_op XOR\n{2'b00, predicted_taken}. This exchanges BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU,\nso the selected comparator directly says whether the predicted direction\nwas wrong. Gate conditional recovery by a legal conditional branch and\nan aligned direct target. Keep the original architectural branch outcome\nfor training, traps and RVFI. For jumps, recover when aligned actual\njump direction differs from predicted_taken; JALR stays unpredicted.\n\nSelect the recovery ADDRESS early using the carried prediction bit:\nif predicted_taken is one, recovery goes to PC+4; otherwise it goes to\nthe existing JAL/JALR or branch target. This address is consumed only\nwhen the mismatch predicate fires, making it equivalent to the resolved\nnext PC without a late actual-outcome mux on the 32-bit recovery bus.\nDo not substitute this speculative address for architectural pc_next.\nCorrectly predicted branches and JAL keep the younger fetched target\ninstruction, while wrong predictions kill it. Preserve link writes and\nmisaligned-control-target trap behavior, including JALR bit-zero masking.\n\nTrain the single indexed bit directly to the actual direction exactly\nonce when a valid legal aligned conditional branch advances from EX.\nUse per-entry write enables/local flops, rather than a read-modify-write\ncounter or write-through table bypass. Simultaneous lookup and training\nuse the pre-edge bit. Suppress training and recovery while older dmem\nbackpressure or multiply/divide ownership prevents EX advancement.\nReset initializes the table; invalid bubbles, jumps and excluded\nalignment cases cannot train. Aliasing changes performance only.\n\nPreserve the current separation of payload storage from validity kills.\nRaw imem_data/PC reach decode independently of recovery and readiness;\nprediction has no combinational dependence on hazard/flush outputs.\nAdvance fetch only when accepted, excluding imem stalls, load-use bubbles,\ndmem holds and M-unit waits. Reset takes priority, then advancing EX\nrecovery overrides frontend holds and unavailable imem, otherwise fetch\nholds or follows its accepted prediction. Retain original metadata during\nbackend holds. Keep outstanding memory requests, retained MEM/WB bypass,\nreal and ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder default-illegal discipline, nret=1\nports and strict channel-0 retirement order unchanged.\n\nA private RTL trial of this exact predictor on the current source passed\nVerilator -Wall lint and stalled selftest RVFI cosimulation. Stalled\ncanonical CoreMark completed in bounds with every required CRC and the\nvalidation literal intact. Marker-bracketed cycles were 4,496,136.\nGowin placement options 0/1/2 measured 61.943/63.030/63.030 MHz: median\n63.030 MHz, 3,027 LUT4, 883 registers, eight LUT-RAM cells and two DSPs.\nThese measurements imply fitness 140.187 iter/sec, about 7.96 percent\nabove 129.85 and above the 135.8231 acceptance threshold.\n\nThe trial also tested registered sequential-lookahead prediction and\nan ordinary two-bit table with the same early mismatch predicate. Their\nmeasured fitness was 139.052 and 136.391 respectively. Select only the\none-bit direct-lookup design described above: its modest accuracy loss\ncosts 22,365 cycles versus the two-bit trial but its smaller state and\nhigher Fmax deliver better fitness. This is measured trial evidence,\nnot an accepted implementation. Full formal and directed predictor unit\ncoverage remain required during implementation. Predictor routing and\nrecovery equivalence across alignment/hold cases are the principal risks;\nrequire every unchanged correctness gate plus scored vendor timing and\ncanonical marker-bracketed CoreMark before acceptance.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add the 64-entry hashed one-bit last-outcome table with reset-to-not-taken\nand entry-local writes of advancing EX branch outcomes. Predecode legal\nBRANCH/JAL, form exact aligned B/J targets with a dedicated PC-relative\nadder parallel to PC+4, and publish predicted_taken independently of\nhazard/flush feedback. JALR remains sequential. Retain reset/recovery/\naccepted-fetch priority and hold semantics. Do not add lookahead state.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add only predicted_taken to if_id_t and id_ex_t, immediately before\ninstr to retain existing low instruction/valid packing. Preserve all\narchitectural downstream and RVFI fields.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Latch the actual accepted predicted_taken bit with PC and instruction,\npreserve it during backend holds, and retain payload/valid separation\nand complete reset initialization.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Select conditional mismatch using branch_op XOR the prediction in its\nlow bit, with all six legal comparator cases and aligned-target gating.\nHandle jump mismatch separately. Preselect recovery PC+4 versus resolved\ntarget using predicted_taken, while keeping architectural pc_next and\nlink/trap resolution independent. Export exactly-once legal aligned\nconditional training PC/outcome on normal EX advancement. Suppress\nrecovery/training on dmem and M-unit holds. Preserve forwarding,\nmultiplier/divider ownership, real arithmetic and ALTOPS.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire conditional training from EX to IF and route prediction mismatch\nthrough existing redirect/hazard controls. Preserve all top-level\nnret=1 ports, retirement order and memory/RVFI contracts.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain existing checks and add an independent one-bit table model.\nCover cold not-taken state, outcome changes, index collisions and\nsimultaneous read/write; test all six branch predicates with each\nprediction bit to prove the early mismatch transformation. Check JAL\nlinks, unpredicted JALR, consecutive branches, reserved encodings,\nalignment traps, full-width target carries and reset after training.\nExercise load dependencies, imem-unavailable recovery, prolonged dmem\nholds and multiply/divide ownership. Assert original accepted metadata,\none-shot training, PC+4 false-taken recovery, no wrong-path side effects,\nexact RVFI order and bubble-free warm correctly predicted transfers.\nExisting baseline-specific held-redirect expectations must instead\nassert deferred, exactly-once recovery without dropping architectural\nor memory checks; all invariant checks remain enforced.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88))\nfrom jsonschema import validate\nimport json\nvalidate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
