{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r5s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='One-bit predictor with registered direct recovery address and mismatch predicate'\nd['hypothesis']='''Add one small direction predictor whose recovery metadata is prepared in\nfetch/decode and registered with the instruction. Use 64 untagged one-bit\nlast-outcome entries indexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset to not taken.\nPredecode only legal conditional BRANCH funct3 encodings and JAL from raw\nimem_data. A conditional branch uses its table bit; JAL predicts taken;\nJALR and other encodings predict sequentially. Form exact full-width B/J\nPC-relative targets in parallel with PC+4 and suppress taken prediction\nfor misaligned direct targets. Use entry-local writes and pre-edge lookup,\nwithout bypass, tags, a BTB, global history or an added fetch stage.\n\nCarry only predicted_taken, a 32-bit direct recovery address and a direct-\ntarget-aligned bit through IF and ID/EX. The direct recovery address is\nPC+4 for a taken prediction and the exact direct target otherwise. In ID,\nselect and register the conditional mismatch predicate as branch_op XOR\n{2'b00, predicted_taken}. This swaps BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU. EX's\nforwarded-operand comparator then directly produces direction mismatch,\nwithout a late prediction XOR. Preserve the original branch_op for\narchitectural resolution, traps and training. Generate this metadata from\nraw PC/instruction/prediction, independently of stall/flush/validity\nfeedback. Capture it on the same payload edge as the instruction and hold\nit unchanged throughout backend ownership.\n\nEX redirects an aligned conditional mismatch to the registered recovery\naddress. Correctly predicted branches and aligned JAL retain the younger\ninstruction. Retain the current PC+immediate and PC+4 expressions for\narchitectural RVFI pc_next and link writes: do not add separate registered\ndirect-target or fallthrough-PC payloads. Use the registered direct-target\nalignment bit for B/J trap qualification. Misaligned taken branches and\nJAL retain sequential trap behavior, with link writes suppressed. JALR\nremains unpredicted, using the existing forwarded rs1+immediate, bit-zero\nmasking and dynamic alignment checks; select that resolved indirect\naddress instead of direct recovery metadata for JALR. Keep architectural\nRVFI resolution separate from the preselected recovery address. No wide\npredicted-next-PC equality check or late direct recovery-address mux is\nneeded because the prediction's exact target comes from the accepted\ninstruction itself.\n\nTrain exactly once when a valid legal conditional branch with an aligned\ndirect target advances out of EX, writing its actual outcome into its\nhashed entry. Suppress training and recovery during older dmem\nbackpressure or M-unit ownership. Use normal EX advancement directly\n(in.valid && \"'!stall && !is_divide && !divide_active_q), retaining the\ncurrent M snapshot and completion behavior. Simultaneous lookup and\ntraining use the pre-edge bit. Fetch changes PC only for accepted\ninstructions or advancing recovery: reset first, recovery next even if\nimem is unavailable, then hold or predicted advancement. Kill only the\nyounger validity on a mismatch; preserve raw instruction decode,\npayload/valid separation, current registered forwarding and complete ALU\nchoices, outstanding memory requests and retained MEM/WB forwarding.\n\nThis is one timing-conscious predictor integration, preserving pipeline\ndepth, nret=1 IO, decoder default-illegal discipline, retirement order,\nreal RV32M arithmetic, ALTOPS and every evaluation invariant. All RTL\nchanges are confined to the bench core. Validate warm/cold branches,\nboth mismatch polarities, all legal predicates, target alignment and\ncarries, JAL/JALR links, collisions, reset and simultaneous training,\nincluding load-use and both bus stalls. Require all unchanged gates.\n\nA private RTL trial of the specific recovery-only payload above passed\nVerilator -Wall lint and stalled selftest RVFI cosimulation. Canonical\nstalled CoreMark completed in bounds with every required CRC and the\nvalidation literal, taking 4,496,136 marker-bracketed cycles. Gowin\nplacement options 0/1/2 reached 64.214/67.947/67.947 MHz, median 67.947,\nwith 3,206 logic cells, 916 registers, eight LUT-RAMs, six BSRAMs and two\nDSPs. These measurements imply 151.12 iterations/sec, approximately\n7.37 percent above 140.75 and above the 147.2245 acceptance threshold.\nThe final worst option-0 path remains operand/ALU/memory-address logic,\n20.868 ns across 13 cells. This is trial evidence, not an accepted result;\nfull formal and predictor-specific coverage remain implementation gates.\nAdded state and routing remain the main risks. Reimplementation must\nreproduce the median Fmax and bracketed cycles with unchanged checks.\n'\"'''\nfor c in d['changes']:\n if c['file']=='rtl/core_pkg.sv':c['description']='''Add predicted_taken, a 32-bit direct recovery address and direct-target\nalignment to IF/ID and ID/EX, plus the registered mismatch predicate in\nID/EX. Place new fields before instr so the existing low instruction/valid\npacking stays intact. Do not add separate registered target or PC+4\npayloads. Preserve all downstream architectural and RVFI bundles.\n'''\n if c['file']=='rtl/if_stage.sv':c['description']='''Add the hashed 64-entry one-bit last-outcome table with reset-to-not-taken\nand entry-local writes of advancing EX outcomes. Predecode legal B/J,\ncompute exact aligned target in parallel with PC+4, and publish prediction,\nalignment and the preselected direct recovery address from raw fetch\ninputs. Preserve reset/recovery/accepted-fetch PC priority and independent\nraw decode payload. Simultaneous training and lookup use the pre-edge bit.\n'''\n if c['file']=='rtl/ex_stage.sv':c['description']='''Use the registered mismatch predicate with forwarded operands and the\nregistered direct recovery address for aligned conditional recovery. Keep\noriginal architectural branch outcome and PC expressions for RVFI and\nlinks; use registered B/J alignment for trap qualification. Retain dynamic\nJALR forwarding, target masking and alignment, and select its actual target\nfor recovery. Export exactly-once legal aligned branch training on normal\nEX advancement. Preserve producer eligibility, current complete registered\nALU selections, arithmetic and M snapshots/ownership.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'medium'}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90,default_flow_style=False))\nscore=67.947e6*10/4496136\nprint('Revised hypothesis schema validation passed')\nprint('Trial fitness:',score,'delta percent:',(score/140.75-1)*100)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
