lect and register the conditional mismatch predicate as branch_op XOR\n\n  {2''b00, predicted_taken}. This swaps BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU. EX''s\n\n  forwarded-operand comparator then directly produces direction mismatch,\n\n  without a late prediction XOR. Preserve the original branch_op for\n\n  architectur\n…[4467 of 7539 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:72956f7a7a7fadc4]…\ng stays intact. Do not add separate registered target or PC+4\n\n    payloads. Preserve all downstream architectural and RVFI bundles.\n\n    '\n- file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n  description: 'Compute the validated mismatch predicate before ID/EX capture and\n\n    latch the actual accepted prediction and PC-derived metadata with\n\n    the payload. Hold them through backend ownership. Preserve all\n\n    current decoder controls, operand selection exports and independent\n\n    validity kills; reset initializes the new state.\n\n    '\n- file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n  description: 'Use the registered mismatch predicate with forwarded operands and the\n\n    registered direct recovery address for aligned conditional recovery. Keep\n\n    original architectural branch outcome and PC expressions for RVFI and\n\n    links; use registered B/J alignment for trap qualification. Retain dynamic\n\n    JALR forwarding, target masking and alignment, and select its actual target\n\n    for recovery. Export exactly-once legal aligned branch training on normal\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
