ect\n  target otherwise. In decode register branch_op XOR\n  {2'b00,predicted_taken}, swapping each conditional predicate with its\n  complement. EX uses ONE forwarded-operand comparator network to\n  produce direction_mismatch directly. Reconstruct the actual outcome\n  as directi\n…[4186 of 7258 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bd40e0b1e06ceb2d]…\ntraining to IF and mismatch recovery to the\n      existing hazard control. Preserve the registered wb_result bypass,\n      complete ALU selection timing, top-level IO and channel-0 order.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all architectural assertions and add an independent pre-edge\n      counter model for saturation, hysteresis, collisions and reset.\n      Cover all six predicates, both mismatch polarities, signed/unsigned\n      boundary operands, consecutive warm branches, B/J target carries,\n      reserved encodings, alignment traps and JAL/JALR links. Exercise\n      load-dependent branches, WB producers, M ownership, both bus stalls,\n      simultaneous lookup/training and deferred exactly-once recovery.\n      Check retained metadata and bypass values, strict RVFI order, stable\n      dmem requests, no wrong-path stores and warm taken-branch bubble\n      elimination. Adapt baseline redirect-cycle stimulus to actual\n      mispredictions while preserving its architectural checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
