{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r7s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Static direct prediction with recovery in the B/J immediate register\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current bench champion scores 181.41 iterations/sec at 86.601 MHz\n  and 4,773,836 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent.\n  Earlier adaptive predictors reduced cycles but lost clock speed: r6s2\n  took 4,471,522 cycles at 80.665 MHz. An isolated two-bit predictor trial\n  on the new registered-WB champion reproduced that cycle count but\n  reached only 80.276 MHz. Its table and recovery metadata still cost too\n  much timing. A smaller static predictor removes the table completely\n  and can reuse the otherwise unnecessary B/J immediate operand register\n  for a prepared recovery address, minimizing added state and routing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add ONE compact static fetch predictor to the CURRENT registered-WB\n  bench core. Predict legal backward conditional branches taken and\n  forward conditional branches not taken, using the B-immediate sign bit.\n  Predict aligned JAL taken; leave JALR unpredicted. Predecode raw\n  imem_data, positively validate conditional funct3, build exact signed\n  B/J immediates and full-width PC-relative targets in parallel with PC+4,\n  and suppress taken predictions for misaligned targets. There is no\n  adaptive table, BTB, return stack, training network or pipeline stage.\n  Prediction computation is independent of hazard/flush/bus-ready\n  feedback; readiness and hazards govern instruction acceptance only.\n\n  Publish predicted_taken, direct-target alignment and a prepared direct\n  recovery address with IF's combinational payload. Recovery is PC+4\n  after a taken prediction and the direct target otherwise. For validated\n  B/J instructions, ID stores this recovery address IN THE EXISTING\n  id_ex_t.imm field, replacing an immediate unused by their integer\n  datapath. Ordinary integer instructions, AUIPC, loads, stores and JALR\n  keep the original immediate exactly. Add no 32-bit ID/EX recovery bank.\n  Retain original instruction bits and recon\n…[4906 of 7978 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c6b1d27783726a04]…\natch recovery through existing hazard wiring\n      without changing IO, retirement, complete ALU selections or the\n      registered WB bypass. Keep all changes scoped to the bench core.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve architectural and invariant assertions; add an independent\n      static prediction model checked on each cycle. Cover all six\n      predicates, both mismatch polarities, forward/backward/zero targets,\n      signed and unsigned boundary operands, consecutive branches,\n      aligned JAL, JALR links, target carries, misalignment and reserved\n      encodings. Exercise both bus stalls, load-use, M ownership, retained\n      WB results, reset and deferred exactly-once recovery. Verify B/J\n      recovery storage cannot alter ordinary immediate operations,\n      architectural PCs, strict RVFI order or memory effects. Adapt\n      baseline redirect stimulus to actual mispredictions while retaining\n      invalid-payload capture, stable requests and wrong-path-store checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
