{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"Registered recovery passed all 53 formal checks and stalled cosim, but its 81.429 MHz Fmax still missed acceptance. I’ll submit a compact 32-entry version of that design as the final hypothesis, with low confidence. It halves the counter storage; its fitness gain remains unmeasured.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Compact 32-entry direction predictor with registered recovery'\nd['motivation'] += '\\\\nA 64-entry registered-recovery trial passed correctness gates and\\\\nimproved recovery-path isolation, but scored only 179.87 iterations/sec\\\\nat 81.429 MHz. Its new worst path is integer EX/ALU/data-memory rather\\\\nthan frontend recovery. Halving direction state and lookup fanout is\\\\nthe remaining concrete predictor refinement to limit routing overhead.\\\\n'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('one 64-entry bimodal','one 32-entry bimodal').replace('PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]','PC[6:2] XOR PC[12:8]').replace('an eight-by-eight grouped lookup','a four-by-eight grouped lookup')\na=d['hypothesis'].index('An isolated trial passed full RVFI')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'][:a]+'''The isolated 64-entry registered-recovery precursor passed warning-free\nVerilator build, all 53 unchanged nret=1 ALTOPS formal checks, and full\nRVFI trace cosimulation for selftest and all three random programs,\neach with no stalls and both bus stalls. Canonical stalled CoreMark\ncompleted in bounds with every required CRC and validation literal,\ntaking 4,527,071 marker-bracketed cycles. Gowin options 0/1/2 reached\n79.755/81.429/81.429 MHz; median 81.429 MHz implies only 179.87\niterations/sec, below the champion and therefore NOT an acceptable\nmeasured candidate. Its 4,662 logic cells and 1,889 registers include\n128 counter flops; the proposed 32-entry version removes 64 of those\nflops, halves local training enables, removes half the grouped lookup\nand narrows the hash to five bits. Keep all recovery and speculative\nsquash semantics proven by that precursor.\n\nThis final 32-entry variant has not been timed or cycle-measured.\nExpect roughly five percent fitness improvement if reduced predictor\nrouting permits about 87-89 MHz with a modest aliasing penalty. This is\na low-confidence architectural projection, not a measured gain: the\nprecursor's ALU critical path may remain limiting despite reduced table\nsize. More aliases can also increase misses, and every miss now costs\nan extra registered-recovery cycle. Measure the actual bracketed cycles\nand median Gowin Fmax; accept only above 189.75486 iterations/sec.\nFor example, 4.55 million cycles require more than 86.338 MHz. Require\nall unchanged gates and explicit speculative-squash coverage on the\n32-entry implementation. No evaluation or arithmetic changes are part\nof this hypothesis.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']=d['changes'][0]['description'].replace('64 locally','32 locally').replace('grouped MSB','four-by-eight grouped MSB')\nd['changes'][0]['description'] += 'Use the five-bit PC[6:2] XOR PC[12:8] hash for lookup and training.\\\\n'\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef str_representer(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,str_representer)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261004-003-r7s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert all(c['file'].startswith(('rtl/','test/test_')) for c in d['changes'])\nprint('Final hypothesis written and schema-valid:',p)\nprint('Category:',d['category'],'Expected impact:',d['expected_impact'])\nPY\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
