{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Direction predictor reuses registered EX lanes for recovery'\nd['motivation']='''The current champion scores 205.00 iter/sec at 97.865 MHz and takes\n4,773,836 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. No LESSONS.md exists.\nPrevious predictors reduced cycles but lost timing: R6s2's live recovery\ncrossed WB/EX/IF/ID; R7s2's registered recovery left EX arithmetic on the\ncritical path. The new parent separates arithmetic and memory request\npayloads. A predictor can reuse those already timed registers for\nrecovery, retaining registered feedback without a separate target bank.\nA private trial of this particular integration reaches 227.15 iter/sec,\nabout 10.8 percent above the champion and above the 214.43 threshold.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Add one 64-entry direction-only predictor with registered recovery\nand registered training, using the existing EX/MEM execution lanes\nfor the recovery address. Use untagged two-bit saturating counters\nindexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset weakly not taken. Implement\nentry-local constant-index updates and an eight-by-eight grouped MSB\nlookup; simultaneous lookup and training observe pre-edge state.\nPredecode only legal BRANCH funct3 values and JAL from raw imem_data.\nPredict aligned JAL taken, conditional direction from the table, and\nJALR sequentially. Form exact full-width B/J targets in parallel with\nPC+4 and suppress taken prediction for misaligned direct targets.\nNo BTB, tags, return stack, cache, global history or extra instruction\nstage. Prediction is independent of hazard, flush and ready feedback.\n\nCarry predicted_taken and direct alignment with IF/ID and ID/EX.\nPrepare the direct recovery address in IF: PC+4 for a taken prediction,\ndirect target otherwise. Reuse ID/EX imm for this address ONLY on\nvalidated B/J instructions. Preserve original immediates for arithmetic,\nAUIPC, memory and JALR. Reconstruct original B/J immediates from the\nretained instruction bits in EX for architectural targets and RVFI.\nRegister branch_op XOR {2'b00,predicted_taken} as the mismatch predicate.\nOne forwarded-operand comparator gives direction mismatch; reconstruct\nactual outcome as mismatch XOR predicted_taken. Preserve original\nbranch_op, architectural operand snapshots and all trap semantics.\n\nFor a validated conditional branch, select the existing ALU_LUI operation\nand immediate B operand internally at ID/EX capture. Export the same\nbranch immediate selection to the registered complete ALU choices.\nThis passes its prepared recovery address through the EXISTING integer\nALU and arithmetic_result_q register. A branch has no architectural rd\nwrite, so this payload is available for predictor recovery without any\narchitectural result change. Decoder legality and branch predicates\nremain intact; standalone decoder outputs need no modification. For\nJALR, the existing independent effective_addr_q already captures the\nforwarded rs1 plus its original immediate. Its registered value with\nbit zero cleared is the actual recovery target. JALR's arithmetic lane\nstill contains PC+4 for its link write. Avoid adding a recovery mux after\nthe ALU or changing the actual memory-address/store-data capture path.\n\nRegister ONLY recovery_valid at the edge that advances the resolving\ninstruction into EX/MEM; do not add a separate 32-bit recovery-target\nregister. On the following pending cycle, select redirect_target from\narithmetic_result_q for a conditional branch, or the bit-zero-masked\neffective_addr_q for JALR, using the resolving registered control tag.\nConditional recovery is an aligned mismatch; aligned JALR always recovers.\nCorrect predictions need no recovery. Capture events only for valid\nnormal EX advancement, excluding older dmem holds, M ownership and\npending recovery. The resolving branch/JALR is non-memory and therefore\nits EX/MEM entry cannot itself cause a dmem hold on the recovery cycle.\nConsume the pre-edge registered recovery payload before ordinary lane\ncapture updates it. Reset has highest PC priority, pending recovery\noverrides imem unavailability next, otherwise hold or accept prediction.\n\nDuring pending recovery the younger ID/EX instruction is speculative:\nsuppress its EX/MEM valid, reg_write, mem_read and mem_write, upcoming\nforwarding eligibility, M launch AND wait ownership, and secondary\nrecovery. Let the older resolving instruction retire normally. Flush\nthe subsequently fetched instruction and consume recovery exactly once.\nKeep independent effective-address, store-data and arithmetic-result\nregister capture unchanged on every edge without an older dmem hold;\nonly authoritative validity and side-effect controls squash speculation.\nThe saved-M completion mux remains confined to metadata and arithmetic.\n\nTrain from the REGISTERED resolving EX/MEM branch's retained PC, actual\nbranch_taken, validated is_branch and aligned original branch target.\nUpdate only when that valid legal conditional instruction leaves MEM.\nTraining happens once even when younger M ownership or pending recovery\nis present: neither may suppress the older resolving branch's update.\nSquashed younger entries never train. Explicitly qualify MEM advancement.\nThis places a register boundary between the live branch comparator and\nall entry-local predictor write enables and data inputs.\n\nPreserve real/ALTOPS M arithmetic and latency, exclusive ownership,\nsnapshots, stable outstanding requests, retained complete WB forwarding,\nyoungest-writer priority, registered complete ALU choices, payload/valid\nseparation, exact branch/jump/memory alignment traps, sequential trapped\npc_next and suppressed jump links on faults. Keep writing-producer\neligibility independent of non-writing conditional comparisons. RVFI\npc_next is architectural. Preserve decoder default-illegal discipline,\nnret=1 IO, strictly consecutive channel-0 retirement and every fixed gate.\n\nAn isolated trial of this exact design passed warning-free Verilator\nlint. Canonical stalled CoreMark completed in bounds with all required\nCRCs, the validation literal and markers: 4,527,071 bracketed cycles,\n10 iterations. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 reached\n98.318/102.833/102.833 MHz; median 102.833 MHz gives 227.15 iter/sec,\na 10.8 percent gain. Option 0 uses 4,656 logic cells, 1,897 registers,\nzero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its worst path is PC through IF\ninto ID's recovery immediate, 15.465 ns across 13 cells. The separate\nrecovery-bank precursor reached only 90.959 MHz and 200.92 iter/sec,\nso reusing the existing execution lanes is essential to this proposal.\nThis is trial evidence, not an accepted implementation. Reproduce the\nscore and pass all unchanged gates plus independent counter/training\nand speculative-squash coverage. At this measured cycle count, acceptance\nrequires more than 97.074 MHz and fitness above 214.43 iter/sec. Fetch\nadder/lookup routing and correct pre-edge recovery ownership remain the\nmain risks. No arithmetic algorithm or evaluation changes are proposed.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':11,'confidence':'high'}\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Capture prediction, alignment and complemented mismatch predicate.\nUse prepared recovery in imm only for validated B/J. For conditional\nbranches only, select existing ALU_LUI and immediate operand internally,\nincluding incoming_alu_src for registered ALU choices, so the existing\narithmetic lane carries recovery. Preserve original architectural\ncontrols, operand snapshots, decoder legality, holds and validity kills.\n'''\nd['changes'][3]['description']='''Use one mismatch comparator and reconstruct architectural outcome.\nRegister only the advancing recovery-valid bit. Recover through the\nresolving branch's existing arithmetic_result_q or JALR's existing\nbit-zero-masked effective_addr_q, selected by registered control; do\nnot add a recovery-target bank or a new post-ALU payload mux. Suppress\nspeculative younger validity/side effects, M launch and wait ownership,\nsecondary events and forwarding eligibility during pending recovery.\nKeep independent request/arithmetic capture and saved-M topology intact.\nReconstruct exact direct architectural targets and preserve all traps.\n'''\nclass Literal(str):pass\ndef lit(dumper,data):return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|')\nyaml.SafeDumper.add_representer(Literal,lit)\nfor k in ['motivation','hypothesis']:d[k]=Literal(d[k])\nfor change in d['changes']:change['description']=Literal(change['description'])\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Updated hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
