advancement, excluding older dmem holds, M ownership and\npending recovery. The resolving branch/JALR is non-memory and therefore\nits EX/MEM entry cannot itself cause a dmem hold on the recovery cycle.\nConsume the pre-edge registered recovery payload before ordinary lane\ncapture updates it. Reset has highest PC priority, pending recovery\noverrides imem unavailability next, otherwise hold or accept prediction.\n\nDuring pending recovery the younger ID/EX instruction is speculative:\nsuppress its EX/MEM valid, reg_write, mem_read and mem_write, upcoming\nforwarding eligibility, M launch AND wait ownership, and secondary\nrecovery. Let the older resolving instruction retire normally. Flush\nthe subsequently fetched instruction and consume recovery exactly once.\nKeep independent effective-address, store-data and arithmetic-result\nregister capture unchanged on every edge without an older dmem hold;\nonly authoritative validity and side-effect controls squash speculation.\nThe saved-M completion mux remains confined to metadata and arithmetic.\n\nTrain from the REGISTERED resolving EX/MEM branch's retained PC, actual\nbranch_taken, validated is_branch and aligned original branch target.\nUpdate only when that valid legal conditional instruction leaves MEM.\nTraining happens once even when younger M ownership or pending recovery\nis present: neither may suppress the older resolving branch's update.\nSquashed younger entries never train. Explicitly qualify MEM advancement.\nThis places a register boundary between the live branch comparator and\nall entry-local predictor write enables and data inputs.\n\nPreserve real/ALTOPS M arithmetic and latency, exclusive ownership,\nsnapshots, stable outstanding requests, retained complete WB forwarding,\nyoungest-writer priority, registered complete ALU choices, payload/valid\nseparation, exact branch/jump/memory alignment traps, sequential trapped\npc_next and suppressed jump links on faults. Keep writing-producer\neligibility independent of non-writing conditional comparisons. RVFI\npc_next is architectural. Preserve decoder default-illegal discipline,\nnret=1 IO, strictly consecutive channel-0 retirement and every fixed gate.\n\nAn isolated trial of this exact design passed warning-free Verilator\nlint. Canonical stalled CoreMark completed in bounds with all required\nCRCs, the validation literal and markers: 4,527,071 bracketed cycles,\n10 iterations. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 reached\n98.318/102.833/102.833 MHz; median 102.833 MHz gives 227.15 iter/sec,\na 10.8 percent gain. Option 0 uses 4,656 logic cells, 1,897 registers,\nzero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. Its worst path is PC through IF\ninto ID's recovery immediate, 15.465 ns across 13 cells. The separate\nrecovery-bank precursor reached only 90.959 MHz and 200.92 iter/sec,\nso reusing the existing execution lanes is essential to this proposal.\nThis is trial evidence, not an accepted implementation. Reproduce the\nscore and pass all unchanged gates plus independent counter/training\nand speculative-squash coverage. At this measured cycle count, acceptance\nrequires more than 97.074 MHz and fitness above 214.43 iter/sec. Fetch\nadder/lookup routing and correct pre-edge recovery ownership remain the\nmain risks. No arithmetic algorithm or evaluation changes are proposed.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':11,'confidence':'high'}\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Capture prediction, alignment and complemented mismatch predicate.\nUse prepared recovery in imm only for validated B/J. For conditional\nbranches only, select existing ALU_LUI and immediate operand internally,\nincluding incoming_alu_src for registered ALU choices, so the existing\narithmetic lane carries recovery. Preserve original architectural\ncontrols, operand snapshots, decoder legality, holds and validity kills.\n'''\nd['changes'][3]['description']='''Use one mismatch comparator and reconstruct architectural outcome.\nRegister only the advanc