{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id']=='hyp-20261004-003-r11s2':\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace only the direction-table storage and update network with four\n16-entry banks of two-bit counters inferred as asynchronous-read,\nsynchronous-write distributed LUT RAM. Preserve exactly the current\n64-entry hash PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], two-bit saturating update semantics,\nweakly-not-taken initialization and pre-edge lookup behavior. Index[5:4]\nselects a bank and index[3:0] its word. Keep this direction-only: no tags,\nstored targets, global history, indirect prediction or added fetch stage.\n\nProvide independent fetch and training read addresses. Describe each\nbank as two identical resetless 16x2 memories with common write address,\ndata and enable: one asynchronous copy reads fetch index and the other\nreads training index. Four shallow bank selectors yield the fetch MSB\nand old two-bit training counter. Compute the saturating next state once\nfrom the old training counter, then write only the selected bank and\nboth of its copies on the existing one-shot train_valid. There is no\nwrite-through bypass; simultaneous lookup and training use old state.\nUse portable synthesizable memory RTL and the vendor's supported\ndistributed-memory inference attributes. Do not introduce unmodeled\nvendor black boxes into formal. Confirm actual LUT-RAM inference in\nGowin area reports; a flop fallback would defeat this hypothesis.\n\nDo not reset the memory arrays. Instead reset one initialized bit and\na four-bit scrub address. During the first 16 non-reset clocks, write\n2'b01 to the same scrub word in ALL four banks and both copies. Scrub\nhas priority over training, which is ignored until initialization ends.\nSet initialized only after the address-15 write has completed. During\nscrubbing force conditional direction to not taken independently of\nunknown RAM contents; aligned JAL remains predicted taken. The CPU must\ncontinue normal execution and recovery during these 16 clocks: scrubbing\nnever stalls fetch or the backend. A repeated reset restarts the scrub\nand immediately disables RAM-derived conditional predictions. Reset-time\nand pre-initialization lookup must never expose unknown target control.\n\nRetain the current legal B/J predecode, exact full-width target arithmetic,\nalignment gating, unpredicted JALR, accepted predicted_taken metadata,\ncomplemented mismatch predicate, prepared alternate recovery operand,\nregistered recovery and existing execution-lane reuse. Training still\ncomes only from valid legal aligned branches when EX/MEM advances; held\nentries do not train repeatedly. Lookup remains independent of ready,\nflush and hazard feedback. Keep accepted-fetch and reset/recovery PC\npriorities, payload holds, load-use bubbles, retained WB forwarding,\nstable memory requests, wrong-path suppression, all legality/alignment\nchecks, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, nret=1 IO and consecutive RVFI order.\nArchitectural next PCs and traps always use actual resolution.\n\nThis is one predictor storage architecture change. Its intended benefit\nis replacing the counter-flop/reset/write-enable fabric with tiny LUT\nmemories and shallow bank selection. After scrub, the predictor has the\nsame capacity and hysteresis; boot training discarded during scrub can\naffect initial state, so do not assume an identical benchmark cycle count.\nExpect eight percent fitness improvement, with low confidence: this RAM\ncandidate has not been timed, the current worst paths cross EX/bypass,\nand asynchronous RAM delay or training read-modify-write can erase gains.\nRequire unchanged formal and cosim gates, canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs\nand validation text, bounded accesses, marker-bracketed timing and scored\nmedian Gowin fitness strictly above 249.30364 iterations/sec.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
