{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_79", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Decoded coarse shifter with two native fine-shift stages',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 238.34 iterations/sec at 107.897 MHz with\n4,527,071 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent.\nReviewed micro_opt history includes the successful r9 registered\nresult grants and unsuccessful recent alignment, forwarding and\nresult-case rewrites. A reproduced unchanged-core Gowin placement-0\nrun reaches 102.509 MHz. Its near-critical paths include registered\nALU operand selection through the barrel shifters. Moving IF target\nselection or rewriting operand muxes did not improve private trials.\nThe remaining opportunity is reducing serial shifter data-mux depth\nwhile preserving the proven registered grants and existing pipeline.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Change only the PREDECODED_RESULT shifters in alu.sv. Replace each\nfive-level binary barrel with an eight-way decoded constant coarse\nshift followed by the two native fine-shift stages. Decode b[4:2]\ninto eight mutually exclusive choices k=0..7. For each direction form\nconstant shifts by 4*k, mask each term with its distance choice AND\nthat direction's existing registered result grant, and combine the\neight terms using an explicit balanced OR. Then shift that selected\nword by b[1:0], using native left, logical-right or signed-right\noperators as appropriate. Keep directions separate; do not reverse\nbits or share a new direction-controlled barrel.\n\nFor SLL coarse term k is (a << (4*k)) masked by choice[k] and\ngrant[7]. SRL uses (a >> (4*k)) with grant[8]. SRA uses the unsigned\nbit pattern of signed a shifted arithmetically by 4*k, masked by\nchoice[k] and grant[9]. Cast the combined SRA word to signed BEFORE\nthe final arithmetic shift by b[1:0], then cast its result unsigned.\nEach unselected direction must be exactly zero, including for a\nnegative input, so no sign-fill can leak into the result OR. All\nfive shift-amount bits retain their RV32I meanings; ignore b[31:5]\nexactly as before. A shift amount of zero must return a, and 31 must\nretain exact logical-zero or arithmetic-sign behavior.\n\nThe three upper-distance bits plus an operation grant fit a LUT4\nfor each coarse-choice grant. Eight masked data terms can map to a\nbalanced two-level data selector; the two remaining binary stages\nthen produce four serial data-selection levels instead of five.\nThe larger constant shifts also expose zero and repeated sign bits\nfor pruning. This is one local combinational shifter mapping change,\nwith no new pipeline boundary, instruction latency, source encoding,\npredictor, memory optimization or custom carry chain. Keep all\nnon-shift integer/link/M result terms and their existing OR topology,\nencoded standalone ALU behavior, all ALTOPS formulas, actual M units,\nregister enables, operand forwarding and retained WB values intact.\nPreserve default-illegal decoding, every trap, bus-handshake behavior,\nexact nret=1 top-level ports and consecutive architectural RVFI.\n\nA scratch implementation of this precise coarse-first arrangement\npasses Yosys combinational equivalence against the original\nPREDECODED_RESULT ALU under ALTOPS: all 34 equivalence cells are\nproved, including every output bit, with arbitrary operands,\noperations and result grants. The real M arithmetic is unchanged;\nthis arithmetic-substituted equivalence is not a replacement for\nthe fixed real-arithmetic and architectural correctness gates.\nVendor timing is pending. Predict six percent fitness gain with low\nconfidence: decoded-grant fanout, added LUTs, synthesis refactoring\nand nearly tied RF/IF/forwarding paths can erase the data-depth gain.\nRequire actual scored median Gowin timing, not the depth estimate.\nAt unchanged cycles acceptance requires fitness strictly above\n249.30364 iter/sec and median Fmax above about 112.862 MHz. Require\nall unchanged unit/formal/full-RVFI cosim gates, every canonical\nstalled CoreMark CRC, validation literal, bounded accesses and the\noriginal start/stop timing markers.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Replace only the three PREDECODED_RESULT variable shifts with\nseparate eight-way coarse constant-shift selectors for 0/4/8/12/\n16/20/24/28 bits and native fine shifts by b[1:0]. Integrate each\nexisting operation grant into the coarse-choice masks and use\nbalanced reductions. Preserve signed SRA at both shifts, zero\nunselected contributions, all other ALU expressions and services.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain every existing arithmetic and handshake assertion. Extend\npredecoded-mode coverage with independent Python shift references\nfor all 32 distances, all five-bit masking aliases, signed extrema,\nnegative SRA inputs, random operands, every individual result grant,\nzero grants and other selected operations with unused negative\nshift operands. Include coarse/fine boundaries 3/4, 7/8, 15/16,\n27/28 and 30/31. Keep M ownership/completion and ALTOPS checks.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Updated hypothesis validates:',p)\nfor n in ['onehot_barrel','hybrid_barrel','coarse_onehot_barrel']:\n p=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypgen_r14')/n/'gowin_p0/gw.log'\n print(n,'\\\\n'.join(p.read_text(errors='replace').splitlines()[-2:]) if p.exists() else 'pending')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
