{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_82", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,json,yaml,jsonschema\nbase=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypgen_r14')\nsrc=base/'hybrid_barrel/rtl';dst=base/'fine_sll_only/rtl'\nshutil.copytree(src,dst,dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=dst/'alu.sv';s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('''        | (fine_right >> {shamt[4:3], 3'b000})\n        | \"'$unsigned($signed(fine_arithmetic) >>> {shamt[4:3], 3'\"'b000});''','''        | ((a & {32{result_grants[8]}}) >> shamt)\n        | \"'$unsigned($signed(a & {32{result_grants[9]}}) >>> shamt);'\"''')\n# Unused right networks are eliminated in synthesis; remove them explicitly.\ns=s.replace('    wire [31:0] fine_right_terms [0:7];\\\\n','').replace('    wire [31:0] fine_arithmetic_terms [0:7];\\\\n','')\ns=s.replace('wire [31:0] fine_left, fine_right, fine_arithmetic;','wire [31:0] fine_left;')\ns=s.replace('      assign fine_right_terms[k] = (a >> k) & {32{selected && result_grants[8]}};\\\\n','').replace('      assign fine_arithmetic_terms[k] = \"'$unsigned($signed(a) >>> k) & {32{selected && result_grants[9]}};'\"\\\\n','')\nfor prefix in ['fine_right','fine_arithmetic']:\n start=s.index('    assign '+prefix+' =')\n end=s.index(';',start)+1\n s=s[:start]+s[end:]\np.write_text(s)\npath=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\nh['title']='Eight-way fine SLL selection with native coarse stages'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 238.34 iter/sec at 107.897 MHz and 4,527,071\nmarker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Reviewed\nmicro_opt history shows the r9 registered grants and early shift masks\nimproved fitness; recent alignment, eligibility and result-case\nrewrites regressed. An unchanged-core private Gowin placement-0 run\nreproduces 102.509 MHz with nearly tied EX, forwarding, RF and IF paths.\nA selective SLL mapping can shorten one serial data path with less\nrouting cost than replacing all three shifters.'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Change only the PREDECODED_RESULT SLL contribution. Replace its\nfive-level binary left barrel with an eight-way decoded fine shift\nfollowed by the two existing native coarse shifts. For k=0..7 form\nterm[k] = (a << k) AND a 32-bit mask of\n(result_grants[7] AND (b[2:0] == k)). Constant shifts are wires and\nzero fill. Combine the eight terms with an explicit balanced OR,\nthen left-shift that word by {b[4:3],3'b000}. The decoder uses exactly\nthree distance bits plus the registered SLL grant, fitting a LUT4;\na balanced eight-term masked selector can use two data LUT levels.\nKeeping the native 8/16-bit stages gives four data-selection levels\ninstead of the original five, subject to actual vendor mapping.\n\nRetain the original separate SRL and SRA expressions, including their\nearly input masks and signed cast. This targets SLL only, limiting\nextra LUTs and routing rather than expanding every shift network.\nPreserve the complete existing ALU result OR and every ADD/SUB,\nBoolean, comparison, LUI, link and owned-M contribution. Preserve\nstandalone encoded ALU behavior, real M units, ALTOPS formulas,\nregistered result grants, operand selection and every capture/hold\nenable. Do not add a pipeline register, an immediate-only fast path,\nbit reversal, a shared direction mux or any new architectural state.\nAll five shift bits retain their meaning; b[31:5] is ignored. A zero\nSLL grant must yield zero for every a, and shifts by 0 and 31 must be\nexact. Preserve full RV32IM results, decoder default-illegal behavior,\ntraps, bus handshakes, retained forwarding, nret=1 ports and ordered\nRVFI retirement. Architectural cycle count should be unchanged.\n\nA private precursor applying decoded fine shifts to all three\noperations passes ALTOPS combinational equivalence against the\noriginal ALU: all 34 cells, including all 32 result bits, are proved\nfor arbitrary operands, operations and grants. Its placement-0\nFmax is 100.576 MHz with 4,639 logic cells versus 4,462 for the\nunchanged core. That precursor does not demonstrate a gain. A\ncoarse-first decoded variant measures only 92.102 MHz and a full\n32-distance expansion only 78.069 MHz; neither is proposed. The\nfinal SLL-only design limits expansion to the left-shift network\nand has not yet completed scored timing. Equivalence and unchanged\narithmetic do not establish a frequency improvement. Predict six\npercent fitness gain with low confidence; grant/data fanout,\nrefactoring and nearly tied unaffected paths are material risks.\n\nRequire actual median Gowin Fmax across all scored placements and\nall unchanged correctness gates. Acceptance requires fitness strictly\nabove 249.30364 iter/sec, or approximately 112.862 MHz at the original\n4,527,071 cycles. Require all unit/formal/full-RVFI cosim checks,\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRCs, validation text, bounded accesses\nand the original start/stop markers. Do not weaken checks or claim\nprivate precursor timing as evidence of an accepted improvement.'''\nh['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Replace only PREDECODED_RESULT SLL with eight separately masked\nconstant shifts by 0..7, a balanced OR and native shifts by 8/16\nfrom b[4:3]. Keep original SRL/SRA input masks, all other result\nterms, default encoded behavior, ALTOPS and real M services.'''},{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all existing assertions. Add independent predecoded SLL\nreferences for all 32 distances, high-bit shift-amount aliases,\nrandom operands, extrema and 3/4, 7/8, 15/16, 23/24 and 30/31\nboundaries. Check zero SLL grants while each other operation is\nselected, negative unused shift operands, unchanged SRL/SRA and\ninteger/link/M selection behavior in real and ALTOPS builds.'''}]\npath.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final SLL-only hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
