{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r15s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Shorten fetch target addition with exact signed-offset upper correction\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches 107.897 MHz with 4,527,071 bracketed CoreMark\n  cycles. Recent ALU selector, custom shifter and forwarding-eligibility\n  trials lost vendor frequency. IF PC-to-ID recovery-address paths are\n  also near critical: r12s0 and r14s0 end at ID/EX immediate capture.\n  Fetch currently selects a sign-extended B/J immediate before a full\n  32-bit PC addition, then selects the predicted or alternate path.\n  RV32I direct offsets have only 13 or 21 meaningful bits. Specializing\n  this arithmetic can shorten carry propagation without changing any\n  prediction, accepted instruction or architectural cycle schedule.\n  LESSONS.md is absent; micro_opt history and relevant predictor target\n  arithmetic notes were reviewed. This does not repeat the unsuccessful\n  EX carry-select, shared-shifter or forwarding-control proposals.\nhypothesis: |\n  Change only IF's direct PC-relative target arithmetic. Compute exact\n  branch and JAL targets in parallel, selecting the complete targets\n  with the existing validated raw pre_jal predicate. For each offset\n  width W (13 for B and 21 for J), form a W+1-bit unsigned low sum from\n  explicitly zero-extended pc[W-1:0] and the original encoded offset's\n  low W bits. Retain both the W result bits and its carry C. Independently\n  prepare H=pc[31:W], H+1 and H-1 at the exact 32-W bit width. Let S be\n  the offset sign bit. The target upper portion is H when C equals S,\n  H+1 when C=1,S=0, and H-1 when C=0,S=1. Concatenate that selected upper\n  portion with the low sum. All operations wrap modulo 2^32. This is the\n  identity PC+sign_extend(offset), including negative displacements,\n  sign boundaries and carry across bit 13 or 21; it must not truncate\n  the PC or assume a workload address range. Upper increment/decrement\n  candidates are computed before low-carry selection, so the low carry\n  selects prepared data rather than entering another c\n…[1742 of 4814 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e4899b54c50f2eed]…\nvement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the selected sign-extended 32-bit direct-target addition\n      with parallel exact B13 and J21 low additions and independently\n      prepared upper same/increment/decrement candidates, selecting the\n      upper candidate by carry/sign and the final target by pre_jal.\n      Preserve all predictor state, raw payloads, alignment, sequential\n      and alternate PC selection, and existing capture/hold priorities.\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every independent predictor, predecode, target and priority\n      assertion. Add target arithmetic cases across bit-13 and bit-21\n      carries/borrows, offset extrema, negative displacements, full-PC\n      wraparound and unaligned standalone redirect PCs. Compare exact\n      direct_target, alignment and alternate PC against unrestricted\n      modulo-32-bit reference addition under both predictions and holds.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
