orwarding and the combinational ALU, and median Fmax\\nis only 5.442 MHz. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately with / and %, exposing a large, deeply cascaded\\narithmetic network to Gowin synthesis. Shortening this network can\\nimprove every CoreMark cycle even when that cycle does not divide.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 40, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the four real / and % operation expressions with a single\\nexplicitly unrolled radix-4 quotient/remainder network, using\\nexact divisor multiples, width-bounded borrow-driven subtracts,\\nsigned magnitude conversion, and\n…[115309 of 118381 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:939ee6cb42d3f871]…\nve that dependency while compulsory recovery\\nsafely replays the rare fault case. LESSONS.md is absent; relevant\\npredictor and alignment-related log.jsonl history was reviewed.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Add one focused prediction policy: assume a validated JALR is aligned\\nonly when selecting the next consumer's bypass, and reconcile this\\nprediction through compulsory registered recovery. Preserve the existing\\ndirection predictor and direct JAL prediction exactly. Add no target\\ntable, return stack, fetch stage, queue or JALR validation cycle.\\n\\nCompute upcoming normal writer eligibility from captured validated\\nin.ctrl.reg_write and normal valid ownership, excluding a misaligned\\ndirect JAL with the already registered direct_aligned bit. For JALR,\\nignore live target alignment ONLY in this speculative next_reg_write\\nexpression. Still exclude invalid instructions, pending recovery,\\nolder dmem holds and M launch/busy; keep the saved-M completion producer\\npath unchanged. The forward unit retains its x0 exclusi\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
