{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor d in rows:\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-002-r7s1','hyp-20261004-002-r10s1','hyp-20261004-002-r11s1','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-002-r13s1']:\n  print('\\\\n', d['id'], d['title'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261004-002-r7s1 Partition EX into independently registered memory and arithmetic result lanes\nPartition the existing EX/MEM boundary by destination resource, retaining pipeline depth, single issue and nret=1. Create a dedicated registered effective address from the actual forwarded architectural rs1 plus immediate. MEM uses this register exclusively for the external address, alignment, subword extraction, byte masks and aligned RVFI memory address. The arithmetic/link result remains the early register-result bypass source and WB source for nonloads.\n\nThe memory request address and raw store-data registers capture on every edge without an outstanding older dmem hold, independently of M launch, busy, result-valid, saved M metadata and whole-bundle bubble insertion. Store data captures actual forwarded rs2. An inert instruction may change these payloads but must never issue a request. During an outstanding memory hold retain the complete address, data, width and request strobes. Completed M instructions must not substitute their saved arithmetic result or snapshot into the request-payload registers. This independent capture is essential: merely adding an address field inside the existing zero/snapshot/normal mux did not improve the current champion.\n\nComplete the resource partition by giving the clocked M service a separate result path into the saved M instruction's EX/MEM arithmetic result. Normal integer and link results never select registered multiply/divide data through the encoded integer ALU result case. Register validated multiply/divide class bits with ID/EX; use them for dispatch and wait control. Keep operation subtype for real arithmetic and ALTOPS. On acceptance remember the selected unit. With one outstanding operation, completion comes from the exclusive units' combined result-valid, qualified by EX's registered active ownership, and result data is selected by saved unit ownership. Result consumption uses this owner, not a live opcode. A compatibility parameter may retain the existing standalo\n…[21909 of 24981 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a77fb7478d98b5d7]…\norts and consecutive channel-0 retirement. Change\nonly internal test assumptions equating buffered decode with live fetch\nPC/data; retain every architectural assertion and fixed gate.\n\nThis final topology has not been implemented, timed or verified. Prior\nqueue correctness supports its transfer protocol, not a measured gain\nfor this proposal. Expected benefit is roughly the earlier fall-through\ncycle reduction with local write controls and less storage/read cost\nthan the three-slot registered design. At 4,190,068 cycles, acceptance\nabove 249.30364 iter/sec requires median Gowin Fmax above 104.459 MHz;\nfull-credit deferral may increase cycles and raise that requirement.\nMeasure actual bracketed cycles and all three placement options. Remaining\nALU paths, the decode OR, source-grant updates and forfeited full-pop fetches\nmay erase the gain; confidence is low. Require unchanged formal and\ncomplete-RVFI cosim gates, canonical stalled 2K CoreMark CRCs, validation\nliteral, bounded accesses and marker-only timing.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
