{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat tools/eval/formal.py; tail -3 cores/bench/generated/mul_trial/cosim_build2.log; tail -4 cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Runs the real riscv-formal suite via formal/run_all.sh.\n\nThe real suite is generated at runtime by formal/run_all.sh (which invokes\ngenchecks.py against our rtl/*.sv + wrapper.sv + checks.cfg) and runs the\n~45 I-base / M-ext insn checks plus reg / pc_fwd / pc_bwd / causal /\nunique / cover / ill / liveness — 53 total against the V0 baseline.\n\nIf genchecks.py crashes mid-run and only emits one .sby task that\nvacuously passes, the old `passed > 0 and failed == 0` rule would\nreturn success. EXPECTED_MIN_CHECKS prevents that.\n\"\"\"\nimport os, shutil, subprocess, json, re, uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport yaml\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import run_pgroup\n\n\ndef read_nret(core_yaml_path: Path) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Read the `nret` field from a core.yaml. Defaults to 2 when the file\n    or field is missing — preserves backward compat with cores authored\n    before the nret-aware fixture (every existing core today).\n\n    Only 1 and 2 are supported. NRET=1 selects the single-issue formal\n    wrapper (wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg); NRET=2 uses the dual-channel\n    default (wrapper.sv + checks.cfg).\n    \"\"\"\n    p = Path(core_yaml_path)\n    if not p.exists():\n        return 2\n    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\n    n = y.get(\"nret\", 2)\n    if n not in (1, 2):\n        raise ValueError(f\"core.yaml nret must be 1 or 2, got {n!r}\")\n    return n\n\n# Floor on how many .sby tasks must pass for a \"formal: green\" result.\n# V0 baseline produces 53. Allow some slack (≥50) so a future checks.cfg\n# tweak that legitimately drops 1-2 checks doesn't trigger a false alarm,\n# but reject a partial genchecks run that emits 1-2 tasks.\nEXPECTED_MIN_CHECKS = int(os.environ.get(\"FORMAL_MIN_CHECKS\", \"50\"))\n\n\n# Patterns that prove SBY actually executed at least one check before the\n# post-run `*.sby` glob came up empty. Any one of these in the output\n# means `no_checks_generated` is the wrong label — checks DID generate,\n# they just got wiped or interrupted between SBY's output and the tally.\n_SBY_RAN_PATTERNS = (\n    re.compile(r'^SBY \\d+:\\d+\n…[8164 of 11236 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:31427cff1c764bb5]…\nheck': 'setup',\n            'detail': output[-4000:],\n        }\n    finally:\n        _cleanup_formal_workdir(worktree_path, env.get(\"CORE_NAME\"), work_id)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    import sys\n    result = run_formal(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else '.', sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else None)\n    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n- Verilator: Built from 0.786 MB sources in 16 modules, into 0.620 MB in 7 C++ files needing 0.001 MB\n- Verilator: Walltime 4.577 s (elab=0.008, cvt=0.050, bld=4.505); cpu 0.070 s on 1 threads; allocated 27.242 MB\nBuilt: cores/bench/obj_dir/cosim_sim\nGenerate file \"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261005-002-r14s1-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr.html\" completed\nGenerate file \"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261005-002-r14s1-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\" completed\nMon Oct  5 00:56:24 2026\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r14s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['hypothesis']+= '''\\\\n\\\\nCapture an explicit validated is_low_mul bit in ID/EX alongside the existing execution classes, using dec_is_illegal and dec_alu_op==ALU_MUL on the same payload capture/hold edges. Route this registered bit to low-lane ownership and the late-producer interlock; do not decode the five-bit live ALU opcode in those EX control paths. For anticipated normal EX/MEM write eligibility, outside ALTOPS exclude the existing registered is_multiply OR is_divide classes directly, which includes low MUL and every service-owned operation. Saved service completion retains its existing separate producer term. Under ALTOPS all M operations remain normal single-cycle writers. Preserve actual architectural write suppression and every alignment/trap check. This class separation is part of the dedicated low-MUL resource topology, not speculative forwarding eligibility.\\\\n\\\\nA temporary direct-product-lane precursor passes warning-free real lint and all eight selftest/random complete-RVFI cosim comparisons with/without both bus stalls. Canonical stalled CoreMark retains all five CRCs, validation literal and bounded accesses: markers 15,359 and 4,295,332 give 4,279,973 cycles, 5.46 percent below the champion. Instruction-stream profiling counts 93,960 low MULs and 35,640 immediate dependencies; these account for the available overlap opportunity. The precursor's option-0 timing is only 98.274 MHz, with its worst path in forwarded-target/write eligibility, so it does not itself improve fitness. The final registered-class refinement above must recover timing; it is not justified to claim the cycle savings alone meet acceptance. At these measured cycles the required scored median is above 106.704 MHz. Implementation must reproduce both cycles and median timing and pass all fixed gates.\\\\n'''\nd['changes'].insert(1,{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture explicit validated low-MUL execution class beside existing M classes using the original payload enable, reset and hold semantics; avoid live opcode decoding in EX ownership/hazard paths and preserve decoder legality.'})\nd['changes'][2]['description']+=' Use the captured low-MUL bit and direct registered M classes for anticipated normal-producer eligibility, retaining saved-completion priority and exact ALTOPS normal writers.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Hypothesis refinement is schema valid.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
