{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r15s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"MEM-local JALR link production removes early bypass alignment feedback\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's critical path runs from the registered arithmetic result\n  back into registered operand forwarding selections. A valid JALR makes\n  next_reg_write depend on its forwarded base plus immediate and target\n  alignment, coupling arithmetic data to the following consumer's bypass\n  control. The r11 alignment-sideband, r12 writer-predecode and r13\n  optimistic-alignment attempts all lost fitness. Recent fetch buffers and\n  pipelined MUL also traded cycle improvements for excessive frequency loss.\n  LESSONS.md is absent; the structural history and related JALR attempts\n  were reviewed. JALR's existing compulsory registered recovery provides\n  enough time to produce its link at MEM without exposing it as an early\n  producer or speculating about faults.\nhypothesis: |\n  Partition indirect-jump link production from ordinary early EX results.\n  Keep direct JAL's predicted path and early PC+4 bypass unchanged. For\n  validated JALR, disable the EX integer/link result grants, produce PC+4\n  locally in MEM, and register that complete link in the existing MEM/WB\n  wb_result. EX/MEM still carries the original JALR instruction, PC,\n  destination, full architectural operands, resolved next PC and exact\n  post-alignment write/trap controls. The independent effective-address\n  lane still captures the actual forwarded base plus immediate and supplies\n  aligned JALR recovery with bit zero cleared. No new instruction stage,\n  recovery cycle, fault replay, target predictor or memory queue is added.\n\n  Make upcoming EX/MEM bypass eligibility structurally exclude ALL JALR\n  instructions, whether aligned or faulting. Compute the ordinary early\n  term directly from resident valid ownership, validated decoded reg_write,\n  not-JALR, and direct-JAL alignment using the retained direct_aligned bit.\n  Do not obtain this early term from normal_result.ctrl.reg_write or live\n  misalign_jump, whic\n…[3552 of 6624 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d92c63a9d06bdddc]…\noperands, memory lanes, M ownership/completion and all other results.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Generate JALR PC+4 locally and select it into the existing MEM/WB\n      wb_result on the instruction's normal transfer. Preserve exact\n      post-trap write eligibility, load extraction, request outputs, RVFI\n      data and retained complete WB values through holds.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve every architectural assertion and fixed gate. Add full-RVFI\n      tests for correct-target consumers of the JALR link, rd=rs1,\n      loaded/M/ALU-produced jump bases, direct-JAL early link dependencies,\n      misaligned and reserved JALR followed by old-value consumers, older\n      writers to the same rd, x0, both bus stalls, prolonged older memory\n      holds and reset/recovery. Verify that JALR never advertises an early\n      producer, actual writes/traps stay exact, squashed consumers cannot\n      issue effects or M requests, and retirement order has no gaps.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
