{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r15s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Separate early bypass producer tokens from JALR retirement eligibility\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's worst path feeds its registered arithmetic result back\n  into forwarding selections. Upcoming producer eligibility depends on\n  forwarded JALR operands, target alignment and M dispatch, even though\n  an aligned JALR's immediate younger instruction will be squashed by\n  existing registered recovery. The r11 alignment sideband, r12 writer\n  predecode retaining live alignment, and r13 optimistic fault replay\n  all lost fitness. Fetch buffers and pipelined MUL also lost more Fmax\n  than they gained in cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; structural history\n  and these related attempts were reviewed. Splitting early bypass\n  capability from architectural retirement eligibility can eliminate\n  this feedback without adding a stage or speculation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Preserve the existing pipeline and datapaths, but give each incoming\n  instruction a registered early_writer capability token in ID/EX.\n  Unlike architectural reg_write, this token is ALWAYS false for JALR:\n  an indirect jump keeps its exact PC+4 result and architectural write,\n  but is visible to useful consumers only at the existing WB boundary.\n  Direct JAL retains its predicted path and early link forwarding.\n\n  Compute the token before ID/EX capture as validated dec_reg_write AND\n  NOT dec_is_jalr AND (NOT dec_is_jump OR in.direct_aligned). In real\n  hardware additionally exclude the entire M class using raw OP opcode\n  0x33 and funct7 0x01; validated dec_reg_write remains authoritative.\n  In RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS exclude no M operations, since all eight retain\n  their exact single-cycle formulas and ordinary early forwarding.\n  No live forwarded value, ALU result, JALR sum, branch comparator,\n  aggregate trap flag or M request/completion participates in token\n  generation. Reset clears the token; capture and hold it with ID/EX\n  payload, including invalid captures. Consumer validity is qualified\n  separately,\n…[4029 of 7101 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:285cb05642d362c8]…\nnchanged.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form upcoming bypass eligibility from the registered normal token\n      and the original owned-M completion producer as disjoint terms.\n      Remove live JALR alignment and M dispatch from the normal term.\n      Preserve every actual write/trap, target, link result, recovery,\n      memory lane, architectural operand and service handshake.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Keep every architectural assertion and fixed gate. Independently\n      check token/class/validity correspondence and no JALR early writer.\n      Cover correct-target link consumers, rd=rs1, ALU/load/M jump bases,\n      direct-JAL early link consumers, misaligned/reserved JALR followed\n      by old-value consumers, competing older writers, x0, both bus\n      stalls, long older memory holds, M completion and reset/recovery.\n      Check full RVFI values, exact traps, request stability, suppression\n      of wrong-path effects and strictly consecutive retirement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
