{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Compact agree predictor reduces direction-table cost and alias conflict',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already predicts direct branches with 64 two-bit direction\ncounters. Prior wide target tables, LUT-RAM counters, return-stack\nvalidation and optimistic JALR alignment lost fitness. Three temporary\nlookahead-selector trials also lost vendor Fmax. A much smaller agree\npredictor instead uses the branch displacement sign as a static bias and\nlearns agreement with that bias. Oppositely biased branches sharing an\nentry can then reinforce one another rather than fight over direction.\nLESSONS.md is absent; all prior predictor hypotheses were reviewed.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the conditional direction table with a 16-entry agree\npredictor. Bias is the sign bit of the original B immediate, instr[31]:\nnegative displacements predict taken, nonnegative ones predict not taken.\nIndex both fetch and training by PC[7:4] XOR PC[12:9], which groups PCs at\n16-byte granularity and folds another four address bits. This is one\nuniform address hash, with no benchmark PC constants or special cases.\nUse two-bit entry-local saturating agreement counters initialized to 10,\nweakly agreeing. MSB=1 selects the bias; MSB=0 selects its complement.\nThe conditional taken decision is counter_msb XNOR fetched instr[31].\n\nTrain exactly once from the existing advancing valid aligned EX/MEM\nconditional branch. Use its actual branch_taken and its own retained\ninstr[31], never the current fetch's sign. Increment if actual outcome\nequals that bias and decrement otherwise, saturating at 00/11. Expose a\none-bit internal training-bias input on if_stage and wire the registered\nEX/MEM instruction sign from core. Preserve the existing training-valid\nqualification and update timing. A not-taken branch whose direct target\nis misaligned remains excluded, as in the champion. Reset installs 10 in\nevery entry. Keep entry-local constant-index writes and a two-by-eight\nMSB lookup, with one final two-way group selection. No counter-value\nread-modify-write mux, RAM macro, valid/tag array or additional stage.\n\nKeep actual predicted_taken metadata, not agreement, with the accepted\ninstruction. Existing ID mismatch_op XOR prediction, EX actual-outcome\nreconstruction, IF alternate recovery address and registered recovery\ntherefore work unchanged. Keep aligned direct JAL prediction and exact\nfull-width B/J target arithmetic; JALR retains its current behavior.\nPrediction remains independent of hazard/ready/flush feedback and live\ncounter updates remain visible through PC holds. Preserve every bus\nhold, forwarding and M ownership rule, illegal/default decoder checks,\nall target/memory traps, complete architectural RVFI and nret=1 ports.\n\nReference replay of canonical 2K CoreMark finds 529,588 conditional\nbranches between the markers. This 16-entry agree table has 49,631\nserial-replay direction misses, versus 41,558 for the champion's 64-entry\ntable and 73,442 for a 16-entry raw-direction table with the old hash.\nReplay uses actual architectural branch outcomes and includes warm-up\noutside the markers. It does not model delayed MEM training, speculation\nor changing stall alignment and is not a measured cycle count. The\nsmall expected direction-accuracy loss may be offset by eliminating\n96 counter flops and shrinking lookup/update fanout and decode. Predict\nsix percent fitness gain with low confidence; only unchanged correctness\ngates, actual stalled CoreMark CRCs/markers and median Gowin timing can\nestablish it. No selector-lookahead trial is part of this proposal.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the 64 raw-direction counters and hash with 16 reset-10 agreement\ncounters indexed by PC[7:4] XOR PC[12:9]. Read via two eight-entry groups\nand XNOR the selected MSB with the fetched branch displacement sign.\nAdd registered-source train_bias input and train from actual agreement.\nPreserve all direct target, metadata, acceptance and recovery behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire if_stage.train_bias from ex_mem_w.instr[31], belonging to the same\nregistered advancing branch as train_pc and train_taken. Retain the\nexisting train_valid gate and all other backend, hazard and RVFI wiring.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'''Extend the independent model for the new hash, table size, reset state,\nstatic displacement bias and agreement updates. Exercise forward and\nbackward branches sharing an index, both saturation directions, warm-up,\nphase reversal, same-index lookup/training with different biases, target\nalignment, full-width PC wrap, prolonged holds and reset. Retain legal\npredecode and architectural target/metadata assertions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Update only the independent predictor model and prediction-dependent\ninternal cycle expectations to the agree policy. Model training bias\nfrom the actual older instruction and actual outcome. Preserve every\narchitectural assertion; cover consecutive opposite-bias aliases,\nload-dependent branches, M ownership, both bus stalls, pending recovery,\nwrong-path memory/M suppression, once-only training and retirement order.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80,default_style=None))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
