{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_75", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Dedicated resolved-branch feedback removes the EX/MEM payload mux from predictor training',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already has effective direction prediction; prior wider\nnext-PC tables, RAM counters, return-stack validation and optimistic JALR\nalignment lost fitness. Local selector-lookahead and smaller agree-table\ntrials also lost vendor Fmax. Current training reads branch PC, outcome,\nvalidity and target alignment through the general EX/MEM normal-versus-M\nsnapshot machinery. Predictor feedback gives these otherwise RVFI-only\nfields a timed fanout. Dedicated resolved-branch feedback can remove that\nmux and unnecessary arithmetic from this dependency without changing\nbranch accuracy, prediction policy or frontend latency. LESSONS.md is\nabsent; all predictor log.jsonl entries were reviewed.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the current 64-entry two-bit direction predictor, hash, weakly\nnot-taken initialization, entry-local writes and grouped lookup exactly.\nChange only its resolved-branch feedback path: give legal aligned normal\nEX branches a dedicated training register boundary parallel to EX/MEM,\nrather than sourcing training from the general normal/M metadata bundle.\n\nDefine a branch acceptance event as \"'!reset && !stall && in.valid &&\n!recovery_valid_q && !divide_active_q && !is_divide &&\n!in.ctrl.is_illegal && in.ctrl.is_branch && in.direct_aligned.\nCapture training PC from that accepted instruction'\"'s in.pc and actual\noutcome from the existing branch_taken signal (the shared mismatch\npredicate XOR carried predicted_taken). Use the original instruction's\nvalidated direct_aligned bit; do not recompute a target adder for predictor\nqualification and do not train a branch with a misaligned direct target,\neven when not taken, preserving the champion's update policy. Hold the\ntraining PC/outcome payload on non-events. At every nonreset edge set the\ntraining-valid register to the acceptance event, clearing it on any\nnon-event, including an older data-memory hold or M ownership. On reset\nclear validity and initialize payload. Gate its external valid by \"'!reset.\n\nFeed this registered PC, actual outcome and valid directly to IF'\"'s existing\ntraining inputs on the following cycle. This is the SAME update cycle as\nthe champion's advancing EX/MEM branch, with no extra feedback latency.\nA valid resolved conditional branch owns a non-memory EX/MEM entry, so\nMEM cannot hold that branch: after deferred EX acceptance it advances at\nthe next edge. Pending recovery or a younger M operation must not suppress\nthis older registered training event. Consecutive branches may train on\nconsecutive cycles. Squashed younger instructions, bubbles, held branches\nand M snapshots must never generate an event; each accepted branch trains\nonce. Keep counter lookup's existing pre-edge semantics, with no bypass.\n\nRemove predictor consumers of ex_mem_w.pc, branch_taken, branch_target and\ngeneral valid/ctrl qualification from core. Retain all architectural/RVFI\nfields and the existing EX/MEM snapshot mux where still needed; allow the\nvendor flow to prune feedback-only snapshot and target logic naturally.\nDo not optimize or weaken RVFI, decoder, alignment or arithmetic checks.\nThe core's new internal training wires are separate from top-level IO.\n\nPreserve B/J predecode and full-width targets, prepared alternate recovery\noperands, carried predictions and complemented mismatch predicates,\nregistered correction using the existing execution lanes, all JALR/link\nand trap behavior, branch recovery priority, bus acceptance and stalls,\nstable memory requests, retained WB forwarding, M/ALTOPS arithmetic and\nownership, exact nret=1 port shape and consecutive retirement order.\nNo table-size change, extra fetch stage, return stack, cache or different\nprediction algorithm is included in this final proposal.\n\nExpect lower training control/data fanout and removal of the M-snapshot\nmux from predictor feedback, with identical predictions and 4,527,071\nmarker-bracketed CoreMark cycles if the event equivalence is correct.\nEstimate six percent fitness improvement with low confidence: ALU and\nforwarding paths may remain dominant, and new register enables or routing\ncan erase the benefit. Require exact independent cycle-by-cycle training\nand counter equivalence, unchanged formal and full-RVFI cosim gates,\ncanonical stalled 2K CoreMark CRCs, validation text, bounded accesses and\nmarker-only timing. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires fitness\nabove 249.30364 iter/sec and median Gowin Fmax above 112.861528 MHz.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Add dedicated registered valid/PC/actual-outcome branch-training outputs.\nCapture only accepted valid legal aligned normal branches, outside M\nownership and pending recovery. Clear event-valid on every non-event;\nhold event payload when invalid. Derive outcome from the existing shared\nbranch comparator and alignment from retained direct_aligned. Preserve\nall current execution, EX/MEM, recovery and snapshot behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect EX's dedicated training registers directly to IF. Remove the\nEX/MEM metadata-based train_valid expression and PC/outcome feedback;\npreserve all other top-level, hazard, forwarding and RVFI connections.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'''Retain the independent 64-entry counter model and all pre-edge lookup,\nhash, saturation, target alignment and reset assertions. Confirm the\nunchanged IF training interface and prediction policy are preserved.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every architectural assertion and the independent predictor/\nrecovery model. Compare the new event each cycle with the former advancing\nEX/MEM legal aligned conditional-branch predicate, including exact PC and\noutcome. Cover consecutive branches, held load-dependent branches,\ntraining during pending recovery or younger M ownership, wrong-path\nbranch/M/store suppression, both bus stalls and reset. Require identical\ncounter updates, predictions, recovery cycles and retirement ordering.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Dedicated-feedback hypothesis schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
