r\nplace_option 2: Fmax 96.17 MHz, 10 logic levels; logic 4491, registers 1938, LUT-RAM 0, BSRAM 4, DSP 2\n  path 1: 15.693 ns, 12 cells, cpu/u_if/pc_2_s1 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.imm_16_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_id\n  path 2: 15.692 ns, 6 cells, lfsr_17_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_23_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_rf\n  path 3: 15.687 ns, 6 cells, lfsr_22_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_23_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_rf\n  path 4: 15.686 ns, 7 cells, lfsr_17_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_27_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_rf\n  path 5: 15.651 ns, 6 cells, lfsr_17_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_17_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_rf\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 96.17 MHz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_85", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Entry-local registered training pulses isolate direction-predictor feedback'\nd['hypothesis']='''Keep the current 64-entry two-bit direction predictor, hash, weakly\nnot-taken initialization, entry-local counters and grouped fetch lookup.\nChange only resolved-branch feedback: register a one-hot entry selection\nand actual outcome directly from accepted normal EX branches, outside\nthe general EX/MEM normal-versus-M metadata mux. Each counter receives\nits own registered update pulse on the following cycle, with no training\nPC read mux, post-register address hash or shared enable decoder.\n\nDefine branch acceptance as \"'!reset && !stall && in.valid &&\n!recovery_valid_q && !divide_active_q && !is_divide &&\n!in.ctrl.is_illegal && in.ctrl.is_branch && in.direct_aligned.\nFor every constant entry e, capture train_entry_en[e] <= acceptance &&\n((in.pc[7:2] XOR in.pc[13:8]) == e). Reset all 64 pulses to zero.\nOverwrite every pulse at every edge: a non-event, including an older\nmemory hold, M ownership or pending recovery, clears all pulses rather\nthan retaining them. Capture actual branch_taken from the existing shared\nmismatch predicate XOR carried prediction when acceptance is true; hold\nthis one-bit payload otherwise. Reset initializes it. Pulse and outcome\nmust describe the same accepted instruction. Decode uses the full original\nhash and no workload-specific PC constants. Alignment comes from the\nretained validated direct_aligned bit, avoiding predictor-only target\narithmetic and preserving exclusion of even not-taken misaligned targets.\n\nSupply the 64 registered entry pulses and registered actual outcome to\nIF. Each local counter updates only on its own pulse, with the existing\nsaturating 00/01/10/11 transition function. Pulse bits must be one-hot or\nall-zero; implement constant-index storage/update logic rather than a\nvariable-index write array. Keep counter lookup'\"'s existing pre-edge\nsemantics, with no update bypass. These pulses replace the timed use of\nEX/MEM PC, outcome, branch_target, validity and general control tags for\ntraining. Architectural and RVFI fields stay intact; allow synthesis to\nprune their former feedback-only M snapshot/target logic naturally.\nA static standalone compatibility parameter for the original PC-indexed\nIF training interface is acceptable for existing unit tests, but core\nmust elaborate exclusively to the registered-pulse path; no runtime mux.\n\nThis preserves the SAME training edge as the champion: a normal branch\ncaptured into EX/MEM is non-memory, so MEM cannot hold it at the next\nedge. A branch held by an older memory request emits no pulse until it\ncan advance. Once captured, older training proceeds even during pending\nrecovery or younger M ownership. Consecutive accepted branches can emit\nconsecutive pulses, including repeated updates to the same entry.\nSquashed younger branches and M snapshots never emit a pulse. Reset\ncancels pending updates. No additional feedback or frontend cycle is\nintroduced, and counter behavior must match the champion exactly.\n\nPreserve B/J predecode and full-width targets, prepared alternate recovery\noperands, carried predictions and mismatch predicates, existing registered\ncorrection lanes, all JALR/link and trap behavior, PC recovery priority,\nbus handshakes and stable requests, retained forwarding, real/ALTOPS M\narithmetic and ownership, decoder default-illegal checks, exact nret=1 IO\nand consecutive retirement order. No table-size, history, fetch-stage,\nreturn-stack, cache or prediction-algorithm change is included.\n\nThe dedicated binary-address feedback precursor passed warning-free lint,\nthe existing independent predictor and pipeline suites, all eight full-\nRVFI selftest/random cosim comparisons with and without both stalls, and\ncanonical stalled CoreMark with every CRC, validation text and bounded\naccesses. It retained exactly 4,527,071 marker-bracketed cycles. Gowin\noptions 0/1/2 reached 98.964/106.857/106.857 MHz; this precursor did NOT\nclear the acceptance threshold. The FINAL one-hot pulse refinement is\ndistinct: it moves entry decoding before the register boundary and makes\nevery counter update enable local. Its extra pulse flops and acceptance\nfanout may outweigh the shorter feedback path, and existing ALU/forwarding\npaths may remain dominant. Estimate six percent gain with low confidence,\nnot a measured accepted improvement. Require unchanged formal/cosim gates,\nindependent pulse/counter/event equivalence, actual canonical stalled\nCoreMark and all scored Gowin options. At unchanged cycles, acceptance\nrequires fitness above 249.30364 iter/sec and median Fmax above\n112.861528 MHz. No failed lookahead or agree-table variant is included.\n'''\nd['changes']=[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Create entry-local registered one-hot training pulses from the accepted\nnormal legal aligned branch's original PC hash. Clear all pulses on\nreset or every non-event; capture actual shared-comparator outcome on\nacceptance. Keep pulse/outcome identity, defer through older holds and\nexclude M ownership and pending-recovery consumers. Preserve all existing\nexecution, EX/MEM, recovery, trap and snapshot behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Consume registered per-entry update pulses and outcome directly in the\n64 local two-bit counters, retaining exact reset state, saturation and\nfetch lookup. Remove post-register training-address decoding from the\ncore's elaborated path. A static legacy-interface parameter may retain\nstandalone tests without introducing runtime selection or changing the\nproduction update edge. Preserve fetch prediction and all metadata.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect EX's registered training pulses/outcome to IF. Remove timed\nEX/MEM metadata-based predictor training and elaborate the local-pulse\nupdate path. Keep any comparison-only debug wires untimed; preserve all\nother top-level, hazard, forwarding and RVFI wiring.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_predictor.py','description':'''Retain the independent counter model and every lookup, hash, saturation,\npredecode, target and reset assertion. Exercise the new pulse interface\nwith zero/one-hot updates, same-entry consecutive events, simultaneous\nlookup/update and reset cancelation; compare both static interfaces if a\nlegacy standalone mode is retained. Verify exact 64-entry behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve every architectural assertion and independent predictor/recovery\nmodel. Compare each registered pulse and outcome against the former\nadvancing EX/MEM legal aligned branch predicate and original PC hash.\nRequire one-hot-or-zero pulses and identical counter/prediction/recovery\nsequences. Cover consecutive and same-entry branches, prolonged older\nholds, training during recovery/younger M, reset cancelation and wrong-\npath branch/M/store suppression under both bus stalls.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final pulse hypothesis schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
