{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-003-r10s2','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-003-r8s2']:\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes','')[-4000:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-003-r8s2 Direction predictor reuses registered EX lanes for recovery\nAdd one 64-entry direction-only predictor with registered recovery\nand registered training, using the existing EX/MEM execution lanes\nfor the recovery address. Use untagged two-bit saturating counters\nindexed by PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8], reset weakly not taken. Implement\nentry-local constant-index updates and an eight-by-eight grouped MSB\nlookup; simultaneous lookup and training observe pre-edge state.\nPredecode only legal BRANCH funct3 values and JAL from raw imem_data.\nPredict aligned JAL taken, conditional direction from the table, and\nJALR sequentially. Form exact full-width B/J targets in parallel with\nPC+4 and suppress taken prediction for misaligned direct targets.\nNo BTB, tags, return stack, cache, global history or extra instruction\nstage. Prediction is independent of hazard, flush and ready feedback.\n\nCarry predicted_taken and direct alignment with IF/ID and ID/EX.\nPrepare the direct recovery address in IF: PC+4 for a taken prediction,\ndirect target otherwise. Reuse ID/EX imm for this address ONLY on\nvalidated B/J instructions. Preserve original immediates for arithmetic,\nAUIPC, memory and JALR. Reconstruct original B/J immediates from the\nretained instruction bits in EX for architectural targets and RVFI.\nRegister branch_op XOR {2'b00,predicted_taken} as the mismatch predicate.\nOne forwarded-operand comparator gives direction mismatch; reconstruct\nactual outcome as mismatch XOR predicted_taken. Preserve original\nbranch_op, architectural operand snapshots and all trap semantics.\n\nFor a validated conditional branch, select the existing ALU_LUI operation\nand immediate B operand internally at ID/EX capture. Export the same\nbranch immediate selection to the registered complete ALU choices.\nThis passes its prepared recovery address through the EXISTING integer\nALU and arithmetic_result_q register. A branch has no architectural rd\nwrite, so this payload is available for predictor recovery without any\narchitectural result change. Dec\n…[13069 of 16141 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a0f9e012d4b53d01]…\n control-flow entry on advancement. Preserve\noriginal prediction metadata on all holds, old-state table reads, reset\npriority, redirect priority over unavailable fetch, raw decode payload,\nload-use bubbling, stable outstanding requests, retained WB forwarding,\nall real and ALTOPS arithmetic, traps, nret=1 IO and consecutive RVFI\norder. Architectural RVFI next PCs never come from speculation.\n\nThis is one predictor replacement, not a pipeline-depth, queue, cache\nor arithmetic-algorithm change. Expect an eight-percent fitness gain\nif eliminating fetch target arithmetic outweighs target/tag routing\nand extra cold/conflict misses. Confidence is low until vendor timing\nand cycle counts are measured. The old BTB's clock loss is a specific\nrisk; entry-local flop storage and registered recovery are essential.\nRequire canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs, validation text, bounded\naccesses, exact marker timing, all unchanged formal/cosim gates, and\nscored fitness above 249.30364 iterations/sec, the 4.6 percent threshold.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
