{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r15s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Parallel segmented direct targets for the fetch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 64-entry direction predictor and registered recovery already\n  reduce control-flow bubbles. Previous tagged target tables, RAM counters,\n  return-stack validation and entry-local training pulses lost vendor Fmax.\n  Its fetch path still chooses between B/J immediates before a full-width\n  target addition, then selects the predicted and alternate paths. Prior\n  timing reports identify IF PC update and IF-to-ID recovery-immediate paths\n  as critical. Shortening exact direct-target generation offers a focused\n  predictor improvement without extra misses or speculative target state.\n  LESSONS.md is absent; the predictor entries in log.jsonl were reviewed.\nhypothesis: |\n  Change only fetch-time direct-target generation. Compute exact branch and\n  JAL target candidates concurrently from the raw instruction and current\n  full-width PC, and select the completed candidates with the existing JAL\n  predecode. Remove opcode selection from before the target carry chain.\n  Preserve the existing sequential PC increment and direction lookup.\n\n  Exploit sign extension with segmented addition rather than computing two\n  full-width ripple additions. For BRANCH, form the original B immediate's\n  low 12 bits and add them to PC[11:0] using an explicitly widened 13-bit\n  unsigned sum. Independently form PC[31:12]+1 and PC[31:12]-1 modulo 20 bits.\n  Select the target high 20 bits as the unchanged PC high bits when the low\n  carry equals instruction bit 31, the incremented value for carry=1/sign=0,\n  and the decremented value for carry=0/sign=1. Combine this selected high\n  portion with the low sum. For JAL apply the identical construction at\n  bit 20: a 21-bit unsigned low sum and independent 12-bit high increment\n  and decrement. These equations reproduce PC plus the fully sign-extended\n  original immediate modulo 2^32, including negative offsets, page crossings\n  and wraparound; do not truncat\n…[1984 of 5056 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4deed133b8abe089]…\n JAL predecode,\n      derive alignment from low bits, and preserve every predictor, training,\n      sequential-PC, recovery-operand and acceptance behavior.\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve the independent saturating-counter and full-width target model.\n      Extend target checks across every encoded B/J immediate and representative\n      PCs exercising low-sum carries, both signs, 4K/1M boundaries, upper-half\n      addresses and 32-bit wraparound. Cover simultaneous lookup/training,\n      misaligned targets, stalls, recovery priority and reset.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all architectural assertions and add accepted-fetch and recovery\n      cases crossing the segmented target boundaries in both directions.\n      Compare resolved RVFI PCs and jump links against the independent ISS;\n      exercise conditional hits/misses, JAL, misalignment traps, older memory\n      holds, unavailable fetch, wrong-path side effects and ordered retirement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
